    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Australia 1996) Forest is defined as areas dominated by trees having usually a single stem and a mature or potentially mature stand height exceeding 5 metres, and with existing or potential projective cover of overstorey strata about equal to or greater than 30 per cent; while woodland is similarly defined but with a projective cover of overstorey strata of less than 30 per cent. http://www.oecd.org/officialdocuments/publicdisplaydocumentpdf/?cote=OCDE/GD(96)5&docLanguage=En"@en .

