    skos:note "(Australia 1998) Forest - A land area, incorporating all living and non-living components, dominated by trees usually having a single stem and a mature or potentially mature stand height exceeding 2 metres, and with existing or potential crown cover of overstorey strata about equal to or greater than 20%. This definition includes native forests and plantations and areas of trees that are sometimes described as woodlands. http://adl.brs.gov.au/data/warehouse/pe_brs90000003841/sofr2008Full_11a.pdf"@en .

