ex:Def_def_aus_1998_419 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Australia-Queensland) There are many definitions of what constitutes a forest o..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Australia ;
    ex:country "Australia" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Australia-Queensland) There are many definitions of what constitutes a forest or woody vegetation. A common definition used by foresters is 20 per cent crown cover which equates to approximately 12 per cent foliage projective cover (FPC) (NFI, 1998) http://www.nrm.qld.gov.au/slats/final9799.html"@en .

