    skos:note "(Estonia 1999) Forest land [metsamaa] - Land that is assigned for growing ligneous plants (by land survey or by land cadastre). Other lands that have importance for forestry can also be assigned into forest land if these are not suitable for other category. Current Estonian Forestry Act (valid until 01/01/99) From: \"Sulev Svilponis\" Sulev@ekm.envir.ee. Definitions are unofficial translations."@en .

ex:Def_def_est_2002_1010 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Estonia 2002) By legal definition, \"forest\" means a site of woody vegetation wi..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Estonia ;
    ex:country "Estonia" ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_est_2002_1010_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Estonia 2002) By legal definition, \"forest\" means a site of woody vegetation with an area of at least 0,5 ha, and at least one of the following requirements: Trees with the height of at least 1,3 m and with the canopy coverage of at least 30 %. If the site is managed for obtaining timber or other forest products. http://www-sydsvenskskogsvetenskap.slu.se/Grundutbildning/Masterk/2002/Estonia/forest.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_est_2002_1010_criteria ex:minArea "5.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "5.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCover "30.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCoverSI "30.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "3.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "3.0"^^xsd:float .

