ex:Def_def_fin_2009_1014 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Finland 2009) The second definition is the national definition of forest that i..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Finland ;
    ex:country "Finland" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_fin_2009_1014_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Finland 2009) The second definition is the national definition of forest that in Finland is the same as in the two other Nordic countries, Sweden and Norway: forest is defined as a land capable of producing an annual increment of volume growing stock of at least 1 m3/ha per year over the rotation under the most favorable tree species composition, and not used for any other purpose than forestry or forestry related purposes. METLA (Finnish Forest Research Institute),"@en .

ex:Def_def_fin_2009_1014_criteria ex:minHeight "1.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "1.0"^^xsd:float .

