ex:Def_def_fra_2011_1015 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(France 2011) Forest: Wooden area of 50 acres with trees able to reach a height ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_France ;
    ex:country "France" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_fra_2011_1015_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(France 2011) Forest: Wooden area of 50 acres with trees able to reach a height greater than five meters at maturity in situ, a of more than 10% and a width of at least 20 meters. Areas temporarily cleared or regenerating forests are classified as though they covered less than 10% during the inventory. Note: poplar (rate of free covered poplar grown on more than 75%) are included in the definition of forest. In contrast, walnut groves and chestnut groves as well as truffle cultivation and orchards are excluded (agricultural production). http://www6.nancy.inra.fr/lef_eng/LEF-Data-Group/Tools/Glossary/ FN definition , new inventory method . 2009. http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf"@en .

