    skos:note "(Georgia 2010) A forest is defined as land with tree crown cover of more than 10%, an area of more than 0.5 ha and an average width of more than 20 m. Trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 5 m at maturity in situ. FAO, 2010. http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf"@en .

