ex:Def_def_ger_2001_1017 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Germany 2001) Forest within the meaning of the FFI (Federal Forest Inventory) i..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Germany ;
    ex:country "Germany" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_ger_2001_1017_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Germany 2001) Forest within the meaning of the FFI (Federal Forest Inventory) is any area of ground covered by forest vegetation, irrespective of the information in the cadastal survey or similar records. The term forest also refers to cutover or thinned areas, forest tracks, firebreaks, openings and clearings, forest glades, feeding grounds for game, landings, rides located in the forest, further areas linked to and serving the forest including areas with recreation facilities, overgrown heaths and moreland, overgrown former pastures, alpine pastures and rough pastures, as well as areas of dwarf pines and green alders. Heaths, moorland, pastures, alpine pastures and rough pastures are considered to be overgrown if the natural forest cover has reached an average age of five years and if at least 50% of the area is covered by forest. Areas with forest cover in open pasture land or in built-up areas of under 1000 m2, coppices under 10 m wide and the cultivation of Christmas trees and ornamental brushwood as well as parkland attached to country houses are not forest within the meaning of the FFI. Watercourses up to 5 m wide do not break the continuity of a forest area. (Source: Anon. 2003. Survey instructions for Federal Forest Inventory II (2001-2002). 2nd corrected and revised reprint. May 2001. Bundesministerium für Verbaraucherschutz Ernährung und Landwirtschaft, Bonn, Germany)"@en .

ex:Def_def_ger_2001_1017_criteria ex:minCanopyCover "50.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCoverSI "50.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "1000.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "1000.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minWidth "10.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minWidthSI "10.0"^^xsd:float .

