    skos:note "(Hungary) -By law forest means area covered by woody vegetation with area bigger than 0,15 ha. Other wooded lands not included can be only row of trees, alleys, etc. having no adequate system (ortho-photos, software, etc.) its quantity can be only wrong estimated. http://www.fao.org/forestry/foris/webview/forestry2/index.jsp?siteId=5081&sitetreeId=18927&langId=1&geoId=0"@en .

ex:Def_def_hun_unknown_925_criteria ex:minArea "15.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "15.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_ind_1879_108 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(India 1879). \" Reserved Forest\" means waste land which has been declared as* re..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_India ;
    ex:country "India" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_ind_1879_108_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(India 1879). \" Reserved Forest\" means waste land which has been declared as* reserved forest at settlement or by any subsequent order of competent authority. * \"'Village Forest\" means such waste land as has been set apart under section 8 or section 9. http://books.google.com/books?pg=RA6-PA56&lpg=RA6-PA56&dq=%22forest%20means%22&sig=0C-6Qq9owihmR0j54aj8YA7qI30&ei=aQhXS92fHJCXtgfdlpW0BA&ct=result&id=RiETAAAAYAAJ&ots=6GPnEMMlVl&output=text ."@en .

ex:Def_def_ind_1879_108_criteria ex:minHeight "20.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "20.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_ind_1927_109 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(India 1927) “forest land” means a piece of land notified by the Government as t..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_India ;
    ex:country "India" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(India 1927) “forest land” means a piece of land notified by the Government as the forest land to develop, protect and conserve forest and includes a rangeland and wasteland;"@en .

ex:Def_def_ind_1927_110 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(India 1927) Forest is defined as a tract of land that is legally proclaimed to ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_India ;
    ex:country "India" ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(India 1927) Forest is defined as a tract of land that is legally proclaimed to be a forest under the forest laws (mainly 1865 and 1927) and is notified as forest in the government gazette. http://www.itto.int/direct/topics/topics_pdf_download/topics_id=39100000&no=1&disp=inline"@en .

ex:Def_def_ind_1947_111 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(India 1947) \"forest\" means any land which the State Government may, by notifica..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_India ;
    ex:country "India" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(India 1947) \"forest\" means any land which the State Government may, by notification, declare to be forest for the purposes of this Act and shall be deemed to include any land which is entered as forest or jungle or jungle- Jhori or described by any synonymous term in any record-of-rights finally published under any law for the time being in force unless it is proved that such entry in respect of the land is incorrect ; BIHAR PRIVATE Forest ACT 1947 [Act No IX of 1948] http://www.ielrc.org/content/e4701.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_ind_1967_117 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Indonesia 1967) Forest under the BFL (Basic Forestry Law) is defined as any kin..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Indonesia ;
    ex:country "Indonesia" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Indonesia 1967) Forest under the BFL (Basic Forestry Law) is defined as any kind of land-cover area (with or without tress), which is stated by the government as forest. It may be in the form of forest area or area without trees which the government as forest has designated. http://www.jica.go.jp/project/indonesia/0065045I0/activities/pdf/output1_2_1_fulltext.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_ind_1967_1455 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Indonesia 1967) Forest under the BFL (Basic Forestry Law) is defined as any kin..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Indonesia ;
    ex:country "Indonesia" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Indonesia 1967) Forest under the BFL (Basic Forestry Law) is defined as any kind of land-cover area (with or without tress), which is stated by the government as forest. It may be in the form of forest area or area without trees which the government as forest has designated. http://www.jica.go.jp/project/indonesia/0065045I0/activities/pdf/output1_2_1_fulltext.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_ind_1967_860 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Indonesia 1967) Forest under the BFL (Basic Forestry Law) is defined as any kin..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Indonesia ;
    ex:country "Indonesia" ;
