    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Indonesia 1967) Forest under the BFL (Basic Forestry Law) is defined as any kind of land-cover area (with or without tress), which is stated by the government as forest. It may be in the form of forest area or area without trees which the government as forest has designated. http://www.jica.go.jp/project/indonesia/0065045I0/activities/pdf/output1_2_1_fulltext.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_ind_1978_411 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(INDIA-Kerala 1978)-“Forest” means any reserved forest within the meaning of the..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_India ;
    ex:country "India" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(INDIA-Kerala 1978)-“Forest” means any reserved forest within the meaning of the Kerala Forest Act. 1961 (4 of 1962) and includes any forest vested in the Government under section 3 of the Kerala Private Forests (Vesting and assignment) Act. 1971 (26 of 1971). www.ielrc.org/content/e7805.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_ind_1980_112 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(India 1980) Any land recorded as forest in any of the land records is legally a..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_India ;
    ex:country "India" ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Forest_Conservation_Act_1980_From_Vivek_K ;
    skos:note "(India 1980) Any land recorded as forest in any of the land records is legally a forest land. This legal connotation provides a working definition of forest land to the forest managers in India for all the practical purposes. This definition disregards whether there is any vegetation on that land or not. [Source: Forest Conservation Act, 1980, From: \"Vivek K. Varma\" v.varma@landfood.unimelb.edu.au Date: Fri, 17 Jul 1998 02:28:29 -0400 (EDT)]."@en .

ex:Def_def_ind_1980_113 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(India 1980) ) The term “Forest land’ mentioned in Section 2 of the Act refers t..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_India ;
    ex:country "India" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(India 1980) ) The term “Forest land’ mentioned in Section 2 of the Act refers to reserved forest, protected forest or any area recorded as forest in the Government records. Lands which are notified under Section 4 of the Indian Forest Act would also come within the purview of the Act. (Supreme Court’s Judgment in NTPC’s case). It would also include “Forest” as understood in the dictionary sense. (Supreme Court order dated: 12.12.1996 in WP No. 202/1995 – Annexure-I)… The term “forest” shall not be applicable to the plantations raised on private lands, except notified private forests. http://forestsclearance.nic.in/writereaddata/FormA/UserAgencydoc/711712712128TYIMCompendium_on_FCA.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_ind_1998_1022 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Indonesia 1998) the legal definition of forest in Indonesia is: \"a spread out a..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Indonesia ;
    ex:country "Indonesia" ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Indonesia 1998) the legal definition of forest in Indonesia is: \"a spread out area filled with or planned to be filled with trees, other living (biological) and non-living elements which as a whole form an ecosystem unit\" (Law on Forestry 1998, Tr. Nico Smith 1999). http://europe.mtnforum.org/rs/econfreports/MountainPeopleForestsAndTrees.pdf"@en .

