ex:Def_def_ind_2002_1161 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(INDONESIA-Papua-2002) Forest means a unit of ecosystem in the form of lands com..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Indonesia ;
    ex:country "Indonesia" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(INDONESIA-Papua-2002) Forest means a unit of ecosystem in the form of lands comprising biological resources, dominated by trees in their natural forms and environment, which can not be separated each other. http://74.125.93.132/search?q=cache:bwzUkrDvEFsJ:www.papuaweb.org/dlib/lap/sullivan/perdasi-perdasus/forestry.rtf+%22forest+means%22&cd=215&hl=en&ct=clnk&gl=us&client=safari"@en .

ex:Def_def_ind_2002_1248 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Indonesia - 2002) The permanent removal of forest cover and conversion of the l..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Indonesia ;
    ex:country "Indonesia" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UN-FAO ;
    skos:note "(Indonesia - 2002) The permanent removal of forest cover and conversion of the land to other uses. According to the land use definition used by FAO and accepted by most governments, forest land that has been harvested, even clear-cut, is not regarded as deforested because, in principle, trees may regrow or be replanted. Deforestation is recorded only when the land is permanently converted to nonforest use. However, the remote sensing imagery used in this report to determine land cover (the presence or absence of forest) over time does not make such a distinction and clear-cut land has been recorded as nonforest or deforested land. http://www.globalforestwatch.org/common/indonesia/sof.indonesia.english.low.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_ind_2002_1404 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Indonesia - 2002) The permanent removal of forest cover and conversion of the l..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Indonesia ;
    ex:country "Indonesia" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UN-FAO ;
    skos:note "(Indonesia - 2002) The permanent removal of forest cover and conversion of the land to other uses. According to the land use definition used by FAO and accepted by most governments, forest land that has been harvested, even clear-cut, is not regarded as deforested because, in principle, trees may regrow or be replanted. Deforestation is recorded only when the land is permanently converted to nonforest use. However, the remote sensing imagery used in this report to determine land cover (the presence or absence of forest) over time does not make such a distinction and clear-cut land has been recorded as nonforest or deforested land. http://www.globalforestwatch.org/common/indonesia/sof.indonesia.english.low.pdf"@en .

