    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Indonesia 2002) Land on which trees form the dominant vegetation type. The Indonesian government uses a land use definition of forest in the various land use classes that comprise “Permanent Forest Status” (see below). However, up to 20 percent of Permanent Forest Status land has been deforested. http://www.globalforestwatch.org/common/indonesia/sof.indonesia.english.low.pdf and SaveForest. n.d..Definitions. http://www.freewebs.com/irwantoforester/definition2.html"@en .

