    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Indonesia 2009) Forest means a unity of ecosystem in the form of land consisting of biological resources dominated by trees in their natural form and environment, in which one and another are inseparable. https://www.elaw.org/system/files/REDD_PERMENHUT_P-30-2009_BILINGUAL.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_ind_2010_412 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(INDIA-Mizoram 2010) “Reserved Forest” means any area which is constituted as re..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_India ;
    ex:country "India" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(INDIA-Mizoram 2010) “Reserved Forest” means any area which is constituted as reserved forest under the Assam Forest Regulation, 1891 as adopted. http://www.forest.mizoram.gov.in/index.php?option=com_content&task=view&id=127"@en .

ex:Def_def_ind_2015_1394 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Indonesia 2015) In this submission, deforestation was defined as a conversion o..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Indonesia ;
    ex:country "Indonesia" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UN-FAO ;
    skos:note "(Indonesia 2015) In this submission, deforestation was defined as a conversion of natural forest cover into other land-cover categories that has only occurred one time in particular areas. The practical definition emphasises on land cover instead of land use. Consequently it is different from the definition of deforestation by FAO, which employed terminology of land use. http://redd.unfccc.int/files/national_frel_for_redd__in_indonesia_2015.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_ind_2015_231 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Indonesia 2015) In this document, the term “working definition” of forest was u..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Indonesia ;
    ex:country "Indonesia" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_ind_2015_231_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UNFCCC ;
    skos:note "(Indonesia 2015) In this document, the term “working definition” of forest was used to produce land-cover maps through visual interpretation of satellite images in a scale that minimum area for polygon delineation is 0.25 cm2 at 1: 50,000 of scale which equals to 6.25 ha. http://redd.unfccc.int/files/national_frel_for_redd__in_indonesia_2015.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_ind_2015_231_criteria ex:minArea "6.25"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "6.25"^^xsd:float .

