ex:Def_def_ind_unknown_552 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(India) - The term used in this report refers to the notional area covered by cr..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_India ;
    ex:country "India" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(India) - The term used in this report refers to the notional area covered by crown of trees that is too small to be delineated by digital interpretation of remote sensing data used for forest cover delineation. http://moef.gov.in/nfc/s-git.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_ind_unknown_612 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Definitions are grouped depending on if they are changes in land cover, land use..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Indonesia ;
    ex:country "Indonesia" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Definitions are grouped depending on if they are changes in land cover, land use, or both. Additional discussions of the meaning of \"deforestation\" may be found in Sunderlin, William D.; Resosudarmo, Ida Aju Pradnja. Rate and Causes of Deforestation in Indonesia: Towards a Resolution of the Ambiguities. http://www.cgiar.org/cifor/publications/occpaper/occpaper9.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_ind_unknown_628 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "The destruction of forest. This normally refers to deforestation of tropical rai..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Indonesia ;
    ex:country "Indonesia" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "The destruction of forest. This normally refers to deforestation of tropical rainforests in Indonesia, Brazil and in West Africa. http://www.kgv.edu.hk/eden/glossary.php"@en .

ex:Def_def_ind_unknown_638 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Deforestation refers to the loss of forest cover; land that is permanently conve..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Indonesia ;
    ex:country "Indonesia" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_ind_unknown_638_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UN-FAO ;
    skos:note "Deforestation refers to the loss of forest cover; land that is permanently converted from forest to agricultural land, golf courses, cattle pasture, homes, lakes, or desert. The FAO (Food and Agriculture Organization of the U.N.) defines tropical deforestation as \"change of forest with depletion of tree crown cover to less than 10%.\" Depletion of forest to tree crown cover greater than 10% (say from 100% to 12%) is considered forest degradation. Logging most often falls under the category of forest degradation and thus is not included in deforestation statistics. Therefore forest degradation rates are considerably higher than deforestation rates. For example, according to satellite surveys Indonesia has considerable forest coverage, but millions of hectares are highly degraded by logging and no longer contain their full diversity or original structure. http://www.mongabay.com/08define.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_ind_unknown_638_criteria ex:minCanopyCover "10.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCoverSI "10.0"^^xsd:float .

