    skos:note "(Kazakhstan 2002) \"forest\" means a natural complex formed on a certain territory based on the aggregate of trees and shrubs vegetations and other wildlife components interacting with environment and having environmental, economic and social importance; Forest Code of the Republic of Kazakhstan: faolex.fao.org/docs/texts/kaz41426E.doc"@en .

ex:Def_def_ken_1964_121 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Kenya 1964) Forest areas means an area of land declared under section 4 to be a..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Kenya ;
    ex:country "Kenya" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Kenya 1964) Forest areas means an area of land declared under section 4 to be a forest area. Section 4(1) empowers the Minister from time to time, by notice in the Gazettee:- Declare any unalienated Government land to be a forest area:- Declare the boundaries of a forest and from time to time after those boundaries; Declare that a forest area shall cease to be a forest area;http://freeafrica.tripod.com/ogiekland/book/Chapter06.htm#ActForest"@en .

ex:Def_def_ken_2005_1026 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Kenya 2005) Forests are often thought of as areas with continuous tree cover co..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Kenya ;
    ex:country "Kenya" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Kenya 2005) Forests are often thought of as areas with continuous tree cover consisting either of naturally occurring (indigenous) tree species or plantations. However, this definition ignores the importance of open savannah or dry land forests in which individual trees are scattered over wide areas of grassland. It also fails to cover small groups of trees planted on farms and other cultivated land. It is these dry land forests and farm trees that provide important livelihood strategies for many of Kenya’s poor people, including wood fuel, charcoal burning for income, and use of wood products for building. Forest Act 2005. http://www.donorplatform.org/load/5971"@en .

ex:Def_def_ken_2005_1174 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Kenya 2005) Tree means any timber producing plant, or shrubs, bush of any kind ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Kenya ;
    ex:country "Kenya" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Kenya 2005) Tree means any timber producing plant, or shrubs, bush of any kind and includes a seedling, sapling or reshoot of any age or any part thereof . http://formin.finland.fi/public/download.aspx?ID=15959&GUID=%7B88EFD0B8-9F47-4528-A24F-66DDE0CFE370%7D"@en .

ex:Def_def_ken_2005_1211 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Kenya 2005) Woodland means an open stand of trees less than ten metres tall whi..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Kenya ;
    ex:country "Kenya" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Kenya 2005) Woodland means an open stand of trees less than ten metres tall which has come about by natural regeneration. http://formin.finland.fi/public/download.aspx?ID=15959&GUID=%7B88EFD0B8-9F47-4528-A24F-66DDE0CFE370%7D"@en .

ex:Def_def_ken_2005_122 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Kenya 2005) Forest area means any land declared to be a forest land under this ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Kenya ;
    ex:country "Kenya" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Kenya 2005) Forest area means any land declared to be a forest land under this act. http://formin.finland.fi/public/download.aspx?ID=15959&GUID=%7B88EFD0B8-9F47-4528-A24F-66DDE0CFE370%7D and http://www.fankenya.org/downloads/ForestsAct2005.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_ken_2005_1291 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Kenya 2005) “forests” refers to any land containing a vegetation association do..." ;
