    skos:note "(Nepal 1999) Forest is defined as the land with a forest cover, i.e. with trees whose crown cover more than 10 percent of the area and not used primarily for the purpose other than forestry and shrub is same as forest but well defined stem can not be found (MFSC, 1999) http://eprints.usq.edu.au/568/1/Livelihood_Paper-Final.pdf"@en .

