ex:Def_def_per_2015_958 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Peru 2015 – Amazon) Currently being implemented, the National Forest Inventory ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Peru ;
    ex:country "Peru" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_per_2015_958_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UNFCCC ;
    skos:note "(Peru 2015 – Amazon) Currently being implemented, the National Forest Inventory applies specific forest definitions for the three biomes Costa, Sierra, and the Amazon. In case of the Amazon, the following parameters are used: • Minimum area: 0.50 hectares; • Minimum width: 20.00 m • Minimum tree height at maturity in situ: 5.00 m; • Minimum crown cover: 10%. http://redd.unfccc.int/files/2015_submission_frel_peru_en.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_per_2015_958_criteria ex:minArea "0.5"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "0.5"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCover "10.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCoverSI "10.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "20.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "20.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minWidth "20.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minWidthSI "20.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_per_2015_959 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Peru 2015 - CDM) The Peruvian Designated National Authority (DNA) of the Clean ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Peru ;
    ex:country "Peru" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_per_2015_959_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UNFCCC ;
    skos:note "(Peru 2015 - CDM) The Peruvian Designated National Authority (DNA) of the Clean Development Mechanism (CDM) reported to the UNFCCC the following definition of “forest”, which is used in the context of afforestation and reforestation project activities under the CDM. • Minimum area: 0.50 hectares; • Minimum tree height at maturity in situ: 5.00 m; • Minimum crown cover: 30%. http://redd.unfccc.int/files/2015_submission_frel_peru_en.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_per_2015_959_criteria ex:minArea "0.5"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "0.5"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCover "30.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCoverSI "30.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "5.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "5.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_per_unknown_361 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Peru) “Forest Land” means (i) that portion of SINANPE described in Exhibit A, w..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Peru ;
    ex:country "Peru" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Peru) “Forest Land” means (i) that portion of SINANPE described in Exhibit A, which will be conserved, maintained and restored with funds provided pursuant to the Forest Conservation Agreement, and (ii) any other forest land in Perú approved for conservation, maintenance and restoration by a majority vote of the Oversight Committee in accordance with the terms of the Forest Conservation Agreement. http://www.mef.gob.pe/DGCP/Documentacion/fondos/PERU_USA/convenio_dinat.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_phi_1975_136 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Philippines 1975) Forest lands include the public forest, the permanent forest ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Philippines ;
    ex:country "Philippines" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Philippines 1975) Forest lands include the public forest, the permanent forest or forest reserves, and forest reservations. a. Public forest is the mass of lands of the public domain which has not been the subject of the present system of classification for the determination of which lands are needed for forest purposes and which are not. b. Permanent forest or forest reserves refers to those lands of the public domain which have been the subject of the present system of classification and declared as not needed for forest purposes. Forestry Code, Revised (PD No. 705, 1975, as amended) http://bim.aseanbiodiversity.org/elib/reference/download.php?refNo=00541&fileId=541"@en .

ex:Def_def_phi_1975_137 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Philippines 1975) The term “forest land” refers to all property owned by the na..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Philippines ;
    ex:country "Philippines" ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Philippines 1975) The term “forest land” refers to all property owned by the national government that is still in the public domain. It is a legal, not a botanical description. http://www.cifor.org/publications/pdf_files/Books/Bchokkalingam0605-02.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_phi_1975_1459 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Philippines 1975) Forest lands include the public forest, the permanent forest ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Philippines ;
    ex:country "Philippines" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Philippines 1975) Forest lands include the public forest, the permanent forest or forest reserves, and forest reservations. a. Public forest is the mass of lands of the public domain which has not been the subject of the present system of classification for the determination of which lands are needed for forest purposes and which are not. b. Permanent forest or forest reserves refers to those lands of the public domain which have been the subject of the present system of classification and declared as not needed for forest purposes. Forestry Code, Revised (PD No. 705, 1975, as amended) http://bim.aseanbiodiversity.org/elib/reference/download.php?refNo=00541&fileId=541"@en .

ex:Def_def_phi_1996_138 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Philippines 1996) FOREST LAND – refers to the public forest, or permanent fores..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Philippines ;
    ex:country "Philippines" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Philippines 1996) FOREST LAND – refers to the public forest, or permanent forest inside the watershed reservations. http://www.napocor.gov.ph/WMD%20WEBPAGE/mandates/memorandum/mo%2096-27.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_phi_2000_1483 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Philippines 2000) – Refers to land with an area of more than 0.5 hectare and tr..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Philippines ;
    ex:country "Philippines" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_phi_2000_1483_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Philippines 2000) – Refers to land with an area of more than 0.5 hectare and tree crown cover (or equivalent stocking level) of more than 10 percent. The trees should be able to reach a minimum height of 5 meters at maturity in situ. It consists either of closed forest formations where trees of various storeys and undergrowth cover a high proportion of the ground or open forest formations with a continuous vegetation cover in which tree crown cover exceeds 10 percent. Young natural stands and all plantations established for forestry purposes, which have yet to reach a crown density of more than 10 percent or tree height of 5 meters are included under forest. These are normally forming part of the forest area, which are temporarily unstocked as a result of human intervention or natural causes but which are expected to revert to forest. It includes forest nurseries and seed orchards that constitute an integral part of the forest; forest roads, cleared tracts, firebreaks and other small open areas; forest within protected areas; windbreaks and shelter belts of trees with an area of more than 0.5 hectare and width of more than 20 meter; plantations primarily used for forestry purposes, including rubber wood plantations. It also includes bamboo, palm and fern formations (except coconut and oil palm). Reference: Food and Agriculture Organization, 2000 http://www.nscb.gov.ph/glossary/AGRI.ASP"@en .

ex:Def_def_phi_2000_1483_criteria ex:minArea "0.5"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "0.5"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCover "10.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCoverSI "10.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "5.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "5.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minWidth "20.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minWidthSI "20.0"^^xsd:float .

