    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_por_1994_963_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Portugal 1994) - According to minimum tree densities which vary from species to species (as low as 90/ha for cork oak, up to 840 for most conifers) with conifer heights from 1.5-5m hand broadleaf heights from 2-5m; or where the projected area of crowns of trees more than 5m height covers more than 15% of the ground areas. This rather complicated definition is necessary to define when grant payments are applicable and is necessary because Portugal has a long agroforestry tradition. (decree 199/94) From: Gerry Lawson <gjl@ite.ac.uk"@en .

ex:Def_def_por_1994_963_criteria ex:minCanopyCover "15.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCoverSI "15.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "5.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "5.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_por_1997_364 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Portugal 1997) Every portion of land with a greater than 2000 m2 and 15 m wide,..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Portugal ;
    ex:country "Portugal" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_por_1997_364_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Portugal 1997) Every portion of land with a greater than 2000 m2 and 15 m wide, is considered forest area. Forest area includes exploitable forests, recently harvested or burned areas, recent seedlings and plantations, and green zones (reserves, protection forests and recreation forests). (European Communities 1997b - p. 879)."@en .

ex:Def_def_por_1997_364_criteria ex:minHeight "2000.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "2000.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minWidth "15.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minWidthSI "15.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_rom_1996_1485 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Romania 1996) - The total forest vegetation mentioned in the Forest Management ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Romania ;
    ex:country "Romania" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_rom_1996_1485_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UN-FAO ;
    skos:note "(Romania 1996) - The total forest vegetation mentioned in the Forest Management Plans, both state-owned or private property, constitute the national forest area. Under the Forestry Code/1996 a forest area is defined as an area larger than 0.25 ha and covered with forest trees; the current forestry code refers to forest vegetation not included in the national forest area as forested pastures, forest windbreaks, forested low production areas, forests for watershed protection, community forest parks, dendrologic collections, forest tree alignments and the alpine vegetation with Pinus mugo. http://www.fao.org/docrep/w7170E/w7170e0f.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_rom_1996_1485_criteria ex:minArea "0.25"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "0.25"^^xsd:float .

