    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_European_Union ;
    skos:note "(Romania) Forest - National definition in use: designated areas, no sampling on other areas but for these areas some old data exist http://www.metla.fi/eu/cost/e43/minutes/wg1-min-florence.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_rom_unknown_1713 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Romania) According to the definition given in our “Forest Code”, forest is cons..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Romania ;
    ex:country "Romania" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_rom_unknown_1713_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Romania) According to the definition given in our “Forest Code”, forest is considered land covered by forest vegetation with an area of more than 0.25 ha. In order to approximate the TBFRA definition of the forest, the item “Forest” includes lands needed for culture (nurseries, orchards...), for production (game food...), for administration (forest roads, fire breaks...) and temporarily excluded from the “forest fund”. These are separately recorded in our statistics and in addition to forest area make “forest fund. http://www.unece.org/fileadmin/DAM/timber/fra/pdf/chp1_tot.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_rom_unknown_1713_criteria ex:minArea "0.25"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "0.25"^^xsd:float .

