ex:Def_def_swe_2009_1043 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Sweden 2009) Types of land under the Forestry Act Determined for the traditiona..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_Sweden ;
    ex:country "Sweden" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_swe_2009_1043_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Sweden 2009) Types of land under the Forestry Act Determined for the traditional types of land in productive forest, bog, mountain pine forests and other land. Forest land: Land bearing forest or without measures to increase production has the potential to bear forest with a height of 5 m and with a crown cover of at least 10%. Sveriges Lantbruksuniversitet (SLU), 2009. http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf (Sweden) Land that is suitable for timber production and that is not used for other purposes to any significant degree. Soil is deemed suitable if it can produce on average a total forest cubic metre of 1 m3 per ha and year for a 100 year growth period (min. site quality class VIII according to Jonson or H100 higher than approx. 10 m). The class ’forest land‘ includes extensively grazed permanent pasture and land within wildlife reserves that is not agricultural land. Also classified as forest land are abandoned farmland and other land suitable for forest production but not used for that purpose, unless forest is a clearly inappropriate land use (e.g. monument areas). Farmland that has not been used within the previous three years is considered abandoned and re-classified as forest land. However so-called transition land is classified as farmland until its land use is altered. Plant nurseries, seed plantations, ornamental plant cultivations, clear cases of Christmas tree plantations and energy forest plantations are classified as built-up land. http://www-markinfo.slu.se/eng/soildes/ago/agodef.html Swedish forest taxation system,"@en .

ex:Def_def_swe_2009_1043_criteria ex:minCanopyCover "10.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCoverSI "10.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "5.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "5.0"^^xsd:float .

