    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UN-FAO ;
    skos:note "(Turkey 1937) The first Forest Code defined forests as “areas covered by a collection of trees and shrubs grown either naturally or cultivated by humans, and producing woody materials or any kind of forest yield”. This definition excluded steppes, city parks, thorny areas, and areas of less than 5 ha that were not adjacent to natural forest boundaries and were owned by private entities. http://www.fao.org/forestry/16407-0c0665eddd86a68c9fbbe87cdde52501c.pdf."@en .

ex:Def_def_tur_1937_291_criteria ex:minArea "5.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "5.0"^^xsd:float .

