ex:Def_def_uni_2009_1051 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(United Kingdom 2009) The UK has chosen the following definition of forest and s..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_United_Kingdom ;
    ex:country "United Kingdom" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_uni_2009_1051_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(United Kingdom 2009) The UK has chosen the following definition of forest and single minimum values (also in table NIR.1). A definition of „forest‟ as agreed with the Forestry Commission comprising:  a minimum area of 0.1 hectares;  a minimum width of 20 metres;  tree crown cover of at least 20 per cent, or the potential to achieve it;  a minimum height of 2 metres, or the potential to achieve it. This definition includes felled areas awaiting restocking and integral open space (open areas up to 1 hectare) (Forestry Statistics 2009, section 11.1). http://uk-air.defra.gov.uk/reports/cat07/1010151419_ukghgi-90-08_main_chapters_Issue3_r.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_uni_2009_1051_criteria ex:minArea "0.1"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "0.1"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "20.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "20.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minWidth "20.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minWidthSI "20.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_uni_2009_1296 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(United Kingdom 2009) For the National Forest Inventory (2009-2014), the definit..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_United_Kingdom ;
    ex:country "United Kingdom" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_uni_2009_1296_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(United Kingdom 2009) For the National Forest Inventory (2009-2014), the definition of forest or woodland as an area of tree covered land greater than 0.5ha (about 1.25 acres) and at least 20 m wide whose “canopy cover” or “canopy closure” extends to 20% or more of the land area (or the potential to achieve this).In other words, if the site were viewed from the air, 20% or more of the ground would be obscured by the trees' foliage when the trees are mature. This definition of woodland is in keeping with other internationally accepted definitions of woodland. The current National Inventory is being carried out between 2009 and 2014. FC, 2010. http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_uni_2009_1296_criteria ex:minArea "0.5"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "0.5"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCover "20.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCoverSI "20.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "20.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "20.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minWidth "20.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minWidthSI "20.0"^^xsd:float .

