ex:Def_def_uni_2010_1050 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(United Kingdom 2010) The definition of woodland in United Kingdom forestry stat..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_United_Kingdom ;
    ex:country "United Kingdom" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_uni_2010_1050_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(United Kingdom 2010) The definition of woodland in United Kingdom forestry statistics and in National Inventory is land under stands of trees with a canopy cover of at least 20% (or having the potential to achieve this), including integral open space, and including felled areas that are awaiting restocking. There is no minimum size for a woodland. http://uk-air.defra.gov.uk/reports/cat07/1010151419_ukghgi-90-08_main_chapters_Issue3_r.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_uni_2010_1050_criteria ex:minCanopyCover "20.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCoverSI "20.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_uni_2010_1297 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(United Kingdom 2010) - For the National Inventory of Woodland, forest is define..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_United_Kingdom ;
    ex:country "United Kingdom" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_uni_2010_1297_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(United Kingdom 2010) - For the National Inventory of Woodland, forest is defined as areas with a canopy cover of 20% or more (or the potential to achieve this) and over 50 m in width. The NIWT woodland map aimed to include all areas satisfying this definition and with a minimum area of 2.0 ha or over. Woodland area from 0.1 ha to 2.0 ha was derived from the Survey of Small Woods and Trees http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_uni_2010_1297_criteria ex:minArea "2.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "2.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCover "20.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCoverSI "20.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "50.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "50.0"^^xsd:float .

