ex:Def_def_unk_1998_1284 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Aruba 1998) Forest: (thorny) woodlands, protected areas including mangrove area..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UN-FAO ;
    skos:note "(Aruba 1998) Forest: (thorny) woodlands, protected areas including mangrove areas, urban parks and trees for agricultural and commercial purposes are considered to fit the definition of forest as well. Even single trees are included in the definition if they form important esthetical elements in town or in the landscape. FAO Forestry paper 137/2, FORESTRY POLICIES IN THE CARIBEAN, volume 2: Reports of 28 selected countries and territories, FAO 1998. Facundo Franken, Department of Agriculture, Animal Production and Fisheries, Section Natural Resources Aruba."@en .

