ex:Def_def_unk_2008_148 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Taiwan 2008). state forest means a forest belonging to the nation and in the te..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Taiwan 2008). state forest means a forest belonging to the nation and in the territory of the nation, but without an owner. 2. A public forest means a forest held by a direct municipality, county (city), town, village or legal public entity. 3. A private forest means the ownership of a forest acquired by a private citizen or private legal entity. Chiayi Forest District Office. 2008. http://chiayi.forest.gov.tw/ct.asp?xItem=34177&CtNode=3036&mp=341"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_2009_1177 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(South Sudan 2009) “Tree” means forest trees including bushes, palms, bamboos, s..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(South Sudan 2009) “Tree” means forest trees including bushes, palms, bamboos, shrubs, brushwood, creepers and climbers at all stages of their growth; (GOSS, 2009)"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_2009_1289 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Cayman Islands 2009) Forest and woodland defined as a class of vegetation chara..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_2009_1289_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Cayman Islands 2009) Forest and woodland defined as a class of vegetation characterized by a closed tree canopy, with interlocking crowns generally providing 60-100% cover. “Woodland”, by comparison, is characterized by an open canopy, with tree crowns constituting just 25-60% cover. The canopy height of forest and woodland ranges from about 16m, down to about 4.5m in height, below which shrubland species dominate. Burton (2008b): http://www.seaturtle.org/mtrg/projects/cayman/Cayman_NBAP.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_2009_1289_criteria ex:minCanopyCover "60.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCoverSI "60.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "16.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "16.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_unk_2009_1339 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Natural forest be differentiated from plantations and that for defining “forest”..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_2009_1339_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Natural forest be differentiated from plantations and that for defining “forest” the lower height limit defining “trees” be set at more than 5 m tall with the minimum cover of trees be set at more than 40%. Sasak, Nophea; Putz, Francis E. 2009. Critical need for new definitions of “forest” and “forest degradation” in global climate change agreements. Conservation Letters xx (2009) 1–7. http://www.redd-monitor.org/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2009/09/2009-Putz-Conservation-Letters-on-REDD.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_2009_1339_criteria ex:minCanopyCover "40.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCoverSI "40.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "5.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "5.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_unk_2009_1350 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Sasaki, Nophea; Putz, Francis E. 2009. Critical need for new definitions of “for..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
