ex:Def_def_unk_2010_85 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(UN-CBD 2010) - Forest is a land area of more than 0.5 ha, with a tree canopy co..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_2010_85_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_United_Nations ;
    skos:note "(UN-CBD 2010) - Forest is a land area of more than 0.5 ha, with a tree canopy cover of more than 10%, which is not primarily under agriculture or other specific non-forest land use. In the case of young forest or regions where tree growth is climatically suppressed, the trees should be capable of reaching a height of 5m in situ, and of meeting the canopy cover requirement.’ Convention on Biological Diversity. http://www.google.com/url?sa=t&source=web&cd=51&ved=0CBgQFjAAODI&url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.iucnael.org%2Fen%2Fdocuments%2Fdoc_download%2F560-lesniewska-definition-of-forests-in-international-environmental-law.html&rct=j&q=forest%20definition&ei=AqRmTpnYOsbe0QHf17yJBw&usg=AFQjCNGm0ZOpKMree20-X8hkABhetZUfiw"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_2010_85_criteria ex:minArea "0.5"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "0.5"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCover "10.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCoverSI "10.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "5.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "5.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_unk_2010_879 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Bahamas 2010) Forest means any area consisting mainly of trees including forest..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Bahamas 2010) Forest means any area consisting mainly of trees including forest cover, all other vegetation, wetlands, coil and ground beneath it. Bahamas Forestry Act of 2010. http://www.bahamasforestry.com/docs/ForestryAct2010.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_2010_933 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Ireland 2010) To define area as a forest it has to pass these minimum requireme..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_2010_933_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Ireland 2010) To define area as a forest it has to pass these minimum requirements: - tree crown cover: 10%- land area: 0.5 ha - tree height: 2 m. Further IFI has added practical requirements that are in accordance to international definitions: - minimum width of forest: 20 m - maximum permanent gap in forest. 0.5 ha. Tomppo E., Gschwantner T., Lawrence M., 2010. http://www.efi.int/files/attachments/publications/annex_1_to_efi_technical_report_88__2013.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_2010_933_criteria ex:minArea "0.5"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "0.5"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCover "10.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCoverSI "10.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "2.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "2.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minWidth "20.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minWidthSI "20.0"^^xsd:float .

