ex:Def_def_unk_2017_615 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(ICRAF- 2017) Change from a forested to a non-forested state, which depending on..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(ICRAF- 2017) Change from a forested to a non-forested state, which depending on forest definition, relates to both institutional and tree cover dimensions http://dx.doi.org/10.5716/WP16079.PDF"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_2017_822 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(ICRAF- 2017) Land with trees under specified management authority; common defin..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(ICRAF- 2017) Land with trees under specified management authority; common definitions combine biophysical aspects of tree cover (minimum spatial tree cover over defined percentage of time at defined measurement scale) with institutional aspects (excluding trees that are considered to be agricultural) http://dx.doi.org/10.5716/WP16079.PDF"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_2017_907 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Ethiopia 2017) In February 2015 Ethiopia adopted a new forest definition (MEF 2..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_2017_907_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UNFCCC ;
    skos:note "(Ethiopia 2017) In February 2015 Ethiopia adopted a new forest definition (MEF 2015) as follows: 'Land spanning more than 0.5 ha covered by trees (including bamboo) (with a minimum width of 20m or not more than two‐thirds of its length) attaining a height of more than 2m and a canopy cover of more than 20% or trees with the potential to reach these thresholds in situ in due course (Minutes of Forest sector management, MEFCC, Feb. 2015). Ethiopia is in the process of approving this as its national legal definition. http://redd.unfccc.int/files/ethiopia_frel_3.2_final_modified_submission.pdf"@en .

