ex:Def_def_unk_2084_1700 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Forest land is synonymous with \"designated forest land\" and means any parcel of ..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Forest land is synonymous with \"designated forest land\" and means any parcel of land that is twenty or more acres or multiple parcels of land that are contiguous and total twenty or more acres that is or are devoted primarily to growing and harvesting timber. Designated forest land means the land only and does not include a residential homesite. The term includes land used for incidental uses that are compatible with the growing and harvesting of timber but no more than ten percent of the land may be used for such incidental uses. It also includes the land on which appurtenances necessary for the production, preparation, or sale of the timber products exist in conjunction with land producing these products. http://www.mrsc.org/mc/rcw/RCW%20%2084%20%20TITLE/RCW%20%2084%20.%2033%20%20CHAPTER/RCW%20%2084%20.%2033%20.035.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_2084_46 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Forest land is synonymous with \"designated forest land\" and means any parcel of ..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Forest land is synonymous with \"designated forest land\" and means any parcel of land that is twenty or more acres or multiple parcels of land that are contiguous and total twenty or more acres that is or are devoted primarily to growing and harvesting timber. Designated forest land means the land only and does not include a residential homesite. The term includes land used for incidental uses that are compatible with the growing and harvesting of timber but no more than ten percent of the land may be used for such incidental uses. It also includes the land on which appurtenances necessary for the production, preparation, or sale of the timber products exist in conjunction with land producing these products. http://www.mrsc.org/mc/rcw/RCW%20%2084%20%20TITLE/RCW%20%2084%20.%2033%20%20CHAPTER/RCW%20%2084%20.%2033%20.035.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_0 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "DEFINITIONS OF FOREST, DEFORESTATION, AFFORESTATION, AND REFORESTATION" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "DEFINITIONS OF FOREST, DEFORESTATION, AFFORESTATION, AND REFORESTATION"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1028 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Korea, Republic of) Forest is defined as one of followings: 1. collectively sta..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Korea, Republic of) Forest is defined as one of followings: 1. collectively standing and growing trees and bamboos, and the land that have them. 2. the land that temporarily lost standing trees and bamboos. 3. the land that is used for collectively growing trees and bamboos. 4. forestry roads. 5. rockland and wetland within 1, 2 and 3. Forest does not include followings 1. Orchard 2. the land that have growing trees and bamboos within buildings 3. the road with growing street trees. 4. stream banks. Korean Forestry Law. \"Matthias ChangDuck Koo\" koochangd@hotmail.com."@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1046 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Taiwan, ROC) Forest land - the land that is at least 0.5 hectare in size with a..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1046_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_The_Third_Forest_Resources_and_Land_Use_Inventory_in_Taiwan ;
    skos:note "(Taiwan, ROC) Forest land - the land that is at least 0.5 hectare in size with at least 10% of the area covered with tree crowns or commercial bamboo, the forest belt beside road or river is at least 50 meters wide. The road, river, other water area or open lands in forest is less than 20 meters wide. The open land over than 0.5 hectare which is considered to reforestation or afforestation. Source: The Third Forest Resources and Land Use Inventory in Taiwan&uml; - \"&ordf;L&deg;È&sect;&frac12;service\" service@dns.forest.gov.tw"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1046_criteria ex:minArea "0.5"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "0.5"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "50.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "50.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minWidth "50.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minWidthSI "50.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1062 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Kazakhatan) \"forest\" means a natural complex formed on a certain territory base..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UN-FAO ;
    skos:note "(Kazakhatan) \"forest\" means a natural complex formed on a certain territory based on the aggregate of trees and shrubs vegetations and other wildlife components interacting with environment and having environmental, economic and social importance; http://faolex.fao.org/docs/texts/kaz41426E.doc"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1175 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Isle of Man) The term \"tree\" is generally not defined. In certain Acts the term..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Isle of Man) The term \"tree\" is generally not defined. In certain Acts the term is given a special meaning, e.g. - In the Forestry Act \"trees\" is defined as including shrubs. \"IOM Gov DAFF\" <daff@gov.im"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1179 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Swaziland) \"tree\" means a perennial plant having a self-supporting woody main s..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Swaziland) \"tree\" means a perennial plant having a self-supporting woody main stem or trunk and growing to a height of not less than five feet, but does not include bushes or shrubs http://www.sntc.org.sz/legislat/sntcact1.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1190 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "A large perennial woody plant. Though there is no set definition of size, it is ..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1190_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "A large perennial woody plant. Though there is no set definition of size, it is generally at least 6 m (20 ft) high at maturity, and with branches supported on a single main stem. Compared with most other forms of plants, trees are long-lived. http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tree"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1190_criteria ex:minHeight "6.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "6.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1191 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "A large perennial woody plant. Though there is no set definition of size, it is ..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1191_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "A large perennial woody plant. Though there is no set definition of size, it is generally at least 6 m (20 ft) high at maturity, and with branches supported on a single main stem. Compared with most other forms of plants, trees are long-lived. A few species of trees grow to over 100 m (300 ft) tall and some live for several millennia. Trees are important components of the natural landscape and significant elements in landscaping. http://explanation-guide.info/meaning/Tree.html and http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tree"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1191_criteria ex:minHeight "6.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "6.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1193 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "A woody perennial plant that has a trunk circumference of twenty (20) inches mea..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "A woody perennial plant that has a trunk circumference of twenty (20) inches measured at twenty-four (24) inches above the ground surface; or A woody perennial plant at least fifteen (15) feet in height that usually, but not necessarily, has a single trunk. In applying subsection (1) above, for trees with more than one trunk, the circumference measurement shall be ascertained from a single measurement around the outside perimeter of all trunks and shall not be calculated as the sum total of the circumferences of the individual trunks. References to \"tree\" shall include the plural. http://www.tiburon.org/Government/images/Departments/planning%20dept/plng%20forms/TreeOrd.htm#Section%2015A-2.%20Definitions."@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1194 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Tree means any tree, sapling or shrub, now or hereafter growing on property of t..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Tree means any tree, sapling or shrub, now or hereafter growing on property of the City, unless a contrary intention appears. http://code.municipalworld.com/kitchener/690.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1195 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Tree means any tree. http://www.newrichmond.org/treeord.pdf" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Tree means any tree. http://www.newrichmond.org/treeord.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1196 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Tree -The definition of a tree that most tree scholars recognize is \"a woody pla..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Tree -The definition of a tree that most tree scholars recognize is \"a woody plant with a single erect perennial trunk that reaches at least 3 inches in diameter at breast height (DBH} when mature https://www.thoughtco.com/worlds-smallest-tree-species-1343503?utm_campaign=wilat&utm_medium=email&utm_source=cn_nl&utm_content=9497194&utm_term"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1197 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Usually trees are defined as having a large, single trunk rising above the groun..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Usually trees are defined as having a large, single trunk rising above the ground. The trunk is composed of wood and is divided usually into a series of branches. http://www.alienexplorer.com/ecology/e17.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1198 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Woody perennial plant characterized by having a main stem or trunk or a multi-st..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Woody perennial plant characterized by having a main stem or trunk or a multi-stemmed trunk system with more or less definitely formed crown, usually over ten feet high at maturity. This definition shall not include trees planted, grown and held for sale by licensed nurseries or the first removal or transplanting of such trees pursuant to and as part of the operation of a licensed nursery business. http://bpc.iserver.net/cgi-bin/hilite.pl/codes/scottsva/_DATA/TITLE17/Chapter_17_44__GENERAL_AND_SPECIAL/17_44_080_Tree_protection_regu.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1206 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "The following table (table 3) focuses on national definitions of forest. Some co..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "The following table (table 3) focuses on national definitions of forest. Some countries reported having no national or official definitions of forest or tree. This information is also useful. Countries reporting no official definitions include:"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1207 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "You will note that some of the definitions contain a minimum height for a plant ..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "You will note that some of the definitions contain a minimum height for a plant to be classed as a tree. If taken literally, newly planted or established seedlings would not be considered \"trees\" under these definitions. If they are not considered trees, what are they?"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1216 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "A forest with low tree densities, often defined as less than 20% to 30% crown co..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1216_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "A forest with low tree densities, often defined as less than 20% to 30% crown cover when trees are mature. http://www.sfrc.ufl.edu/Extension/ssfor11.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1216_criteria ex:minCanopyCover "30.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCoverSI "30.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1217 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "A landscape where the dominant vegetation is composed of tree species that are g..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "A landscape where the dominant vegetation is composed of tree species that are generally not capable of producing commercial tree growth. http://www.for.nau.edu/courses/for250/Definitions/Definitions.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1219 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "An area planted to trees for fuel, or timber. http://www.echonet.org/Technotes/A..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "An area planted to trees for fuel, or timber. http://www.echonet.org/Technotes/AgroforestryPrinciples.html#definitions"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1220 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "An environment characterized by patchy stands of relatively short trees separate..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "An environment characterized by patchy stands of relatively short trees separated by grassy areas. http://www.becominghuman.org/resources/glossary.php?mode=definition&termID=268"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1221 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Area that has some forest characteristics but does not meet the definition of fo..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Area that has some forest characteristics but does not meet the definition of forest given above. Includes areas occupied by windbreaks groups of trees, fallow land, and shrubland. http://www.wrm.org.uy/actors/WB/1991policy3.html and. https://www.uni-hohenheim.de/i490a/teaching/M4901-430/ws_03_04/reading_materials/New_Neef_Schwarzmeier_Studie.pdf."@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1223 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "In ecological terms, a forest may be differentiated from a woodland: a forest is..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "In ecological terms, a forest may be differentiated from a woodland: a forest is considered to have a more or less closed canopy, where the branches and foliage of trees meet or interlock; a woodland is considered to have an open canopy, where some sunlight penetrates between the trees (see also: savanna). http://explanation-guide.info/meaning/Forest.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1224 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Trees outside forests (ToF). Trees and tree environments on lands not defined as..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1224_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UN-FAO ;
    skos:note "Trees outside forests (ToF). Trees and tree environments on lands not defined as forest or other wooded lands. Include: (a) groups of trees covering an area of less 0.5 ha, including lines and shelterbelts along infrastructure features and agricultural fields; (b) scattered trees in agricultural landscapes; (c) tree plantations mainly for other purposes than wood, such a fruit orchards and palm plantations; and trees in parks and gardens and around buildings. ToF are not assigned an area in the overall land use classification, but occurs inside Other wooded land and Other land. Although the definition of ToF is based on the trees, the concept includes also the site and other vegetation at the location. (FAO 2000b)"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1224_criteria ex:minArea "0.5"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "0.5"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1225 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Wood lot means any piece of land of which trees in each hectare being not less t..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Wood lot means any piece of land of which trees in each hectare being not less than twenty-five; http://www.goaforest.com/regulation/body_preservoftrees2.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1226 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Wooded area - Corresponds to the FAO definition of forest and woodland. It refer..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UN-FAO ;
    skos:note "Wooded area - Corresponds to the FAO definition of forest and woodland. It refers to land under natural or planted stands of trees, whether productive or not, and includes land from which forests have been cleared but that will be reforested in the foreseeable future. http://www.tpesp.es/informe/HTMNF/COMPENDI/CHAP8.HTM"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1227 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Woodland refers to the type of land cover characterized by trees and shrubs: htt..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Woodland refers to the type of land cover characterized by trees and shrubs: http://www.millenniumassessment.org/documents/document.290.aspx.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1231 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Stocking – The relative degree of occupancy land by trees, measured as basal are..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Stocking – The relative degree of occupancy land by trees, measured as basal area or the number of trees in a stand by size or age and spacing, compared to the basal area or number of trees required to fully utilize the growth potential of the land; that is, the stocking standard. http://216.239.39.100/search?q=cache:iFF2UlzBb4kC:socrates.lv-hrc.nevada.edu/fia/dab/core1-6/appendix7_12_00.doc+%22stand+density%22++definition+glossary&hl=en&ie=UTF-8"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1232 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "The amount of live trees on a given area in relation to what is considered the o..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USDA ;
    skos:note "The amount of live trees on a given area in relation to what is considered the optimum. [Source: USDA Forest Service General Technical Report WO-44. Forest Stand Density and Stocking: concepts, terms, and use of the stocking guides. 8 p.]"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1234 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "3.1 AFFORESTATION - Afforestation may be a legal term or a process of stocking l..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "3.1 AFFORESTATION - Afforestation may be a legal term or a process of stocking land. In the case of the latter, we group the definitions into those that imply a change in land cover only and those that imply a change in land cover and use. Four definitions specify \"crops\" implying that the trees will be later removed for commercial purposes. The time period for lands \"never having been forested\" vary from never to 30 to 100 years."@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1238 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Generally refers to the planting of trees on ground where trees have never exist..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Generally refers to the planting of trees on ground where trees have never existed or were last present hundreds of years ago. Afforestation carbon offset projects bear an additional burden of showing ecological compatibility. http://www.usask.ca/agriculture/caedac/dbases/glossary.htm and http://www.undp.org/seed/forest/pdf/InnovatForesFinanc.pdf."@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1245 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Forest loss; typically defined as a forest losing 40 percent or more of the tree..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Forest loss; typically defined as a forest losing 40 percent or more of the trees. http://www.oznet.ksu.edu/library/MISC2/SB661.PDF"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1246 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "The clearing, destroying, or otherwise removal of trees through deliberate, natu..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "The clearing, destroying, or otherwise removal of trees through deliberate, natural or accidental means. http://www.pachamama.org/effects-of-deforestation"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1252 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "The clearing of virgin forests, or intentional destruction or removal of trees a..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "The clearing of virgin forests, or intentional destruction or removal of trees and other vegetation for agricultural, commercial, housing, or firewood use without replanting (reforesting) and without allowing time for the forest to regenerate itself. Deforestation is one of the major factors contributing to the greenhouse effect and desertification. http://www.businessdictionary.com/definition/deforestation.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1254 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "The willful and permanent transition in vegetative cover from that which is clea..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "The willful and permanent transition in vegetative cover from that which is clearly \"forest\" (regardless of the commercial or aesthetic value of the trees) to that which is clearly devoted to other uses - with trees seen as undesirable invaders. On this definition, the clear cutting of portions of a forest with the intention of allowing regeneration of trees does not qualify as deforestation - even though all the trees are removed at a certain time (Daniel W. Bromley, Deforestation: Institutional Causes And Solutions, in World Forests, Society and Environment, Volume I. In press)."@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1260 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Generally refers to planting trees on land that has been cleared of forest withi..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Generally refers to planting trees on land that has been cleared of forest within the relatively recent past. May or may not refer to planting trees on land that has just been harvested. . http://www.climateservices.com/glossary.htm and http://www.undp.org/seed/forest/pdf/InnovatForesFinanc.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1265 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Renewal of a tree crop, either by natural or artificial means. -Young tree crop ..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Renewal of a tree crop, either by natural or artificial means. -Young tree crop (17). http://rredc.nrel.gov/biomass/forest/tim_glossary/t_glossary.html#F"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1267 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "The renewal of a tree crop through either natural means (seeded on-site from adj..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "The renewal of a tree crop through either natural means (seeded on-site from adjacent stands or deposited by wind, birds or animals) or artificial means (by planting seedlings or direct seeding). http://www.interfor.com/glossary/glossary29.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1268 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "The purpose of this paper is not to come up with final definitions, but to show ..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "The purpose of this paper is not to come up with final definitions, but to show the breadth of definitions in use. There is a test at the end of this document. Ultimately, all countries should come up with the same answers. In the meantime, we can ponder such things as are natural tree invasions, in the case of afforestation, and natural regeneration, in the case of reforestation, acknowledged or accepted? Do the terms reforestation and afforestation imply that there will be timber crops produced or just tree cover increased? . Do human-induced \"afforestation, deforestation, and reforestation\" cover all forestry activities that affect carbon emissions and sinks we need to track? What about natural deforestation, afforestation, and reforestation? Do we need other terms to describe other situations - such as the restocking of a recent clearcut area?"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1269 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "If one is speaking of carbon sequestration, the fact that some lands with trees ..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "If one is speaking of carbon sequestration, the fact that some lands with trees are considered forests and others are considered agricultural lands is unimportant. Rather than getting embroiled with definitions of forests, etc., we may prefer to speak of vegetated, revegetated, and devegetated lands where woody vegetation is the primary interest. Thus, one would include all lands with trees on them (forests, agricultural lands, urban areas, etc) and the changes in that cover."@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1271 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Definitions: forest, tree, forest summary, woodland, afforestation, deforestatio..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Definitions: forest, tree, forest summary, woodland, afforestation, deforestation, reforestation, other terms."@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1272 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "An area of woodland, esp. one owned by the sovereign and set apart as a hunting ..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "An area of woodland, esp. one owned by the sovereign and set apart as a hunting ground with its own laws and officers. http://dictionary.reverso.net/english-definition/forest%20reserve"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1275 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "A piece of land that is thickly covered with trees is the general of definition ..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "A piece of land that is thickly covered with trees is the general of definition of a forest. Forest is also known as woods, weald or woodlands. http://hassam.hubpages.com/hub/Types-Of-Forests"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1277 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Forest is defined as >30% crown cover and the tree height shall be >7 m. Seedlin..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1277_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Forest is defined as >30% crown cover and the tree height shall be >7 m. Seedlings under forest are also included in this class. Areas occupied by forest and woodlands with a vegetation pattern composed of native or exotic coniferous trees, and which can be used for the production of timber or other forest products. The forest trees are under normal climatic conditions higher than 5 m with a canopy closure of 30% at least. http://www.grida.no/baltic/related/balans_landcover_classification_methodology_ver2.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1277_criteria ex:minCanopyCover "30.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCoverSI "30.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "7.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "7.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1278 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Land that is at least 10 percent stocked by forest trees of any size, or land fo..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1278_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Land that is at least 10 percent stocked by forest trees of any size, or land formerly having such tree cover, and is not currently developed for a nonforest use. The minimum area for classification as forest land is one acre. Roadside, stream-side, and shelterbelt strips of timber must have a crown width at least 120 feet wide to qualify as forest land. Unimproved roads and trails, streams and other bodies of water, or natural clearings in forested areas shall be classified as forest, if less than 120 feet in width or an acre in size. Grazed woodlands, reverting fields, and pastures that are not actively maintained are included if the above qualifications are satisfied. (Also see definitions of nonforest land, idle farmland and improved/maintained pasture.) www.socrates.lv-hrc.nevada.edu/fia/dab/core1-7/appendix7_12_00.doc"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1278_criteria ex:minHeight "120.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "36.576"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1280 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(UN-EP-GRID) Forest is defined as >30% crown cover and the tree height shall be ..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1280_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UNEP ;
    skos:note "(UN-EP-GRID) Forest is defined as >30% crown cover and the tree height shall be >7 m. Seedlings under forest are also included in this class. Areas occupied by forest and woodlands with a vegetation pattern composed of native or exotic coniferous trees, and which can be used for the production of timber or other forest products. The forest trees are under normal climatic conditions higher than 5 m with a canopy closure of 30% at least. www.grida.no/baltic/related/balans_landcover_classification_methodology_ver2.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1280_criteria ex:minCanopyCover "30.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCoverSI "30.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "7.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "7.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1330 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "In ecological terms, a forest may be differentiated from a woodland: a forest is..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "In ecological terms, a forest may be differentiated from a woodland: a forest is considered to have a more or less closed canopy, where the branches and foliage of trees meet or interlock; a woodland is considered to have an open canopy, where some sunlight penetrates between the trees (see also: savanna). http://explanation-guide.info/meaning/Forest.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1331 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Wooded area - Corresponds to the FAO definition of forest and woodland. It refer..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UN-FAO ;
    skos:note "Wooded area - Corresponds to the FAO definition of forest and woodland. It refers to land under natural or planted stands of trees, whether productive or not, and includes land from which forests have been cleared but that will be reforested in the foreseeable future. http://www.tpesp.es/informe/HTMNF/COMPENDI/CHAP8.HTM"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1332 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Woodland refers to the type of land cover characterized by trees and shrubs: htt..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Woodland refers to the type of land cover characterized by trees and shrubs: http://www.millenniumassessment.org/documents/document.290.aspx.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1334 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "The permanent destruction of forests and woodlands; it occurs as the forests are..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "The permanent destruction of forests and woodlands; it occurs as the forests are converted for agricultural uses. http://www.auburn.edu/~hurlbkl/definition.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1338 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Recommended Definition) -While a definition of \"forest\" that is globally accept..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1338_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Recommended Definition) -While a definition of \"forest\" that is globally acceptable and appropriate for monitoring using standard remote sensing options will necessarily be based on a small set of easily measured parameters, there are dangers when simple definitions are applied locally. At the very least, we recommend that natural forest be differentiated from plantations and that for defining \"forest\" the lower height limit defining \"trees\" be set at more than 5 m tall with the minimum cover of trees be set at more than 40%. These changes will help reduce greenhouse gas emissions from what is now termed forest \"degradation\" without increasing monitoring costs. Furthermore, these minor changes in the definition of \"forest\" will promote the switch from degradation to responsible forest management, which will help mitigate global warming while protecting biodiversity and contributing to sustainable development. http://www.forestcarbonportal.com/resource/critical-need-new-definitions-forest-and-forest-degradation-global-climate-change-agreement"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1338_criteria ex:minCanopyCover "40.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCoverSI "40.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "5.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "5.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1349 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Induced land degradation in developing countries that is a direct result of land..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Induced land degradation in developing countries that is a direct result of land tenure systems that facilitate property-right acquisition in idle lands. http://www.auburn.edu/~hurlbkl/definition.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1351 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "DEFINITIONS OF FOREST, DEFORESTATION, AFFORESTATION, AND REFORESTATION" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "DEFINITIONS OF FOREST, DEFORESTATION, AFFORESTATION, AND REFORESTATION"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1354 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Our search focused on the key terms - forest, afforestation, deforestation and r..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Our search focused on the key terms - forest, afforestation, deforestation and reforestation. However, we found that we need to discuss and have a common of understanding of other terms as well. Groupings are based upon literal interpretations of the definitions. The decision on which terms and definitions presented here must be considered in light with the end point in mind. Most importantly, we need a clear understanding of what it is that we are interested in and how we wish to use the information. It may turn out that none of the terms listed below are what is needed."@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1355 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Before we can get into a discussion of Afforestation, Deforestation, and Affores..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Before we can get into a discussion of Afforestation, Deforestation, and Afforestation, we need to have an understanding of some basic terms and concepts. These include land - (the terrestrial bio-productive system that comprises soil vegetation, other biota, and the ecological and hydrological processes that operate within the system (Convention to Combat Desertification)), land use, land cover, tree, forest, natural forest, semi-natural forest, plantation, stocking and forestry. Here are some of the definitions we found:"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1356 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Definitions: forest, tree, forest summary, woodland, afforestation, deforestatio..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Definitions: forest, tree, forest summary, woodland, afforestation, deforestation, reforestation, other terms."@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1374 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Taiwan, ROC) Forest land - the land that is at least 0.5 hectare in size with a..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1374_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_The_Third_Forest_Resources_and_Land_Use_Inventory_in_Taiwan ;
    skos:note "(Taiwan, ROC) Forest land - the land that is at least 0.5 hectare in size with at least 10% of the area covered with tree crowns or commercial bamboo, the forest belt beside road or river is at least 50 meters wide. The road, river, other water area or open lands in forest is less than 20 meters wide. The open land over than 0.5 hectare which is considered to reforestation or afforestation. Source: The Third Forest Resources and Land Use Inventory in Taiwan&uml; - \"&ordf;L&deg;È&sect;&frac12;service\" service@dns.forest.gov.tw"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1374_criteria ex:minArea "0.5"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "0.5"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "50.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "50.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minWidth "50.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minWidthSI "50.0"^^xsd:float .

