    skos:note "Is afforestation by natural means a sink that we need to track?"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1398 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "A fancy word that means exactly what you probably think it means: the destructio..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "A fancy word that means exactly what you probably think it means: the destruction of forested lands. http://science.howstuffworks.com/environmental/conservation/issues/what-is-deforestation.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1399 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "The clearing, destroying, or otherwise removal of trees through deliberate, natu..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "The clearing, destroying, or otherwise removal of trees through deliberate, natural or accidental means. http://www.pachamama.org/effects-of-deforestation"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1407 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "The clearing of virgin forests, or intentional destruction or removal of trees a..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "The clearing of virgin forests, or intentional destruction or removal of trees and other vegetation for agricultural, commercial, housing, or firewood use without replanting (reforesting) and without allowing time for the forest to regenerate itself. Deforestation is one of the major factors contributing to the greenhouse effect and desertification. http://www.businessdictionary.com/definition/deforestation.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1409 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "The willful and permanent transition in vegetative cover from that which is clea..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "The willful and permanent transition in vegetative cover from that which is clearly \"forest\" (regardless of the commercial or aesthetic value of the trees) to that which is clearly devoted to other uses - with trees seen as undesirable invaders. On this definition, the clear cutting of portions of a forest with the intention of allowing regeneration of trees does not qualify as deforestation - even though all the trees are removed at a certain time (Daniel W. Bromley, Deforestation: Institutional Causes And Solutions, in World Forests, Society and Environment, Volume I. In press)."@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1417 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Do we need to track reforestation by natural means as a sink?" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Do we need to track reforestation by natural means as a sink?"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1419 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "If change of a designation of forest land to protected, wilderness, or national ..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "If change of a designation of forest land to protected, wilderness, or national park is considered a change in land administration or use, and if change in land use is considered deforestation and if deforestation is considered an emission, then a nation may be reluctant to protect or preserve its forest resources."@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1420 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Implications - Deforestation definition may not be politically acceptable. If bi..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Implications - Deforestation definition may not be politically acceptable. If biomass is not tracked, one could remove the overstory to within the crown cover threshold and be required to report removal as an emission."@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1421 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Here are some generic, politically-correct definitions of deforestation, refores..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Here are some generic, politically-correct definitions of deforestation, reforestation and afforestation applicable to any definition of \"forest land.\""@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1422 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "The purpose of this paper is not to come up with final definitions, but to show ..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "The purpose of this paper is not to come up with final definitions, but to show the breadth of definitions in use. There is a test at the end of this document. Ultimately, all countries should come up with the same answers. In the meantime, we can ponder such things as are natural tree invasions, in the case of afforestation, and natural regeneration, in the case of reforestation, acknowledged or accepted? Do the terms reforestation and afforestation imply that there will be timber crops produced or just tree cover increased? . Do human-induced \"afforestation, deforestation, and reforestation\" cover all forestry activities that affect carbon emissions and sinks we need to track? What about natural deforestation, afforestation, and reforestation? Do we need other terms to describe other situations - such as the restocking of a recent clearcut area?"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1423 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Gambia1998) \"Forest\" means a land area with at least 10% tree cover, naturally ..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1423_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UN-FAO ;
    skos:note "(Gambia1998) \"Forest\" means a land area with at least 10% tree cover, naturally grown or planted, and or 50% or more shrub and tree regeneration cover and includes Government forest parks, community forests and protected forests irrespective of their tree and shrub cover; provided that vegetation on fallow land is not a forest except as specified in section 5 of this Act http://extwprlegs1.fao.org/docs/pdf/gam19052.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1423_criteria ex:minCanopyCover "50.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCoverSI "50.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1435 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "The willful and permanent transition in vegetative cover from that which is clea..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "The willful and permanent transition in vegetative cover from that which is clearly \"forest\" (regardless of the commercial or aesthetic value of the trees) to that which is clearly devoted to other uses - with trees seen as undesirable invaders. On this definition, the clear cutting of portions of a forest with the intention of allowing regeneration of trees does not qualify as deforestation - even though all the trees are removed at a certain time (Daniel W. Bromley, Deforestation: Institutional Causes And Solutions, in World Forests, Society and Environment, Volume I. In press)."@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1438 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "The purpose of this paper is not to come up with final definitions, but to show ..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "The purpose of this paper is not to come up with final definitions, but to show the breadth of definitions in use. There is a test at the end of this document. Ultimately, all countries should come up with the same answers. In the meantime, we can ponder such things as are natural tree invasions, in the case of afforestation, and natural regeneration, in the case of reforestation, acknowledged or accepted? Do the terms reforestation and afforestation imply that there will be timber crops produced or just tree cover increased? . Do human-induced \"afforestation, deforestation, and reforestation\" cover all forestry activities that affect carbon emissions and sinks we need to track? What about natural deforestation, afforestation, and reforestation? Do we need other terms to describe other situations - such as the restocking of a recent clearcut area?"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1440 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Before we can get into a discussion of Afforestation, Deforestation, and Affores..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Before we can get into a discussion of Afforestation, Deforestation, and Afforestation, we need to have an understanding of some basic terms and concepts. These include land - (the terrestrial bio-productive system that comprises soil vegetation, other biota, and the ecological and hydrological processes that operate within the system (Convention to Combat Desertification)), land use, land cover, tree, forest, natural forest, semi-natural forest, plantation, stocking and forestry. Here are some of the definitions we found:"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1446 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Forest – defined as either a geographic area or delineated by the general compos..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Forest – defined as either a geographic area or delineated by the general composition of individuals; https://howlingpixel.com/wiki/Outline_of_forestry"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1448 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(American Legislative Exchange Council) “Forest” means a parcel of land in which..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(American Legislative Exchange Council) “Forest” means a parcel of land in which at least 80% of the parcel is producing or is capable of producing at least 20 cubic feet of merchantable timber per acre per year {or as defined by state statute}. https://www.alec.org/model-policy/the-right-to-practice-forestry-act/"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1453 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Note, many nations may use several definitions of forest land such as one as giv..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UN-FAO ;
    skos:note "Note, many nations may use several definitions of forest land such as one as given in their forestry laws, that which is used for reporting to the FAO for its periodic global forest resource assessment and that which is used for reporting under the Kyoto Protocol under UNFCCC."@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1462 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Trinidad and Tobago) Forest Reserve - means and includes a forest and every par..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Trinidad and Tobago) Forest Reserve - means and includes a forest and every part of a forest declared to be a Forest Reserve under the Land Regulations for the time being in force – Forest Act: Chapter 66:01. Narine Lackhan, Director of Forestry."@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1488 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Trinidad and Tobago) Forest Reserve - means and includes a forest and every par..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Trinidad and Tobago) Forest Reserve - means and includes a forest and every part of a forest declared to be a Forest Reserve under the Land Regulations for the time being in force – Forest Act: Chapter 66:01. Narine Lackhan, Director of Forestry."@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1502 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Iceland) Forest land (skoglendi) - Land that is or will be, mostly or fully, co..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Iceland) Forest land (skoglendi) - Land that is or will be, mostly or fully, covered by forest vegetation, natural or planted, forest or scrub*. *The Icelandic word \"kjarr\", which is translated as scrub, refers to low-growing and crooked birch and in some cases willows. Source: Latest draft of a new forestry act : Þröstur Eysteinsson <throstur@simnet.is"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1505 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Korea, Republic of) Forest is defined as one of followings: 1. collectively sta..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Korea, Republic of) Forest is defined as one of followings: 1. collectively standing and growing trees and bamboos, and the land that have them. 2. the land that temporarily lost standing trees and bamboos. 3. the land that is used for collectively growing trees and bamboos. 4. forestry roads. 5. rockland and wetland within 1, 2 and 3. Forest does not include followings 1. Orchard 2. the land that have growing trees and bamboos within buildings 3. the road with growing street trees. 4. stream banks. Korean Forestry Law. \"Matthias ChangDuck Koo\" koochangd@hotmail.com."@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_151 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Trinidad and Tobago) Forest Reserve - means and includes a forest and every par..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Trinidad and Tobago) Forest Reserve - means and includes a forest and every part of a forest declared to be a Forest Reserve under the Land Regulations for the time being in force – Forest Act: Chapter 66:01. Narine Lackhan, Director of Forestry."@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1536 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Isle of Man) The term \"tree\" is generally not defined. In certain Acts the term..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Isle of Man) The term \"tree\" is generally not defined. In certain Acts the term is given a special meaning, e.g. - In the Forestry Act \"trees\" is defined as including shrubs. \"IOM Gov DAFF\" <daff@gov.im"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1544 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Seychelles (uses the international convention for these definitions - but conven..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Seychelles (uses the international convention for these definitions - but conventions not specified) Source: M.K Vielle Assistant Director Forestry. : \"doe\" <doe@seychelles.net"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1547 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "An area planted to trees for fuel, or timber. http://www.echonet.org/Technotes/A..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "An area planted to trees for fuel, or timber. http://www.echonet.org/Technotes/AgroforestryPrinciples.html#definitions"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1551 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "The purpose of this paper is not to come up with final definitions, but to show ..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "The purpose of this paper is not to come up with final definitions, but to show the breadth of definitions in use. There is a test at the end of this document. Ultimately, all countries should come up with the same answers. In the meantime, we can ponder such things as are natural tree invasions, in the case of afforestation, and natural regeneration, in the case of reforestation, acknowledged or accepted? Do the terms reforestation and afforestation imply that there will be timber crops produced or just tree cover increased? . Do human-induced \"afforestation, deforestation, and reforestation\" cover all forestry activities that affect carbon emissions and sinks we need to track? What about natural deforestation, afforestation, and reforestation? Do we need other terms to describe other situations - such as the restocking of a recent clearcut area?"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1554 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Our search focused on the key terms - forest, afforestation, deforestation and r..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Our search focused on the key terms - forest, afforestation, deforestation and reforestation. However, we found that we need to discuss and have a common of understanding of other terms as well. Groupings are based upon literal interpretations of the definitions. The decision on which terms and definitions presented here must be considered in light with the end point in mind. Most importantly, we need a clear understanding of what it is that we are interested in and how we wish to use the information. It may turn out that none of the terms listed below are what is needed."@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1555 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Before we can get into a discussion of Afforestation, Deforestation, and Affores..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Before we can get into a discussion of Afforestation, Deforestation, and Afforestation, we need to have an understanding of some basic terms and concepts. These include land - (the terrestrial bio-productive system that comprises soil vegetation, other biota, and the ecological and hydrological processes that operate within the system (Convention to Combat Desertification)), land use, land cover, tree, forest, natural forest, semi-natural forest, plantation, stocking and forestry. Here are some of the definitions we found:"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1556 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Recommended Definition) -While a definition of \"forest\" that is globally accept..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1556_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Recommended Definition) -While a definition of \"forest\" that is globally acceptable and appropriate for monitoring using standard remote sensing options will necessarily be based on a small set of easily measured parameters, there are dangers when simple definitions are applied locally. At the very least, we recommend that natural forest be differentiated from plantations and that for defining \"forest\" the lower height limit defining \"trees\" be set at more than 5 m tall with the minimum cover of trees be set at more than 40%. These changes will help reduce greenhouse gas emissions from what is now termed forest \"degradation\" without increasing monitoring costs. Furthermore, these minor changes in the definition of \"forest\" will promote the switch from degradation to responsible forest management, which will help mitigate global warming while protecting biodiversity and contributing to sustainable development. http://www.forestcarbonportal.com/resource/critical-need-new-definitions-forest-and-forest-degradation-global-climate-change-agreement"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1556_criteria ex:minCanopyCover "40.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCoverSI "40.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "5.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "5.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1559 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "An ecosystem characterized by more or less dense and extensive tree cover, often..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "An ecosystem characterized by more or less dense and extensive tree cover, often consisting of stands varying in characteristics such as species compositions, structure, age class and associated processes, and commonly including meadows, streams, fish, and wildlife. Thus forest could be defined as a set of land parcels that has or could have tree vegetation and is managed as a whole to achieve the objective of the owner. http://www.environmental-auditing.org/LinkClick.aspx?fileticket=fbx%2FbAIVeFU%3D&tabid=128&mid=568"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1565 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(UN-FCCC )Forest land - As part of COP7 (Marrakech accords) it was decided that ..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UNFCCC ;
    skos:note "(UN-FCCC )Forest land - As part of COP7 (Marrakech accords) it was decided that parties could select a single value of tree height, crown area and area to define forests, subject to certain ranges. The Designated National Authority in each country is responsible for forest definition (see http://cdm.unfccc.int/DNA and http://www.snvworld.org/en/regions/asia/ourwork/Documents/SNV_UnderstandingREDD.pdf)"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1566 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(World Bank) - An area of land of not less than 1.0 hectare with tree crown cove..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1566_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(World Bank) - An area of land of not less than 1.0 hectare with tree crown cover (or equivalent stocking level) of more than 10 per cent with trees with the potential to reach a minimum height of 2 meters at maturity in situ. A forest may consist of either closed forest formations where trees of various stories and undergrowth cover a high proportion of the ground or open forest. Young natural stands and all plantations which have yet to reach a crown density of 10 per cent or tree height of 2 meters are included under forest, as are areas normally forming part of the forest area which are temporarily unstocked as a result of human intervention such as harvesting or natural causes but which are expected to revert to forest. The definition includes forests dedicated to forest production, protection, multiple- uses or conservation, whether formally recognized or not. The definition excludes areas where other land uses not dependent on tree cover predominate, such as agriculture, grazing or settlements. In low forest-cover countries, the definition may be expanded to include areas covered by trees which fall below the 10 percent threshold for canopy density, but are considered forest under local conditions. http://www.iucn.org/themes/fcp/activities/publications/worldbankdraftdefinitions.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1566_criteria ex:minArea "1.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "1.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCover "10.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCoverSI "10.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "2.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "2.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1567 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(A/R - SSC A/R) - “Forest” is a minimum area of land of 0.05-1.0 hectares with t..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1567_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UNFCCC ;
    skos:note "(A/R - SSC A/R) - “Forest” is a minimum area of land of 0.05-1.0 hectares with tree crown cover (or equivalent stocking level) of more than 10-30 per cent with trees with the potential to reach a minimum height of 2-5 metres at maturity in situ. A forest may consist either of closed forest formations where trees of various storeys and undergrowth cover a high proportion of the ground or open forest. Young natural stands and all plantations which have yet to reach a crown density of 10-30 per cent or tree height of 2-5 metres are included under forest, as are areas normally forming part of the forest area which are temporarily unstocked as a result of human intervention such as harvesting or natural causes but which are expected to revert to forest. A Party not included in Annex I may host an A/R CDM project activity if it has selected and reported to the Executive Board through its designated national authority for the CDM the parameters it has chosen for the definition of “forest” to be used for the purposes of hosting A/R project activities under the CDM. http://cdm.unfccc.int/Reference/Guidclarif/glos_CDM_v04.pdf UNFCCC"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1567_criteria ex:minArea "1.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "1.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "5.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "5.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1569 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(UN-DP) Refers to land under natural or planted stands of trees, whether product..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_United_Nations ;
    skos:note "(UN-DP) Refers to land under natural or planted stands of trees, whether productive or not, including land from which forest has been cleared but which will be reforested in the foreseeable future, and including areas occupied by roads, small cleared tracts and other small open areas within the forest that constitute an integral part of the forest. Includes land under coniferous and non-coniferous forest, land under mixed forest and other wooded land. http://www.undp.kz/infobase/glossary_sector.html?glos_id%5B%5D=42"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1587 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Ethiopia KP) The Ethiopian DNA has determined that within Ethiopia, a forest is..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1587_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Ethiopia KP) The Ethiopian DNA has determined that within Ethiopia, a forest is defined as land with trees that has:  A minimum area of 0.05 hectares;  A minimum tree crown cover of 20 per cent;  A minimum average tree height above 2 m. http://www.climate-standards.org/projects/files/ethiopia/Ethiopia_Humbo_CCBA_PDD_June_6.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1587_criteria ex:minArea "0.05"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "0.05"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "2.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "2.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1614 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Korea, Republic of) Forest is defined as one of followings: 1. collectively sta..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Korea, Republic of) Forest is defined as one of followings: 1. collectively standing and growing trees and bamboos, and the land that have them. 2. the land that temporarily lost standing trees and bamboos. 3. the land that is used for collectively growing trees and bamboos. 4. forestry roads. 5. rockland and wetland within 1, 2 and 3. Forest does not include followings 1. Orchard 2. the land that have growing trees and bamboos within buildings 3. the road with growing street trees. 4. stream banks. Korean Forestry Law. \"Matthias ChangDuck Koo\" koochangd@hotmail.com."@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1664 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "An environment characterized by patchy stands of relatively short trees separate..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "An environment characterized by patchy stands of relatively short trees separated by grassy areas. http://www.becominghuman.org/resources/glossary.php?mode=definition&termID=268"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1666 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Wooded area - Corresponds to the FAO definition of forest and woodland. It refer..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UN-FAO ;
    skos:note "Wooded area - Corresponds to the FAO definition of forest and woodland. It refers to land under natural or planted stands of trees, whether productive or not, and includes land from which forests have been cleared but that will be reforested in the foreseeable future. http://www.tpesp.es/informe/HTMNF/COMPENDI/CHAP8.HTM"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1670 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Stocking – The relative degree of occupancy land by trees, measured as basal are..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Stocking – The relative degree of occupancy land by trees, measured as basal area or the number of trees in a stand by size or age and spacing, compared to the basal area or number of trees required to fully utilize the growth potential of the land; that is, the stocking standard. http://216.239.39.100/search?q=cache:iFF2UlzBb4kC:socrates.lv-hrc.nevada.edu/fia/dab/core1-6/appendix7_12_00.doc+%22stand+density%22++definition+glossary&hl=en&ie=UTF-8"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1671 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "The amount of live trees on a given area in relation to what is considered the o..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USDA ;
    skos:note "The amount of live trees on a given area in relation to what is considered the optimum. [Source: USDA Forest Service General Technical Report WO-44. Forest Stand Density and Stocking: concepts, terms, and use of the stocking guides. 8 p.]"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1673 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Czech Republic1995) Afforestation shall mean the establishment of forest stand,..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Czech Republic1995) Afforestation shall mean the establishment of forest stand, http://www.uhul.cz/images/ke_stazeni/legislativa_jazyky/Lesni_zakon_en.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1681 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "The renewal of a tree crop through either natural means (seeded on-site from adj..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "The renewal of a tree crop through either natural means (seeded on-site from adjacent stands or deposited by wind, birds or animals) or artificial means (by planting seedlings or direct seeding). http://www.interfor.com/glossary/glossary29.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1684 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "A dense grove of trees and underbrush covering a large tract. Grove - A small wo..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "A dense grove of trees and underbrush covering a large tract. Grove - A small wood without underbrush. Wood - A dense grove of trees usually greater in extent than a grove and smaller than a forest. Thicket - A dense growth of shrubbery or small trees. http://www.thealmightyguru.com/Pointless/NatureDefinitions.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1685 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Ecosystem characterized by more or less dense and extensive tree cover, i.e., la..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Ecosystem characterized by more or less dense and extensive tree cover, i.e., larger than what might be called a grove. http://www.Colorado.Edu/INSTAAR/TEAML/atlas/chapters/definitions.html#Forest and http://www.arcticatlas.org/glossary/index"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1693 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "A dense grove of trees and underbrush covering a large tract. Grove - A small wo..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "A dense grove of trees and underbrush covering a large tract. Grove - A small wood without underbrush. Wood - A dense grove of trees usually greater in extent than a grove and smaller than a forest. Thicket - A dense growth of shrubbery or small trees. http://www.thealmightyguru.com/Pointless/NatureDefinitions.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1696 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(American Legislative Exchange Council) “Forest” means a parcel of land in which..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(American Legislative Exchange Council) “Forest” means a parcel of land in which at least 80% of the parcel is producing or is capable of producing at least 20 cubic feet of merchantable timber per acre per year {or as defined by state statute}. https://www.alec.org/model-policy/the-right-to-practice-forestry-act/"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1697 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "An area managed for the production of timber and other forest products, or maint..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "An area managed for the production of timber and other forest products, or maintained under woody vegetation for indirect benefits as protection of a watershed, recreation, or wildlife habitat. When used as a proper noun, it refers to the Chattahoochee or Oconee National Forest (both if plural). http://www.safc.org/resources/glossary.htm#F"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1698 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Forest is defined as >30% crown cover and the tree height shall be >7 m. Seedlin..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1698_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Forest is defined as >30% crown cover and the tree height shall be >7 m. Seedlings under forest are also included in this class. Areas occupied by forest and woodlands with a vegetation pattern composed of native or exotic coniferous trees, and which can be used for the production of timber or other forest products. The forest trees are under normal climatic conditions higher than 5 m with a canopy closure of 30% at least. http://www.grida.no/baltic/related/balans_landcover_classification_methodology_ver2.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1698_criteria ex:minCanopyCover "30.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCoverSI "30.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "7.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "7.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_17 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Forest – defined as either a geographic area or delineated by the general compos..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Forest – defined as either a geographic area or delineated by the general composition of individuals; https://howlingpixel.com/wiki/Outline_of_forestry"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1701 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Land that is at least 10 percent stocked by forest trees of any size, or land fo..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1701_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Land that is at least 10 percent stocked by forest trees of any size, or land formerly having such tree cover, and is not currently developed for a nonforest use. The minimum area for classification as forest land is one acre. Roadside, stream-side, and shelterbelt strips of timber must have a crown width at least 120 feet wide to qualify as forest land. Unimproved roads and trails, streams and other bodies of water, or natural clearings in forested areas shall be classified as forest, if less than 120 feet in width or an acre in size. Grazed woodlands, reverting fields, and pastures that are not actively maintained are included if the above qualifications are satisfied. (Also see definitions of nonforest land, idle farmland and improved/maintained pasture.) www.socrates.lv-hrc.nevada.edu/fia/dab/core1-7/appendix7_12_00.doc"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1701_criteria ex:minHeight "120.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "36.576"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1702 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(UN-EP-GRID) Forest is defined as >30% crown cover and the tree height shall be ..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1702_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UNEP ;
    skos:note "(UN-EP-GRID) Forest is defined as >30% crown cover and the tree height shall be >7 m. Seedlings under forest are also included in this class. Areas occupied by forest and woodlands with a vegetation pattern composed of native or exotic coniferous trees, and which can be used for the production of timber or other forest products. The forest trees are under normal climatic conditions higher than 5 m with a canopy closure of 30% at least. www.grida.no/baltic/related/balans_landcover_classification_methodology_ver2.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1702_criteria ex:minCanopyCover "30.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCoverSI "30.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "7.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "7.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1786 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "An area planted to trees for fuel, or timber. http://www.echonet.org/Technotes/A..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "An area planted to trees for fuel, or timber. http://www.echonet.org/Technotes/AgroforestryPrinciples.html#definitions"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1790 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "The purpose of this paper is not to come up with final definitions, but to show ..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "The purpose of this paper is not to come up with final definitions, but to show the breadth of definitions in use. There is a test at the end of this document. Ultimately, all countries should come up with the same answers. In the meantime, we can ponder such things as are natural tree invasions, in the case of afforestation, and natural regeneration, in the case of reforestation, acknowledged or accepted? Do the terms reforestation and afforestation imply that there will be timber crops produced or just tree cover increased? . Do human-induced \"afforestation, deforestation, and reforestation\" cover all forestry activities that affect carbon emissions and sinks we need to track? What about natural deforestation, afforestation, and reforestation? Do we need other terms to describe other situations - such as the restocking of a recent clearcut area?"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1798 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Lao KP) GOL has already submitted a forest definition to UNFCCC (minimum 20% fo..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1798_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UNFCCC ;
    skos:note "(Lao KP) GOL has already submitted a forest definition to UNFCCC (minimum 20% forest cover, minimum area 0.5 ha, minimum tree height 5 m, and palm trees and bamboo considered as non-forest). http://www.dof.maf.gov.la/docs/Lao_FIP_Investment%20Plan%20Master_2nd%20draft-for-public%20review.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1798_criteria ex:minArea "0.5"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "0.5"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "5.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "5.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_18 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Definitions: forest, tree, forest summary, woodland, afforestation, deforestatio..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Definitions: forest, tree, forest summary, woodland, afforestation, deforestation, reforestation, other terms."@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1808 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(UN-DP) Refers to land under natural or planted stands of trees, whether product..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_United_Nations ;
    skos:note "(UN-DP) Refers to land under natural or planted stands of trees, whether productive or not, including land from which forest has been cleared but which will be reforested in the foreseeable future, and including areas occupied by roads, small cleared tracts and other small open areas within the forest that constitute an integral part of the forest. Includes land under coniferous and non-coniferous forest, land under mixed forest and other wooded land. http://www.undp.kz/infobase/glossary_sector.html?glos_id%5B%5D=42"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1815 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Trees outside forests (ToF). Trees and tree environments on lands not defined as..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1815_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UN-FAO ;
    skos:note "Trees outside forests (ToF). Trees and tree environments on lands not defined as forest or other wooded lands. Include: (a) groups of trees covering an area of less 0.5 ha, including lines and shelterbelts along infrastructure features and agricultural fields; (b) scattered trees in agricultural landscapes; (c) tree plantations mainly for other purposes than wood, such a fruit orchards and palm plantations; and trees in parks and gardens and around buildings. ToF are not assigned an area in the overall land use classification, but occurs inside Other wooded land and Other land. Although the definition of ToF is based on the trees, the concept includes also the site and other vegetation at the location. (FAO 2000b)"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1815_criteria ex:minArea "0.5"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "0.5"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1817 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "A piece of land that is thickly covered with trees is the general of definition ..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "A piece of land that is thickly covered with trees is the general of definition of a forest. Forest is also known as woods, weald or woodlands. http://hassam.hubpages.com/hub/Types-Of-Forests"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1821 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Before we can get into a discussion of Afforestation, Deforestation, and Affores..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Before we can get into a discussion of Afforestation, Deforestation, and Afforestation, we need to have an understanding of some basic terms and concepts. These include land - (the terrestrial bio-productive system that comprises soil vegetation, other biota, and the ecological and hydrological processes that operate within the system (Convention to Combat Desertification)), land use, land cover, tree, forest, natural forest, semi-natural forest, plantation, stocking and forestry. Here are some of the definitions we found:"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1822 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(World Bank) - An area of land of not less than 1.0 hectare with tree crown cove..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1822_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(World Bank) - An area of land of not less than 1.0 hectare with tree crown cover (or equivalent stocking level) of more than 10 per cent with trees with the potential to reach a minimum height of 2 meters at maturity in situ. A forest may consist of either closed forest formations where trees of various stories and undergrowth cover a high proportion of the ground or open forest. Young natural stands and all plantations which have yet to reach a crown density of 10 per cent or tree height of 2 meters are included under forest, as are areas normally forming part of the forest area which are temporarily unstocked as a result of human intervention such as harvesting or natural causes but which are expected to revert to forest. The definition includes forests dedicated to forest production, protection, multiple- uses or conservation, whether formally recognized or not. The definition excludes areas where other land uses not dependent on tree cover predominate, such as agriculture, grazing or settlements. In low forest-cover countries, the definition may be expanded to include areas covered by trees which fall below the 10 percent threshold for canopy density, but are considered forest under local conditions. http://www.iucn.org/themes/fcp/activities/publications/worldbankdraftdefinitions.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1822_criteria ex:minArea "1.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "1.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCover "10.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCoverSI "10.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "2.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "2.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1823 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(A/R - SSC A/R) - “Forest” is a minimum area of land of 0.05-1.0 hectares with t..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1823_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UNFCCC ;
    skos:note "(A/R - SSC A/R) - “Forest” is a minimum area of land of 0.05-1.0 hectares with tree crown cover (or equivalent stocking level) of more than 10-30 per cent with trees with the potential to reach a minimum height of 2-5 metres at maturity in situ. A forest may consist either of closed forest formations where trees of various storeys and undergrowth cover a high proportion of the ground or open forest. Young natural stands and all plantations which have yet to reach a crown density of 10-30 per cent or tree height of 2-5 metres are included under forest, as are areas normally forming part of the forest area which are temporarily unstocked as a result of human intervention such as harvesting or natural causes but which are expected to revert to forest. A Party not included in Annex I may host an A/R CDM project activity if it has selected and reported to the Executive Board through its designated national authority for the CDM the parameters it has chosen for the definition of “forest” to be used for the purposes of hosting A/R project activities under the CDM. http://cdm.unfccc.int/Reference/Guidclarif/glos_CDM_v04.pdf UNFCCC"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1823_criteria ex:minArea "1.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "1.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "5.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "5.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1851 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Stocking – The relative degree of occupancy land by trees, measured as basal are..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Stocking – The relative degree of occupancy land by trees, measured as basal area or the number of trees in a stand by size or age and spacing, compared to the basal area or number of trees required to fully utilize the growth potential of the land; that is, the stocking standard. http://216.239.39.100/search?q=cache:iFF2UlzBb4kC:socrates.lv-hrc.nevada.edu/fia/dab/core1-6/appendix7_12_00.doc+%22stand+density%22++definition+glossary&hl=en&ie=UTF-8"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1852 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "The amount of live trees on a given area in relation to what is considered the o..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USDA ;
    skos:note "The amount of live trees on a given area in relation to what is considered the optimum. [Source: USDA Forest Service General Technical Report WO-44. Forest Stand Density and Stocking: concepts, terms, and use of the stocking guides. 8 p.]"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1853 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "3.1 AFFORESTATION - Afforestation may be a legal term or a process of stocking l..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "3.1 AFFORESTATION - Afforestation may be a legal term or a process of stocking land. In the case of the latter, we group the definitions into those that imply a change in land cover only and those that imply a change in land cover and use. Four definitions specify \"crops\" implying that the trees will be later removed for commercial purposes. The time period for lands \"never having been forested\" vary from never to 30 to 100 years."@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_1858 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "The purpose of this paper is not to come up with final definitions, but to show ..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "The purpose of this paper is not to come up with final definitions, but to show the breadth of definitions in use. There is a test at the end of this document. Ultimately, all countries should come up with the same answers. In the meantime, we can ponder such things as are natural tree invasions, in the case of afforestation, and natural regeneration, in the case of reforestation, acknowledged or accepted? Do the terms reforestation and afforestation imply that there will be timber crops produced or just tree cover increased? . Do human-induced \"afforestation, deforestation, and reforestation\" cover all forestry activities that affect carbon emissions and sinks we need to track? What about natural deforestation, afforestation, and reforestation? Do we need other terms to describe other situations - such as the restocking of a recent clearcut area?"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_19 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "An area of woodland, esp. one owned by the sovereign and set apart as a hunting ..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "An area of woodland, esp. one owned by the sovereign and set apart as a hunting ground with its own laws and officers. http://dictionary.reverso.net/english-definition/forest%20reserve"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_203 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Ethiopia KP) The Ethiopian Designate National Authority for CDM, EPA, has commu..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_203_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_UNFCCC ;
    skos:note "(Ethiopia KP) The Ethiopian Designate National Authority for CDM, EPA, has communicated to the UNFCCC CDM Executive Board the definition of forest used for CDM projects in Ethiopia, which is as follows: •A minimum area of 0.05 hectares; •A minimum tree crown cover of 20 per cent; •A minimum average tree height above 2 m. http://cdm.unfccc.int/filestorage/L/4/Q/L4QB30W8C5RYZMT6UKOFX1PV9GNIHS/Annex%205%20Legal%20aspects.pdf?t=OXR8bHpqZnlvfDByMiF2MIecUaf9gjv8IjJT and http://database.v-c-s.org/sites/v-c-s.org/files/CCB_PROJ_DESC_1340_13OCT2015.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_203_criteria ex:minArea "0.05"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "0.05"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCover "205.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCoverSI "205.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "2.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "2.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_204 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Ethiopia KP) The Ethiopian DNA has determined that within Ethiopia, a forest is..." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_204_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Ethiopia KP) The Ethiopian DNA has determined that within Ethiopia, a forest is defined as land with trees that has:  A minimum area of 0.05 hectares;  A minimum tree crown cover of 20 per cent;  A minimum average tree height above 2 m. http://www.climate-standards.org/projects/files/ethiopia/Ethiopia_Humbo_CCBA_PDD_June_6.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_204_criteria ex:minArea "0.05"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "0.05"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "2.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "2.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_211 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(Gambia) all lands at leas10 % tree cover and 50% vegetative cover http://books...." ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_unk_unknown_211_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(Gambia) all lands at leas10 % tree cover and 50% vegetative cover http://books.google.com/books?id=dZh6-ekpSawC&pg=PA104&lpg=PA104&dq=Ethiopia+Forest+definition+define+%22forest+is%22+law+act&source=bl&ots=Wx8pSUKv7a&sig=I5dj10rusCk4zljYh9dOAZi5Vgw&hl=en&sa=X&ei=jC8-T9mtFqHz0gH49OCpBw&ved=0CCMQ6AEwAA#v=onepage&q=Ethiopia%20Forest%20definition%20define%20%22forest%20is%22%20law%20act&f=false"@en .

