    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Iowa ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Iowa 1999) \"Forest\" means stands of native or introduced trees containing at least two hundred trees per acre and located on privately owned land. However, a stand of fruit trees is not a forest. 1999. http://www.legis.state.ia.us/IACODE/1999SUPPLEMENT/161A/42.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_2000_1115 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-FED-DA-FS-INT) Land that is at least 10 percent stocked by forest trees of ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_2000_1115_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-FED-DA-FS-INT ;
    skos:note "(USA-FED-DA-FS-INT) Land that is at least 10 percent stocked by forest trees of any size (or 5 percent crown cover where stocking cannot be determined), or land formerly having such tree cover, and is not currently developed for a nonforest use. The minimum area for classification as forest land is one acre. Roadside, stream-side, and shelterbelt strips of timber must be at least 120 feet wide to qualify as forest land. Unimproved roads and trails or natural clearings in forested areas shall be classified as forest, if less than 120 feet in width or an acre in size. Streams and other bodies of water within forest will be considered forest land if they are less than 1 acre and 30-feet wide. Grazed woodlands, reverting fields, and pastures that are not actively maintained are included if the above qualifications are satisfied. (Also see definitions of nonforest land, idle farmland and improved/maintained pasture.) Note: In some instances, area previously stocked with woodland species that have had some type of treatment (e.g., chaining or other mechanical treatment) are classified as nonforest land. Interior West FIA annual manual 5/2000 – Terms not in National Manual"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_2000_1115_criteria ex:minArea "1.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "0.404686"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "120.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "36.576"^^xsd:float .

