ex:Def_def_usa_2001_1645 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Ohio 2001) \"Forest land\" means land for which the primary purpose is ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Ohio ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Ohio 2001) \"Forest land\" means land for which the primary purpose is the growing, managing and harvesting of a merchantable forest product of commercial species under accepted silvicultural systems through natural or artificial reforestation methods and for which there is an approved forest management plan. The forest land shall consist of a stand or stands of commercial species of forest trees which contain at least fifty square feet of basal area or at least three hundred stems per acre which shall be evenly distributed throughout the stand. http://www.ohiodnr.com/forestry/rules/pdf/3-10-01.pdf and http://auditor.cuyahoga.oh.us/auditor/appraisal/forestland.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_2001_1649 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Washington 2001) “Forest land\" means all land which is capable of sup..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Washington ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Washington 2001) “Forest land\" means all land which is capable of supporting a merchantable stand of timber and is not being actively used for a use which is incompatible with timber growing. Forest land does not include agricultural land that is or was enrolled in the conservation reserve enhancement program by contract if such agricultural land was historically used for agricultural purposes and the landowner intends to continue to use the land for agricultural purposes in the future. http://www.leg.wa.gov/sl/2001-02/5497-s_sl.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_2001_1730 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-FED-DA-FS 2001) Land that is at least 10 percent stocked by forest trees of..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_2001_1730_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-FED-DA-FS ;
    skos:note "(USA-FED-DA-FS 2001) Land that is at least 10 percent stocked by forest trees of any size, or land formerly having such tree cover, and is not currently developed for a nonforest use. The minimum area for classification as forest land is one acre. Roadside, stream-side, and shelterbelt strips of timber must have a crown width at least 120 feet wide to qualify as forest land. Unimproved roads and trails, streams and other bodies of water, or natural clearings in forested areas shall be classified as forest, if less than 120 feet in width or an acre in size. Grazed woodlands, reverting fields, and pastures that are not actively maintained are included if the above qualifications are satisfied. (Also see definitions of nonforest land, idle farmland and improved/maintained pasture.) Forest land is divided into timberland, reserved timberland and woodland. SRS FIA Southern Research Station Field Guide; Version 1.5; January 8, 2001, Updated March 23, 2001; Based upon FIA National Core Field Guide, Version 1.5, January, 2001 and FIA National Manual v1.4"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_2001_1730_criteria ex:minHeight "120.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "36.576"^^xsd:float .

