    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Washington 2001) “Forest land\" means all land which is capable of supporting a merchantable stand of timber and is not being actively used for a use which is incompatible with timber growing. Forest land does not include agricultural land that is or was enrolled in the conservation reserve enhancement program by contract if such agricultural land was historically used for agricultural purposes and the landowner intends to continue to use the land for agricultural purposes in the future. http://www.leg.wa.gov/sl/2001-02/5497-s_sl.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_2001_307 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-FED-EPA 2001) The term forest means a concentration of trees and related ve..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_2001_307_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-FED-EPA ;
    skos:note "(USA-FED-EPA 2001) The term forest means a concentration of trees and related vegetation in non-urban areas sparsely inhabited by and infrequently used by humans; characterized by natural terrain and drainage patterns. http://a257.g.akamaitech.net/7/257/2422/14mar20010800/edocket.access.gpo.gov/cfr_2002/julqtr/pdf/40cfr171.2.pdf"@en .

