    skos:note "(USA-STATE-California 2002) ‘‘Forest’’ means lands that support, or can support,’’ at least 10 percent tree canopy cover and that allow for management of one or more forest resources including timber, fish and wildlife, biodiversity, water quality, recreation, aesthetics and other public benefits. http://www.climatechange.ca.gov/publications/legislation/SB_812.PDF"@en .

