    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Georgia ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Georgia 2003) - 'Forest' means lands that support, or can support, at least 10 percent tree canopy cover and that allow for management of one or more forest resources including but not limited to timber, fish and wildlife, biodiversity, water quality, air quality, soil conservation, recreation, aesthetics, or other benefits. http://www.legis.state.ga.us/legis/2003_04/fulltext/sb356.htm"@en .

