ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1066 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-FED-DA-NRCS) Forestland ecological sites are separated from rangeland ecolo..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1066_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-FED-DA-NRCS ;
    skos:note "(USA-FED-DA-NRCS) Forestland ecological sites are separated from rangeland ecological sites based on the historic climax plant community that occupied the site before the arrival of European settlers. An Ecological Site Type of \"Forestland\" is assigned and described where this historic vegetation was dominated by a 25% overstory canopy of trees, as determined by crown perimeter-vertical projection. A tree is defined as a woody-stemmed plant that can grow to 4 meters in height at maturity. http://www.statlab.iastate.edu/soils/nssh/622.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1066_criteria ex:minHeight "4.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "4.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1067 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-FED-DI-BIA) (2) \"forest\" means an ecosystem of at least one acre in size, i..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-FED-DI-BIA ;
    skos:note "(USA-FED-DI-BIA) (2) \"forest\" means an ecosystem of at least one acre in size, including timberland and woodland, which - (A) is characterized by a more or less dense and extensive tree cover, (B) contains, or once contained, at least ten percent tree crown cover, and (C) is not developed or planned for exclusive nonforest use; http://codes.lp.findlaw.com/uscode/25/33/3103"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1070 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Alaska) In the Preliminary Classification for Alaskan Vegetation, veg..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1070_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Alaska ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Alaska) In the Preliminary Classification for Alaskan Vegetation, vegetation with at least a 10% crown cover by trees; i.e., single stemmed woody plants at least 5 m in height at maturity. http://www.Colorado.Edu/INSTAAR/TEAML/atlas/chapters/definitions.html#Forest"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1070_criteria ex:minCanopyCover "10.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCoverSI "10.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "5.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "5.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1079 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Arkansas) Forest - a large area of land primarily covered with trees ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Arkansas ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Arkansas) Forest - a large area of land primarily covered with trees as well as the other organisms, soil, water and air associated with them. Source: Principles of Silviculture, Frederick F. Baker Jim Grant jim.grant@mail.state.ar.us no official definitions in Arkansas law."@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1082 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Delaware) \"Forest\" means a biological community dominated by trees co..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Delaware ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Delaware) \"Forest\" means a biological community dominated by trees covering a contiguous area of land and includes any definition thereof developed by the Department of Agriculture Forest Service. A \"forest\" may be identified by the diversity of the tree species composing it or by its type. A \"forest type\" is a forest composed of associations of tree species that have similar ecological requirements."@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1085 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Hawaii-Kauai County) \"Forest\" means forestland occupied by forest tre..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Hawaii-Kauai_County ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Hawaii-Kauai County) \"Forest\" means forestland occupied by forest trees and associated wildlife species, and timber thereon. http://www.kauaigov.org/finance/RPA/tfde.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1086 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Illinois) Forest means a dense growth of trees and underbrush coverin..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Illinois ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Illinois) Forest means a dense growth of trees and underbrush covering a large tract of land, or a significant portion of a large tract of land. http://www.gurnee.il.us/municipal_code/pdf_chapters/chapter45.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1089 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Iowa) \"Forestland\" means stands of native or introduced forest planta..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Iowa ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Iowa) \"Forestland\" means stands of native or introduced forest plantation of at least three acres, including trees located on privately owned land. However, a stand of fruit trees or Christmas trees is not forestland. http://www.legis.state.ia.us/GA/77GA/Legislation/HF/02300/HF02351/Current.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1090 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Kentucky) \"Forest land\" means lands dominated by canopy forming trees..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Kentucky ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Kentucky) \"Forest land\" means lands dominated by canopy forming trees, or from a postmining land use standpoint, areas planted throughout with trees. http://www.surfacemining.ky.gov/Publications/NonCoalRegs/405KAR5_001_Definitions_091203.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1091 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Kentucky) \"Forest\" means a concentration of trees and related vegetat..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Kentucky ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Kentucky) \"Forest\" means a concentration of trees and related vegetation in nonurban areas characterized by natural terrain and drainage patterns. http://www.lrc.state.ky.us/kar/302/028/010.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1092 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Kentucky) Forest - an ecosystem characterized by a more or less dense..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Kentucky ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Kentucky) Forest - an ecosystem characterized by a more or less dense and extensive tree cover, often consisting of composition, structure, age class, and associated processes, and commonly including meadows, streams, fish, and wildlife. The State of Kentucky does not have the terms Forest, Forestland, or Tree officially defined in State Statute or Regulation. The Division of Forestry utilizes the Society of American Forester's definitions for these terms as listed in John A. Helms' The Dictionary of Forestry. Steve.Kull@mail.state.ky.us"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1093 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Maryland) “Forest” means:(i) a biological community dominated by tree..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1093_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Maryland ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Maryland) “Forest” means:(i) a biological community dominated by trees or other woody plants covering a land area of 1 acre or more, or (ii) an area that has been cut but not cleared of trees or other woody plants. http://www.dnr.state.md.us/download/reforest.pdf and http://www.sha.state.md.us/businesswithsha/bizStdsSpecs/oed/reforestationLawSum/reforestlaw.asp"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1093_criteria ex:minArea "1.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "0.404686"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1095 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Michigan) Upland Forest - Natural areas dominated by tree cover that ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1095_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Michigan ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Michigan) Upland Forest - Natural areas dominated by tree cover that is generally over 6 meters, or 20 feet, in height. The forest cover must occur in an upland setting with an understory of natural plant material or ground cover. If the understory has been altered to accommodate an agricultural or urban land use activity, such as a pasture or park, the area would be assigned to the appropriate land use type. Forest cover occurring in wetland environments would be assigned to the forested wetland group. http://www.rsgis.msu.edu/pdf/lclu/MIRIS_2_definitions.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1095_criteria ex:minHeight "6.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "6.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1097 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Montana) \"Forest\" means a tract of land with trees and underbrush. ht..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Montana ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Montana) \"Forest\" means a tract of land with trees and underbrush. http://www.deq.state.mt.us/dir/Legal/Chapters/CH50-08.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1100 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-North Dakota) \"Forest\" means an area of land normally supporting a gr..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-North_Dakota ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-North Dakota) \"Forest\" means an area of land normally supporting a growth of planted tree cover, woodlands, or windbreaks. http://www.state.nd.us/lr//cencode/T57C57.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1102 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Texas) \"Forest\" means a tract of land thick with trees and underbrush..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Texas ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Texas) \"Forest\" means a tract of land thick with trees and underbrush. http://www.capitol.state.tx.us/tlo/74R/billtext/SB00977H.HTM and . http://www.statutes.legis.state.tx.us/Docs/NR/htm/NR.152.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1103 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Texas) (3) \"Forest land\" means land on which the trees are potentiall..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Texas ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Texas) (3) \"Forest land\" means land on which the trees are potentially valuable for timber products, protection of watersheds, wildlife habitat, recreational uses, or for other purposes, but does not include land within the incorporated limits of a village, town, or city. http://capitol.tlc.state.tx.us/cgi-bin/cqcgi?CQ_SESSION_KEY=XMYTLGTJBKOU&CQ_QUERY_HANDLE=123988&CQ_CUR_DOCUMENT=14&CQ_TLO_DOC_TEXT=YES and http://www.statutes.legis.state.tx.us/Docs/NR/htm/NR.152.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1104 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Virginia) - \"Forest land\" means land on which forest trees are found...." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Virginia ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Virginia) - \"Forest land\" means land on which forest trees are found. Under Authority of Department of Forestry. § 10.1-1178. Definitions. \"Starr, James\" starrj@dof.state.va.us."@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1105 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Virginia) – For Gypsy Moth Spraying - Any spray block proposed for tr..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1105_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Virginia ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Virginia) – For Gypsy Moth Spraying - Any spray block proposed for treatment under this program must contain an area that meets the following definition of susceptible forest. A susceptible forest is a wooded area where the trees are 25 feet or more in height and 50% or more of the surface area, when viewed from above, is covered by the tree crowns of moderately or highly susceptible hardwood tree species. Any block that does not contain a forested area as defined will not be accepted for treatment under this program. Residential or other qualified properties with only scattered ornamental trees and shrubs or only a few large shade trees are not acceptable. However, residential or other qualified properties, even if they do not contain trees directly around them, are acceptable if they are less than 200 feet from a susceptible forest. http://gypsymoth.ento.vt.edu/vagm/VDACS_CostShare02.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1105_criteria ex:minHeight "25.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "7.62"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1106 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-West Virginia) (a) \"Timberland\" means any surface real property excep..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-West_Virginia ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-West Virginia) (a) \"Timberland\" means any surface real property except farm woodlots of not less than ten contiguous acres which is primarily in forest and which, in consideration of their size, has sufficient numbers of commercially valuable species of trees to constitute at least forty percent normal stocking of forest trees which are well distributed over the growing site. http://www.legis.state.wv.us/scripts/as_web.exe?Command=search&file=total2&request=forest+definition&MaxHits=10&NumLines=1"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1116 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-FED-DA-FS-NC) Land not currently developed for nonforest use and having a s..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1116_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-FED-DA-FS-NC ;
    skos:note "(USA-FED-DA-FS-NC) Land not currently developed for nonforest use and having a stocking value of at least 10.0 of all live forest trees of any size or formerly having a stocking value of at least 10.0. Unimproved roads and trails, streams or other bodies of water or clearings in forest areas will be classed as forest if less than 120 feet wide. The minimum area for classification of forest land is one acre and 120 feet in width. Roadside, streamside, and shelterbelt strips of timber must be at least 120 feet wide to qualify as forest land. Also see definitions for land area, commercial forest land, noncommercial forest land, productive-reserved forest land, stocking, unproductive forest land, and water. North Central FIA manual 9/99 – terms not in National Manual"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1116_criteria ex:minHeight "120.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "36.576"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1118 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Alaska) \"Forest land\" means land stocked or having been stocked with ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Alaska ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Alaska) \"Forest land\" means land stocked or having been stocked with forest trees of any size and not currently developed for nonforest use, regardless of whether presently available or accessible for commercial purposes, and includes any such land under state, municipal, or private ownership; http://touchngo.com/lglcntr/akstats/Statutes/Title41/Chapter17/Section950.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1120 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-California) \"Forestland\" means the land: (1) can support 10 percent o..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-California ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-California) \"Forestland\" means the land: (1) can support 10 percent or more tree cover with trees native to California, including native oaks, (generally but not always this is Site V (Dunning) and better timberland); and (2) is zoned to allow forest resource management. http://ceres.ca.gov/foreststeward/pdf/CFIPguide.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1121 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-California) ‘‘Forest’’ means lands that support, or can support,’’ at..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-California ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-California) ‘‘Forest’’ means lands that support, or can support,’’ at least 10 percent tree canopy cover and that allow for management of one or more forest resources including timber, fish and wildlife, biodiversity, water quality, recreation, aesthetics and other public benefits. http://www.energy.ca.gov/global_climate_change/documents/SB_812_20020909_chapter.pdf and http://www.arb.ca.gov/bluebook/bb03/HS/42801.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1122 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Colorado) \"Forest land\" means land of which at least ten percent is s..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Colorado ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Colorado) \"Forest land\" means land of which at least ten percent is stocked by forest trees of any size and includes land that formerly had such tree cover and that will be naturally or artificially regenerated. \"Forest land\" includes roadside, streamside, and shelterbelt strips of timber which have a crown width of at least one hundred twenty feet. \"Forest land\" includes unimproved roads and trails, streams, and clearings which are less than one hundred twenty feet wide. http://www.palmerfoundation.org/Legal_CO.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1123 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Florida) ``Forest\" means land stocked by trees of any size used in th..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Florida ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Florida) ``Forest\" means land stocked by trees of any size used in the production of forest products, or forest land that has been harvested and is not currently developed for nonforest use. http://www.myflorida.com/dor/tips/tip98a115.html and http://election.dos.state.fl.us/laws/98laws/ch_98-294.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1124 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Idaho) Forestland means privately owned land being held and used prim..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Idaho ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Idaho) Forestland means privately owned land being held and used primarily for the continuous purpose of growing and harvesting trees of a marketable species. http://www2.state.id.us/tax/propertytax/PTpdfs/revisedforestlanddesign.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1126 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Illinois) \"Forest\" means an area whose principal crop is trees. http:..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Illinois ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Illinois) \"Forest\" means an area whose principal crop is trees. http://www.legis.state.il.us/commission/jcar/admincode/017/017015370000010R.html and http://dnr.state.il.us/legal/1537.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1128 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Kentucky) Forestland - land at least 10 percent stocked by forest tre..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Kentucky ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Kentucky) Forestland - land at least 10 percent stocked by forest trees of any size, including land that formerly had such cover and that will be naturally or artificially regenerated. The State of Kentucky does not have the terms Forest, Forestland, or Tree officially defined in State Statute or Regulation. The Division of Forestry utilizes the Society of American Forester's definitions for these terms as listed in John A. Helms' The Dictionary of Forestry. Steve.Kull@mail.state.ky.us"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1129 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Maine) Forest land. \"Forest land\" means land used primarily for growt..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Maine ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Maine) Forest land. \"Forest land\" means land used primarily for growth of trees to be harvested for commercial use, but does not include ledge, marsh, open swamp, bog, water and similar areas, which are unsuitable for growing a forest product or for harvesting for commercial use even though these areas may exist within forest lands. Source: http://janus.state.me.us/legis/statutes/36/title36sec573.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1134 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Maryland-Easton) \"Forest\" means a biological community dominated by t..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1134_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Maryland-Easton ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Maryland-Easton) \"Forest\" means a biological community dominated by trees and other woody plants covering a land area of 10,000 square feet or greater. B. \"Forest\" includes: (1) Areas that have at least 100 live trees per acre with at least 50 percent of those trees having a 2-inch or greater diameter at 4.5 feet above the ground and larger; and (2) Areas that have been cut but not cleared. C. \"Forest\" does not include orchards. http://www.town-eastonmd.com/Planning/fco/fco_a002.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1134_criteria ex:minCanopyCover "50.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCoverSI "50.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "4.5"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "1.3716000000000002"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1136 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Massachusetts) Forest Land means land with at least 15% of the area o..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Massachusetts ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Massachusetts) Forest Land means land with at least 15% of the area occupied by the crowns of forest trees of any size that contains at least 7.5 square feet of basal area per acre; or that is a plantation containing at least 500 trees per acre; or land recently harvested that is in the process of regeneration. http://www.state.ma.us/dem/regs/304011c.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1137 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Michigan) \"Forest land\" means a tract of land or the timber rights in..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1137_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Michigan ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Michigan) \"Forest land\" means a tract of land or the timber rights in that land owned or occupied by a member, which land is at least 10% occupied by forest tree species with a growth potential of 50 cubic feet per acre per year and consists of 40 acres or more. Forest land includes land from which forest tree species have been removed and have not been restocked, but does not include land converted to uses other than the growing of forest tree species or land currently zoned for uses incompatible with forest practices. http://www.dnr.state.mi.us/www/law/law_book/statutes/code/part501.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1137_criteria ex:minArea "40.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "16.18744"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1140 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Minnesota) Forest land or forest. Forest land or forest, means land o..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Minnesota ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Minnesota) Forest land or forest. Forest land or forest, means land on which occurs a stand or potential stand of trees valuable for timber products, watershed or wildlife protection, recreational uses or other purposes, and shall include lands owned or controlled by the state of Minnesota. http://www.revisor.leg.state.mn.us/stats/89/51.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1142 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Montana) \"Forest land\" means contiguous land of 15 acres or more in o..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1142_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Montana ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Montana) \"Forest land\" means contiguous land of 15 acres or more in one ownership that is capable of producing timber that can be harvested in commercial quantity and is producing timber unless the trees have been removed by man through harvest, including clearcuts, or by natural disaster, including but not limited to fire. Forest land includes land: a) that has not been converted to another use; and b) on which the annual net wood production equals or exceeds 25 cubic feet an acre at the culmination of mean annual increment. http://data.opi.state.mt.us/bills/mca/15/44/15-44-102.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1142_criteria ex:minArea "15.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "6.07029"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1143 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Nevada) “Forest” or “forest land” means land on which occurs a stand ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Nevada ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Nevada) “Forest” or “forest land” means land on which occurs a stand or potential stand of trees valuable for timber products, watershed or wildlife protection, recreational uses or for other purposes. http://www.leg.state.nv.us/NRS/NRS-527.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1144 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Nevada) Land which is at least 10 percent occupied by forest trees of..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Nevada ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Nevada) Land which is at least 10 percent occupied by forest trees of any size or formerly having had such tree cover and not currently developed for non-forest use. Lands developed for non-forest use include areas for crops, improved pasture, residential, or administrative areas, improved roads of any width, and adjoining road clearing and power line clearing of any width. http://www.state.nv.us/cnr/ndwp/dict-1/WORD_F.htm Water Words Dictionary, http://www.nalms.org/glossary/lkword_f.htm Lake and Water Words Glossary, http://www.dcnr.nv.gov/nrp/y-tr1nrp.pdf and (36 CFR 219.3) http://www.safc.org/resources/glossary.htm#definitions"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1145 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-New York) Forest land means land primarily devoted to and suitable fo..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-New_York ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-New York) Forest land means land primarily devoted to and suitable for forest crop production under accepted evenaged or unevenaged forest management systems through natural regeneration or through forestation and sufficiently stocked with forest trees to produce a merchantable forest crop within 30 years of time of original certification. Forest land shall consist of a stand or stands of commercial species of forest trees which contain at least either 500 stems per acre or 60 square feet of basal area per acre which shall be evenly distributed over the area of the stand. The department may approve a smaller number of planted trees per acre if the resulting spacing between trees is appropriate for satisfactory growth for the species being planted. For natural seedlings to be part of a stand, they must be at least one foot in height, and planted trees must be at least in their third growing season on the site. http://www.dec.state.ny.us/website/regs/199.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1146 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-North Carolina-Counties) Forestland means land that is a part of a fo..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1146_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-North_Carolina-Counties ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-North Carolina-Counties) Forestland means land that is a part of a forest unit that is actively engaged in the commercial growing of trees under a sound management program. Forestland includes wasteland that is a part of the forest unit, but the wasteland included in the unit shall be appraised under the use value schedules as wasteland. The requirements for a forestland deferment are as follows: May consist of more than one tract of forestland, but at least one of the tracts must meet the qualification requirements and each tract must be under a sound management program. One tract must consist of at least 20 acres that are in actual production and are not included in a farm unit. If individually owned, the property must be the owner's residence or have been owned by the current owner or a relative of the current owner for four years preceding January 1 of the year in which the benefit is claimed. http://www.lincolncounty.org/County/Departments/Tax/LandUseValueQualifications.htm and http://www.co.anson.nc.us/assessor/defermnt.htm, http://www.co.chatham.nc.us/dept/tax/web/Listing.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1146_criteria ex:minArea "20.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "8.09372"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1149 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Oklahoma) \"Forests\" means forest land that is at least ten percent (1..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Oklahoma ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Oklahoma) \"Forests\" means forest land that is at least ten percent (10%) stocked by forest trees of any size, whether of commercial or noncommercial species, or formerly having such tree cover and not currently developed for nonforest use, including woodlands, woodlots, windbreaks and shelterbelts; Source: &sect;2-1301-102. http://oklegal.onenet.net/oklegal-cgi/isearch"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1150 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Oregon) “Forestland\" means forestland that is a parcel of land of mor..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1150_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Oregon ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Oregon) “Forestland\" means forestland that is a parcel of land of more than 10 acres that has been zoned in the comprehensive plan for exclusive farm use, forest use or farm and forest use and that is, as of the assessment date for which value for the forest homesite is being determined: (a) Land that has as its highest and best use the growing and harvesting of trees of a marketable species; (b) Land that has been designated as forestland under ORS 321.257 to 321.390 or 321.805 to 321.825; or (c) Land that has been classified under ORS 321.705 to 321.765. http://www.savinggraves-us.org/or/laws/308a.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1150_criteria ex:minArea "10.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "4.04686"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1151 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Oregon) Forestland” means land used for the growing and harvesting of..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Oregon ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Oregon) Forestland” means land used for the growing and harvesting of forest tree species, regardless of how the land is zoned, taxed or how any state statutes or local ordinances, rules or regulations are applied. http://159.121.125.11/forasst/Library/Pub/UrbanFP.pdf, http://www.cof.orst.edu/cof/teach/for442/odfdefin.htm and http://arcweb.sos.state.or.us/rules/OARS_600/OAR_629/629_600.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1152 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Rhode Island) -“Forestland” means any tract or contiguous tracts of l..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Rhode_Island ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Rhode Island) -“Forestland” means any tract or contiguous tracts of land, five (5) acres or more bearing a dense growth of trees, young regenerating forest, and having either the quality of selfperpetuation, or being dependent upon its development by the planting and replanting. http://www.state.ri.us/dem/pubs/regs/regs/forest/altgrant.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1153 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Rhode Island) The term \"forest land\" means any tract or contiguous tr..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Rhode_Island ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Rhode Island) The term \"forest land\" means any tract or contiguous tracts of land, ten (10) acres or larger bearing a dense growth of trees, including any underbrush thereon, and having either the quality of self perpetuation, or being dependent upon its development by the planting and replanting of trees in stands of closely growing timber, actively managed under a forest management plan approved by the director of environmental management. http://farm.fic.niu.edu/fic/laws/state/ri44271.html and http://www.state.ri.us/dem/pubs/regs/regs/agric/ffosimp.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1155 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Tennessee) \"Forest land\" means land constituting a forest unit engage..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Tennessee ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Tennessee) \"Forest land\" means land constituting a forest unit engaged in the growing of trees under a sound program of sustained yield management or any tract of fifteen (15) or more acres having tree growth in such quantity and quality and so managed as to constitute a forest; Source: http://farm.fic.niu.edu/fic/laws/state/tn675100.html and http://www.padctn.com/greenbelt_law.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1156 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Texas) \"Forest land\" means land on which the trees are potentially va..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Texas ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Texas) \"Forest land\" means land on which the trees are potentially valuable for timber products, protection of watersheds, wildlife habitat, recreational uses, or for other purposes, but does not include land within the incorporated limits of a village, town, or city. http://www.capitol.state.tx.us/statutes/nr/nr0015200.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1157 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Texas) Forest land” means land on which the trees are potentially val..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Texas ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Texas) Forest land” means land on which the trees are potentially valuable for timber products. http://www.tpwd.state.tx.us/texaswater/rivers/riddellcriminaltrespass.phtml"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1158 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Vermont) (9) \"Managed forest land\" means any land, exclusive of any h..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1158_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Vermont ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Vermont) (9) \"Managed forest land\" means any land, exclusive of any housesite, which is at least 25 acres in size and which is under active forest management for the purpose of growing and harvesting repeated forest crops in accordance with accepted forest management practices. There shall be a presumption that land is under active forest management if at least 50 percent of the land: (A) is certified to be a \"tree farm\" under the American Tree Farm System; (B) has qualified for a federal cost-sharing forest improvement program, and that program has actually been carried out within the past five years; (C) is certified by the county forester as conforming with accepted forest management practices; or (D) conforms with such criteria for managed forest land as are accepted by the board; Source: Vt. Stat. Ann. tit. 32, &sect;&sect; 3751 to 3775 http://farm.fic.niu.edu/fic/laws/state/vt323751.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1158_criteria ex:minArea "25.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "10.11715"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1164 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Minnesota) \"Forest land\" means land which is at least ten percent sto..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1164_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Minnesota ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Minnesota) \"Forest land\" means land which is at least ten percent stocked by trees of any size and capable of producing timber, or of exerting an influence on the climate or on the water regime; land from which the trees described above have been removed to less than ten percent stocking and which has not been developed for other use; and afforested areas. Source: Section: 88.01 continued... http://www.revisor.leg.state.mn.us:81/SEARCH/BASIS/mnstat/public/www/DDW?W%3DTEXT+PH+IS+%27forest+means%27+ORDER+BY+SORT_KEY/Ascend%26M%3D1%26K%3D88.01%26R%3DY%26U%3D20%26PCU%3D1"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1164_criteria ex:minHeight "26.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "26.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1165 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-New Hampshire) \"Forestland'' means all lands in this state, except th..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-New_Hampshire ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-New Hampshire) \"Forestland'' means all lands in this state, except those owned and managed by the United States of America, which by reason of their location and character of soil have the capacity to grow trees and the continuance of which under forest cover is of substantial importance to the public interest. http://www.gencourt.state.nh.us/rsa/html/XIX-A/227-G/227-G-2.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1166 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-North Dakota) \"Forest\" means an area of land normally supporting a gr..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-North_Dakota ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-North Dakota) \"Forest\" means an area of land normally supporting a growth of planted tree cover, woodlands, or windbreaks. http://www.legis.nd.gov/cencode/t57c57.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1167 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Pennsylvania) Forests are defined as ecosystems dominated by trees, b..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Pennsylvania ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Pennsylvania) Forests are defined as ecosystems dominated by trees, but with other components such as shrubs, herbs, mammals, birds, insects, microscopic creatures, soil, air, water, and the interactive processes that bind them together. http://www.dcnr.state.pa.us/forestry/sfrmp/overview.htm#sustainability"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1181 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Airports) \"Tree\" means a tree or other object of natural growth. http..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Airports ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Airports) \"Tree\" means a tree or other object of natural growth. http://www.townofbourne.com/Town%20Offices/Bylaws/Chapter5.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1182 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Arkansas) Tree - a woody plant at least 8 feet tall with one well-def..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1182_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Arkansas ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Arkansas) Tree - a woody plant at least 8 feet tall with one well-defined stem and a more or less definitely formed crown. Other definitions say a woody plant from 12 - 15 feet tall with one well-defined stem and a more or less definitely formed crown. Several sources. The SAF definition is one stem and 15 feet. Other definitions ranged from 8 - 15 feet. Jim Grant jim.grant@mail.state.ar.us no official definitions in Arkansas law."@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1182_criteria ex:minHeight "8.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "2.4384"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1183 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Illinois) \"Tree\" or \"trees\" means any tree, standing or felled, livin..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Illinois ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Illinois) \"Tree\" or \"trees\" means any tree, standing or felled, living or dead, and includes both those trees included within the definition of \"timber\" in Section 2 of the \"Timber Buyers Licensing Act\" and Christmas trees. The term does not apply to trees or parts of trees that have been cut into firewood http://www.legis.state.il.us/ilcs/ch225/ch225act740.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1184 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Indiana-Bloomington) A woody, perennial plant with one main stem or t..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Indiana-Bloomington ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Indiana-Bloomington) A woody, perennial plant with one main stem or trunk which develops many branches. http://www.city.bloomington.in.us/code/TITLE12/Chapter_12_24_TREES/12_24_010_Definitions_.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1185 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Kentucky) A woody perennial plant, typically large and with a well-de..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1185_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Kentucky ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Kentucky) A woody perennial plant, typically large and with a well-defined stem or stems carrying a more or less definite crown (usually more that 12 feet in height at maturity). The State of Kentucky does not have the terms Forest, Forestland, or Tree officially defined in State Statute or Regulation. The Division of Forestry utilizes the Society of American Forester's definitions for these terms as listed in John A. Helms' The Dictionary of Forestry. Steve.Kull@mail.state.ky.us"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1185_criteria ex:minHeight "12.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "3.6576000000000004"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1186 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Maryland-Easton) \"Tree\" means a large, branched woody plant having on..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1186_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Maryland-Easton ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Maryland-Easton) \"Tree\" means a large, branched woody plant having one or several self-supporting stems or trunks that reach a height of at least 20 feet at maturity. http://www.town-eastonmd.com/Planning/fco/fco_a002.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1186_criteria ex:minHeight "20.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "6.096"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1189 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Virginia) - \"Forest trees\" means only those trees which are a part of..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Virginia ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Virginia) - \"Forest trees\" means only those trees which are a part of and constitute a stand of potential, immature, or mature commercial timber trees. The term \"forest trees\" includes shade trees of any species around houses, along highways and within cities and towns if the trees constitute an insect or disease menace to nearby timber trees or timber stands. Under Authority of Department of Forestry. § 10.1-1178. Definitions. \"Starr, James\" starrj@dof.state.va.us"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1229 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Stand Density - A measure of the amount of timber growing on a site expressed in..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Stand Density - A measure of the amount of timber growing on a site expressed in number of trees, basal area, or volume. http://216.239.39.100/search?q=cache:3wFtRKEEkxEC:www.gfc.state.ga.us/Publications/Educational/glossary.pdf+%22stand+density%22++definition+glossary&hl=en&ie=UTF-8#10"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1230 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Stocking - The number of trees in a forest stand. Often, stocking level is compa..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Stocking - The number of trees in a forest stand. Often, stocking level is compared to the desirable number of trees for best growth and management, such as partially stocked, well stocked or over-stocked. http://216.239.39.100/search?q=cache:3wFtRKEEkxEC:www.gfc.state.ga.us/Publications/Educational/glossary.pdf+%22stand+density%22++definition+glossary&hl=en&ie=UTF-8#10"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1258 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-FED-DA-FS) The restocking of an area with forest trees, by either natural o..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-FED-DA-FS ;
    skos:note "(USA-FED-DA-FS) The restocking of an area with forest trees, by either natural or artificial means, such as planting (http://www.fs.fed.us/land/emterms.html)."@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1259 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Oregon) \"Natural reforestation\" means restocking a site with self-gro..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Oregon ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Oregon) \"Natural reforestation\" means restocking a site with self-grown trees resulting from self-seeding or vegetative means. http://www.cof.orst.edu/cof/teach/for442/odfdefin.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1263 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Illinois) \"Reforestation\" means the natural or artificial restocking ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Illinois ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Illinois) \"Reforestation\" means the natural or artificial restocking with trees on forest land. http://dnr.state.il.us/legal/1537.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1266 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "The renewal of a tree crop by either natural or artificial means. The term is al..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "The renewal of a tree crop by either natural or artificial means. The term is also used to refer to the young crop itself (http://www.fs.fed.us/land/emterms.html)."@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1305 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-FED-DI-BIA) (2) \"forest\" means an ecosystem of at least one acre in size, i..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-FED-DI-BIA ;
    skos:note "(USA-FED-DI-BIA) (2) \"forest\" means an ecosystem of at least one acre in size, including timberland and woodland, which - (A) is characterized by a more or less dense and extensive tree cover, (B) contains, or once contained, at least ten percent tree crown cover, and (C) is not developed or planned for exclusive nonforest use; http://codes.lp.findlaw.com/uscode/25/33/3103"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1307 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-North Dakota) \"Forest\" means an area of land normally supporting a gr..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-North_Dakota ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-North Dakota) \"Forest\" means an area of land normally supporting a growth of planted tree cover, woodlands, or windbreaks. http://www.state.nd.us/lr//cencode/T57C57.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1308 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Oregon) \"Forestland\" means any woodland, brushland, timberland, grazi..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Oregon ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Oregon) \"Forestland\" means any woodland, brushland, timberland, grazing land or clearing that, during any time of the year, contains enough forest growth, slashing or vegetation to constitute, in the judgment of the forester, a fire hazard, regardless of how the land is zoned or taxed. As used in this subsection, \"clearing\" means any grassland, improved area, lake, meadow, mechanically or manually cleared area, road, rocky area, stream or other similar forestland opening that is surrounded by or contiguous to forestland and that has been included in areas classified as forestland under ORS 526.305 to 526.370 http://www.leg.state.or.us/ors/477.html and http://www.paperadvantage.org/ORS/526.html#forestland."@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1315 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Oklahoma) \"Forests\" means forest land that is at least ten percent (1..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Oklahoma ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Oklahoma) \"Forests\" means forest land that is at least ten percent (10%) stocked by forest trees of any size, whether of commercial or noncommercial species, or formerly having such tree cover and not currently developed for nonforest use, including woodlands, woodlots, windbreaks and shelterbelts; Source: &sect;2-1301-102. http://oklegal.onenet.net/oklegal-cgi/isearch"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1316 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-North Dakota) \"Forest\" means an area of land normally supporting a gr..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-North_Dakota ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-North Dakota) \"Forest\" means an area of land normally supporting a growth of planted tree cover, woodlands, or windbreaks. http://www.legis.nd.gov/cencode/t57c57.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1317 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Oregon) \"Forestland\" means any woodland, brushland, timberland, grazi..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Oregon ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Oregon) \"Forestland\" means any woodland, brushland, timberland, grazing land or clearing, which, during any time of the year, contains enough forest growth, slashing or vegetation to constitute, in the opinion of the forester, a fire hazard, regardless of how the land is zoned or taxed. Source: 526.005 Definitions http://www.leg.state.or.us/ors/526.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1327 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-FED-DI-GS) -Woodland, which is defined as \"forest land,\" includes deciduous..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1327_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-FED-DI-GS ;
    skos:note "(USA-FED-DI-GS) -Woodland, which is defined as \"forest land,\" includes deciduous, evergreen, and mixed forest land, and orchards. The woodland data layer identifies deforestation or reforestation resulting from urbanization or conservation. The woodland is compiled using criteria based on tint and spectral reflectance. The minimum mapping unit for woodland is 10 acres. The classification scheme adopted for woodland is a modification of the Anderson Level II classification system. All woodland areas are collected as polygons, compiled into one separate coverage, and assigned category 44. http://mcmcweb.er.usgs.gov/phil/gis.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1327_criteria ex:minArea "10.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "4.04686"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1377 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Maryland) “Forest” means:(i) a biological community dominated by tree..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1377_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Maryland ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Maryland) “Forest” means:(i) a biological community dominated by trees or other woody plants covering a land area of 1 acre or more, or (ii) an area that has been cut but not cleared of trees or other woody plants. http://www.dnr.state.md.us/download/reforest.pdf and http://www.sha.state.md.us/businesswithsha/bizStdsSpecs/oed/reforestationLawSum/reforestlaw.asp"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1377_criteria ex:minArea "1.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "0.404686"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1378 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-New York) Forest land means land primarily devoted to and suitable fo..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-New_York ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-New York) Forest land means land primarily devoted to and suitable for forest crop production under accepted evenaged or unevenaged forest management systems through natural regeneration or through forestation and sufficiently stocked with forest trees to produce a merchantable forest crop within 30 years of time of original certification. Forest land shall consist of a stand or stands of commercial species of forest trees which contain at least either 500 stems per acre or 60 square feet of basal area per acre which shall be evenly distributed over the area of the stand. The department may approve a smaller number of planted trees per acre if the resulting spacing between trees is appropriate for satisfactory growth for the species being planted. For natural seedlings to be part of a stand, they must be at least one foot in height, and planted trees must be at least in their third growing season on the site. http://www.dec.state.ny.us/website/regs/199.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1380 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-FED-DI-GS) -Woodland, which is defined as \"forest land,\" includes deciduous..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1380_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-FED-DI-GS ;
    skos:note "(USA-FED-DI-GS) -Woodland, which is defined as \"forest land,\" includes deciduous, evergreen, and mixed forest land, and orchards. The woodland data layer identifies deforestation or reforestation resulting from urbanization or conservation. The woodland is compiled using criteria based on tint and spectral reflectance. The minimum mapping unit for woodland is 10 acres. The classification scheme adopted for woodland is a modification of the Anderson Level II classification system. All woodland areas are collected as polygons, compiled into one separate coverage, and assigned category 44. http://mcmcweb.er.usgs.gov/phil/gis.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1380_criteria ex:minArea "10.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "4.04686"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1414 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Oregon) \"Natural reforestation\" means restocking a site with self-gro..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Oregon ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Oregon) \"Natural reforestation\" means restocking a site with self-grown trees resulting from self-seeding or vegetative means. http://www.cof.orst.edu/cof/teach/for442/odfdefin.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1416 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Illinois) \"Reforestation\" means the natural or artificial restocking ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Illinois ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Illinois) \"Reforestation\" means the natural or artificial restocking with trees on forest land. http://dnr.state.il.us/legal/1537.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1431 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Massachusetts) Forest Land means land with at least 15% of the area o..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Massachusetts ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Massachusetts) Forest Land means land with at least 15% of the area occupied by the crowns of forest trees of any size that contains at least 7.5 square feet of basal area per acre; or that is a plantation containing at least 500 trees per acre; or land recently harvested that is in the process of regeneration. http://www.state.ma.us/dem/regs/304011c.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1432 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-New York) Forest land means land primarily devoted to and suitable fo..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-New_York ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-New York) Forest land means land primarily devoted to and suitable for forest crop production under accepted evenaged or unevenaged forest management systems through natural regeneration or through forestation and sufficiently stocked with forest trees to produce a merchantable forest crop within 30 years of time of original certification. Forest land shall consist of a stand or stands of commercial species of forest trees which contain at least either 500 stems per acre or 60 square feet of basal area per acre which shall be evenly distributed over the area of the stand. The department may approve a smaller number of planted trees per acre if the resulting spacing between trees is appropriate for satisfactory growth for the species being planted. For natural seedlings to be part of a stand, they must be at least one foot in height, and planted trees must be at least in their third growing season on the site. http://www.dec.state.ny.us/website/regs/199.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1494 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA) A stand of trees where trees are no more than 60 feet apart. Based upon ex..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1494_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(USA) A stand of trees where trees are no more than 60 feet apart. Based upon excavated roots of some mature trees and determined that a forest could not be a forest if the trees were more than about 20 meters apart. This definition assumed that the trees were mature. This was a definition for the USA. Source: \"J. Foster\" <borealis@mail.wellsgray.net from an article in Journal of Forestry."@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1494_criteria ex:minHeight "20.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "20.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_152 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA) Pursuant to 16 USCS § 460hhh (1), [Title 16. Conservation; Chapter 1. Nati..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(USA) Pursuant to 16 USCS § 460hhh (1), [Title 16. Conservation; Chapter 1. National Parks, Military Parks, Monuments, and Seashores; Spring Mountains National Recreation Area] the term National Forest lands means “lands included in the National Forest System (as defined in section 11(a) of the Forest and Rangeland Renewable Resources Planning Act. https://definitions.uslegal.com/n/national-forest-lands/"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1522 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Kentucky) Forest - an ecosystem characterized by a more or less dense..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Kentucky ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Kentucky) Forest - an ecosystem characterized by a more or less dense and extensive tree cover, often consisting of composition, structure, age class, and associated processes, and commonly including meadows, streams, fish, and wildlife. The State of Kentucky does not have the terms Forest, Forestland, or Tree officially defined in State Statute or Regulation. The Division of Forestry utilizes the Society of American Forester's definitions for these terms as listed in John A. Helms' The Dictionary of Forestry. Steve.Kull@mail.state.ky.us"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1524 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Virginia) - \"Forest land\" means land on which forest trees are found...." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Virginia ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Virginia) - \"Forest land\" means land on which forest trees are found. Under Authority of Department of Forestry. § 10.1-1178. Definitions. \"Starr, James\" starrj@dof.state.va.us."@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1527 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Illinois) \"Forestry\" means land used or managed for the long-term pro..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Illinois ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Illinois) \"Forestry\" means land used or managed for the long-term production of wood, wood fiber, or wood-derived products. Allowable support facilities include water impoundments, access and fire control lanes, erosion control structures such as grassed waterways, downdrains, terraces and sediment ponds, and other incidental facilities related to sound multiple use management of the forest resource. http://dnr.state.il.us/legal/62-1701.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1528 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Kentucky) Forestland - land at least 10 percent stocked by forest tre..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Kentucky ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Kentucky) Forestland - land at least 10 percent stocked by forest trees of any size, including land that formerly had such cover and that will be naturally or artificially regenerated. The State of Kentucky does not have the terms Forest, Forestland, or Tree officially defined in State Statute or Regulation. The Division of Forestry utilizes the Society of American Forester's definitions for these terms as listed in John A. Helms' The Dictionary of Forestry. Steve.Kull@mail.state.ky.us"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_153 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-FED-DA-FS) (National Forest) - A unit formally established and permanently ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-FED-DA-FS ;
    skos:note "(USA-FED-DA-FS) (National Forest) - A unit formally established and permanently set aside and reserved for National Forest purposes. http://www.fs.fed.us/database/lar/lardefn.htm and http://www.fs.fed.us/land/staff/lar/definitions_of_terms.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1532 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Montana) \"Forest land\" means land that has enough timber, standing or..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Montana ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Montana) \"Forest land\" means land that has enough timber, standing or down, slash, or brush to constitute in the judgment of the department a fire menace to life or property. Grassland and agricultural areas are included when those areas are intermingled with or contiguous to and no further than one-half mile from areas of forest land. http://www.dnrc.state.mt.us/forestry/classifi.htm and http://www.discoveringmontana.com/racicot/eo/21-22-23Background.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1533 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Pennsylvania) Forests are defined as ecosystems dominated by trees, b..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Pennsylvania ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Pennsylvania) Forests are defined as ecosystems dominated by trees, but with other components such as shrubs, herbs, mammals, birds, insects, microscopic creatures, soil, air, water, and the interactive processes that bind them together. http://www.dcnr.state.pa.us/forestry/sfrmp/overview.htm#sustainability"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1539 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Kentucky) A woody perennial plant, typically large and with a well-de..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1539_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Kentucky ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Kentucky) A woody perennial plant, typically large and with a well-defined stem or stems carrying a more or less definite crown (usually more that 12 feet in height at maturity). The State of Kentucky does not have the terms Forest, Forestland, or Tree officially defined in State Statute or Regulation. The Division of Forestry utilizes the Society of American Forester's definitions for these terms as listed in John A. Helms' The Dictionary of Forestry. Steve.Kull@mail.state.ky.us"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1539_criteria ex:minHeight "12.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "3.6576000000000004"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1541 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Virginia) - \"Forest trees\" means only those trees which are a part of..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Virginia ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Virginia) - \"Forest trees\" means only those trees which are a part of and constitute a stand of potential, immature, or mature commercial timber trees. The term \"forest trees\" includes shade trees of any species around houses, along highways and within cities and towns if the trees constitute an insect or disease menace to nearby timber trees or timber stands. Under Authority of Department of Forestry. § 10.1-1178. Definitions. \"Starr, James\" starrj@dof.state.va.us"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_16 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "We found over 1,700 definitions. Thresholds for tree cover vary from 0% to 80%. ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_16_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "We found over 1,700 definitions. Thresholds for tree cover vary from 0% to 80%. [Note: John Dwyer has done some work which shows that average forest cover in urban USA is about 33% (From: Smith_Brad/wo@fs.fed.us)]. A crosswalk of various forest classification systems may be found at http://www.ncasi-nerc.org/projects/evmp/vcst/. We can group forest definitions according to their source - those found in general dictionaries and glossaries, definitions from the International Community, National definitions, and state, provincial or local definitions. We can further group these into 4 categories - those that are declared or administrative units, those that mean a land cover, those that mean a land use and a miscellaneous category."@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1603 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA) A stand of trees where trees are no more than 60 feet apart. Based upon ex..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1603_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(USA) A stand of trees where trees are no more than 60 feet apart. Based upon excavated roots of some mature trees and determined that a forest could not be a forest if the trees were more than about 20 meters apart. This definition assumed that the trees were mature. This was a definition for the USA. Source: \"J. Foster\" <borealis@mail.wellsgray.net from an article in Journal of Forestry."@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1603_criteria ex:minHeight "20.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "20.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1629 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Idaho) Forest land means any land which has enough forest growth, sta..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Idaho ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Idaho) Forest land means any land which has enough forest growth, standing or down, to constitute, in the judgement of the Department, an insect or disease infestation breeding ground of a nature to constitute a menace, injurious and dangerous to the forest resources in the district or zone of infestation. www.fs.fed.us/im/directives/field/r1/fsm/3400/3400_zero_code.rtf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1632 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Iowa) \"Forestland\" means stands of native or introduced forest planta..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Iowa ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Iowa) \"Forestland\" means stands of native or introduced forest plantation of at least three acres, including trees located on privately owned land. However, a stand of fruit trees or Christmas trees is not forestland. http://www.legis.state.ia.us/GA/77GA/Legislation/HF/02300/HF02351/Current.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1633 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Kentucky) \"Forest land\" means lands dominated by canopy forming trees..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Kentucky ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Kentucky) \"Forest land\" means lands dominated by canopy forming trees, or from a postmining land use standpoint, areas planted throughout with trees. http://www.surfacemining.ky.gov/Publications/NonCoalRegs/405KAR5_001_Definitions_091203.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1642 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Minnesota) Forest land or forest. Forest land or forest, means land o..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Minnesota ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Minnesota) Forest land or forest. Forest land or forest, means land on which occurs a stand or potential stand of trees valuable for timber products, watershed or wildlife protection, recreational uses or other purposes, and shall include lands owned or controlled by the state of Minnesota. http://www.revisor.leg.state.mn.us/stats/89/51.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1643 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Nevada) “Forest” or “forest land” means land on which occurs a stand ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Nevada ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Nevada) “Forest” or “forest land” means land on which occurs a stand or potential stand of trees valuable for timber products, watershed or wildlife protection, recreational uses or for other purposes. http://www.leg.state.nv.us/NRS/NRS-527.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1644 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-New York) Forest land means land primarily devoted to and suitable fo..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-New_York ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-New York) Forest land means land primarily devoted to and suitable for forest crop production under accepted evenaged or unevenaged forest management systems through natural regeneration or through forestation and sufficiently stocked with forest trees to produce a merchantable forest crop within 30 years of time of original certification. Forest land shall consist of a stand or stands of commercial species of forest trees which contain at least either 500 stems per acre or 60 square feet of basal area per acre which shall be evenly distributed over the area of the stand. The department may approve a smaller number of planted trees per acre if the resulting spacing between trees is appropriate for satisfactory growth for the species being planted. For natural seedlings to be part of a stand, they must be at least one foot in height, and planted trees must be at least in their third growing season on the site. http://www.dec.state.ny.us/website/regs/199.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1646 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Rhode Island) I.2.c. Forestland - In this report, forestland is defin..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Rhode_Island ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Rhode Island) I.2.c. Forestland - In this report, forestland is defined in the same way as \"commercial forestland,\" and is based on the standard definition developed by the USDA Forest Service. According to the Forest Service, \"Commercial forestland is land that is capable of producing more than 20 cubic feet of biomass per acre per year.\" http://rredc.nrel.gov/biomass/doe/rbep/ri_wd_waste/one.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1647 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Rhode Island) The term \"forest land\" means any tract or contiguous tr..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Rhode_Island ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Rhode Island) The term \"forest land\" means any tract or contiguous tracts of land, ten (10) acres or larger bearing a dense growth of trees, including any underbrush thereon, and having either the quality of self perpetuation, or being dependent upon its development by the planting and replanting of trees in stands of closely growing timber, actively managed under a forest management plan approved by the director of environmental management. http://farm.fic.niu.edu/fic/laws/state/ri44271.html and http://www.state.ri.us/dem/pubs/regs/regs/agric/ffosimp.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1652 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Montana) \"Forest land\" means land that has enough timber, standing or..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Montana ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Montana) \"Forest land\" means land that has enough timber, standing or down, slash, or brush to constitute in the judgment of the department a fire menace to life or property. Grassland and agricultural areas are included when those areas are intermingled with or contiguous to and no further than one-half mile from areas of forest land. http://www.dnrc.state.mt.us/forestry/classifi.htm and http://www.discoveringmontana.com/racicot/eo/21-22-23Background.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1655 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Illinois) \"Tree\" or \"trees\" means any tree, standing or felled, livin..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Illinois ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Illinois) \"Tree\" or \"trees\" means any tree, standing or felled, living or dead, and includes both those trees included within the definition of \"timber\" in Section 2 of the \"Timber Buyers Licensing Act\" and Christmas trees. The term does not apply to trees or parts of trees that have been cut into firewood http://www.legis.state.il.us/ilcs/ch225/ch225act740.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1656 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Virginia) - \"Forest trees\" means only those trees which are a part of..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Virginia ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Virginia) - \"Forest trees\" means only those trees which are a part of and constitute a stand of potential, immature, or mature commercial timber trees. The term \"forest trees\" includes shade trees of any species around houses, along highways and within cities and towns if the trees constitute an insect or disease menace to nearby timber trees or timber stands. Under Authority of Department of Forestry. § 10.1-1178. Definitions. \"Starr, James\" starrj@dof.state.va.us"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1668 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Stand Density - A measure of the amount of timber growing on a site expressed in..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Stand Density - A measure of the amount of timber growing on a site expressed in number of trees, basal area, or volume. http://216.239.39.100/search?q=cache:3wFtRKEEkxEC:www.gfc.state.ga.us/Publications/Educational/glossary.pdf+%22stand+density%22++definition+glossary&hl=en&ie=UTF-8#10"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1669 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Stocking - The number of trees in a forest stand. Often, stocking level is compa..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Stocking - The number of trees in a forest stand. Often, stocking level is compared to the desirable number of trees for best growth and management, such as partially stocked, well stocked or over-stocked. http://216.239.39.100/search?q=cache:3wFtRKEEkxEC:www.gfc.state.ga.us/Publications/Educational/glossary.pdf+%22stand+density%22++definition+glossary&hl=en&ie=UTF-8#10"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1699 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Forest land is characterized by a predominance of tree cover and is further divi..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Forest land is characterized by a predominance of tree cover and is further divided by the U.S. Census into timberland and non-timberland. By definition, the former must be capable of producing 20 cubic feet of industrial wood per acre per year and remain legally open to timber production. http://www.gcrio.org/CONSEQUENCES/spring95/Land.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_16_criteria ex:minCanopyCover "0.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCoverSI "0.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1714 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-FED-Census Bureau1995) Forest land is characterized by a predominance of tr..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-FED-Census_Bureau1995 ;
    skos:note "(USA-FED-Census Bureau1995) Forest land is characterized by a predominance of tree cover and is further divided by the U.S. Census into timberland and non-timberland. By definition, the former must be capable of producing 20 cubic feet of industrial wood per acre per year and remain legally open to timber production. http://www.gcrio.org/CONSEQUENCES/spring95/Land.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1732 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-FED-DI-BIA) (2) \"forest\" means an ecosystem of at least one acre in size, i..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-FED-DI-BIA ;
    skos:note "(USA-FED-DI-BIA) (2) \"forest\" means an ecosystem of at least one acre in size, including timberland and woodland, which - (A) is characterized by a more or less dense and extensive tree cover, (B) contains, or once contained, at least ten percent tree crown cover, and (C) is not developed or planned for exclusive nonforest use; http://codes.lp.findlaw.com/uscode/25/33/3103"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1737 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Hawaii-Kauai County) \"Forest\" means forestland occupied by forest tre..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Hawaii-Kauai_County ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Hawaii-Kauai County) \"Forest\" means forestland occupied by forest trees and associated wildlife species, and timber thereon. http://www.kauaigov.org/finance/RPA/tfde.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1738 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Montana) \"Forest\" means forest land and the timber on the land. http:..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Montana ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Montana) \"Forest\" means forest land and the timber on the land. http://data.opi.state.mt.us/bills/mca/15/44/15-44-102.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1739 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Oregon) \"Forestland\" means any woodland, brushland, timberland, grazi..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Oregon ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Oregon) \"Forestland\" means any woodland, brushland, timberland, grazing land or clearing that, during any time of the year, contains enough forest growth, slashing or vegetation to constitute, in the judgment of the forester, a fire hazard, regardless of how the land is zoned or taxed. As used in this subsection, \"clearing\" means any grassland, improved area, lake, meadow, mechanically or manually cleared area, road, rocky area, stream or other similar forestland opening that is surrounded by or contiguous to forestland and that has been included in areas classified as forestland under ORS 526.305 to 526.370 http://www.leg.state.or.us/ors/477.html and http://www.paperadvantage.org/ORS/526.html#forestland."@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1740 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Texas) (3) \"Forest land\" means land on which the trees are potentiall..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Texas ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Texas) (3) \"Forest land\" means land on which the trees are potentially valuable for timber products, protection of watersheds, wildlife habitat, recreational uses, or for other purposes, but does not include land within the incorporated limits of a village, town, or city. http://capitol.tlc.state.tx.us/cgi-bin/cqcgi?CQ_SESSION_KEY=XMYTLGTJBKOU&CQ_QUERY_HANDLE=123988&CQ_CUR_DOCUMENT=14&CQ_TLO_DOC_TEXT=YES and http://www.statutes.legis.state.tx.us/Docs/NR/htm/NR.152.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1741 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-West Virginia) (a) \"Timberland\" means any surface real property excep..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-West_Virginia ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-West Virginia) (a) \"Timberland\" means any surface real property except farm woodlots of not less than ten contiguous acres which is primarily in forest and which, in consideration of their size, has sufficient numbers of commercially valuable species of trees to constitute at least forty percent normal stocking of forest trees which are well distributed over the growing site. http://www.legis.state.wv.us/scripts/as_web.exe?Command=search&file=total2&request=forest+definition&MaxHits=10&NumLines=1"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1744 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-FED-DA-FS-NC) Land not currently developed for nonforest use and having a s..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1744_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-FED-DA-FS-NC ;
    skos:note "(USA-FED-DA-FS-NC) Land not currently developed for nonforest use and having a stocking value of at least 10.0 of all live forest trees of any size or formerly having a stocking value of at least 10.0. Unimproved roads and trails, streams or other bodies of water or clearings in forest areas will be classed as forest if less than 120 feet wide. The minimum area for classification of forest land is one acre and 120 feet in width. Roadside, streamside, and shelterbelt strips of timber must be at least 120 feet wide to qualify as forest land. Also see definitions for land area, commercial forest land, noncommercial forest land, productive-reserved forest land, stocking, unproductive forest land, and water. North Central FIA manual 9/99 – terms not in National Manual"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1744_criteria ex:minHeight "120.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "36.576"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1746 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-FED-DA–R8) An area managed for the production of timber and other forest pr..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-FED-DA_R8 ;
    skos:note "(USA-FED-DA–R8) An area managed for the production of timber and other forest products, or maintained under woody vegetation for indirect benefits as protection of a watershed, recreation, or wildlife habitat. http://www.r8web.com/gwj/lrmp/plandocs/glossary.html#definitions"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1747 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-California) \"Forestland\" means the land: (1) can support 10 percent o..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-California ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-California) \"Forestland\" means the land: (1) can support 10 percent or more tree cover with trees native to California, including native oaks, (generally but not always this is Site V (Dunning) and better timberland); and (2) is zoned to allow forest resource management. http://ceres.ca.gov/foreststeward/pdf/CFIPguide.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1748 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-California) ‘‘Forest’’ means lands that support, or can support,’’ at..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-California ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-California) ‘‘Forest’’ means lands that support, or can support,’’ at least 10 percent tree canopy cover and that allow for management of one or more forest resources including timber, fish and wildlife, biodiversity, water quality, recreation, aesthetics and other public benefits. http://www.energy.ca.gov/global_climate_change/documents/SB_812_20020909_chapter.pdf and http://www.arb.ca.gov/bluebook/bb03/HS/42801.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1749 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-California-Mendocino County) “Forest Land” means lands, which are sui..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-California-Mendocino_County ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-California-Mendocino County) “Forest Land” means lands, which are suited for and are appropriately retained for the growing, harvesting and production of timber and forest and timber-related products. The classification includes lands eligible to be zoned Timberland Production (TPZ), including lands which have the present or future potential for timber production, intermixed smaller parcels and other contiguous lands, the inclusion of which is necessary for the protection and efficient management of forest resource lands. http://mendolafco.org/lafcopp/lafcopandp2002.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1750 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Colorado) \"Forest land\" means land of which at least ten percent is s..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Colorado ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Colorado) \"Forest land\" means land of which at least ten percent is stocked by forest trees of any size and includes land that formerly had such tree cover and that will be naturally or artificially regenerated. \"Forest land\" includes roadside, streamside, and shelterbelt strips of timber which have a crown width of at least one hundred twenty feet. \"Forest land\" includes unimproved roads and trails, streams, and clearings which are less than one hundred twenty feet wide. http://www.palmerfoundation.org/Legal_CO.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1754 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Michigan) \"Forest land\" means a tract of land or the timber rights in..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1754_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Michigan ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Michigan) \"Forest land\" means a tract of land or the timber rights in that land owned or occupied by a member, which land is at least 10% occupied by forest tree species with a growth potential of 50 cubic feet per acre per year and consists of 40 acres or more. Forest land includes land from which forest tree species have been removed and have not been restocked, but does not include land converted to uses other than the growing of forest tree species or land currently zoned for uses incompatible with forest practices. http://www.dnr.state.mi.us/www/law/law_book/statutes/code/part501.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1754_criteria ex:minArea "40.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "16.18744"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1755 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Michigan) \"Forest land\" means timbered land, potential timber-produci..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Michigan ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Michigan) \"Forest land\" means timbered land, potential timber-producing land, cutover or burned timber land or grass lands not including lands devoted to agriculture. http://www.michigan.gov/dnr/0,1607,7-153-10367_11851-24039--,00.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1757 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Minnesota) Forest land or forest. Forest land or forest, means land o..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Minnesota ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Minnesota) Forest land or forest. Forest land or forest, means land on which occurs a stand or potential stand of trees valuable for timber products, watershed or wildlife protection, recreational uses or other purposes, and shall include lands owned or controlled by the state of Minnesota. http://www.revisor.leg.state.mn.us/stats/89/51.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1759 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Montana) \"Forest land\" means contiguous land of 15 acres or more in o..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1759_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Montana ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Montana) \"Forest land\" means contiguous land of 15 acres or more in one ownership that is capable of producing timber that can be harvested in commercial quantity and is producing timber unless the trees have been removed by man through harvest, including clearcuts, or by natural disaster, including but not limited to fire. Forest land includes land: a) that has not been converted to another use; and b) on which the annual net wood production equals or exceeds 25 cubic feet an acre at the culmination of mean annual increment. http://data.opi.state.mt.us/bills/mca/15/44/15-44-102.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1759_criteria ex:minArea "15.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "6.07029"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1760 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Nevada) “Forest” or “forest land” means land on which occurs a stand ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Nevada ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Nevada) “Forest” or “forest land” means land on which occurs a stand or potential stand of trees valuable for timber products, watershed or wildlife protection, recreational uses or for other purposes. http://www.leg.state.nv.us/NRS/NRS-527.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1761 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Oregon) \"Forestland\" means land zoned in a county comprehensive plan ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Oregon ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Oregon) \"Forestland\" means land zoned in a county comprehensive plan for forest or farm use that is capable of producing commercial hardwood or softwood timber, regardless of the vegetation currently on the land. http://arcweb.sos.state.or.us/rules/OARS_600/OAR_629/629_022.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1762 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Rhode Island) The term \"forest land\" means any tract or contiguous tr..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Rhode_Island ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Rhode Island) The term \"forest land\" means any tract or contiguous tracts of land, ten (10) acres or larger bearing a dense growth of trees, including any underbrush thereon, and having either the quality of self perpetuation, or being dependent upon its development by the planting and replanting of trees in stands of closely growing timber, actively managed under a forest management plan approved by the director of environmental management. http://farm.fic.niu.edu/fic/laws/state/ri44271.html and http://www.state.ri.us/dem/pubs/regs/regs/agric/ffosimp.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1764 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Texas) \"Forest land\" means land on which the trees are potentially va..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Texas ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Texas) \"Forest land\" means land on which the trees are potentially valuable for timber products, protection of watersheds, wildlife habitat, recreational uses, or for other purposes, but does not include land within the incorporated limits of a village, town, or city. http://www.capitol.state.tx.us/statutes/nr/nr0015200.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1765 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Texas) Forest land” means land on which the trees are potentially val..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Texas ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Texas) Forest land” means land on which the trees are potentially valuable for timber products. http://www.tpwd.state.tx.us/texaswater/rivers/riddellcriminaltrespass.phtml"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1768 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Washington) (3) \"Timber land\" means any parcel of land that is five o..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Washington ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Washington) (3) \"Timber land\" means any parcel of land that is five or more acres or multiple parcels of land that are contiguous and total five or more acres which is or are devoted primarily to the growth and harvest of forest crops for commercial purposes. Wash. Rev. Code secs. 84.34.010 to - .922 http://farm.fic.niu.edu/fic/laws/state/wa8434.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1769 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Washington-San Juan County) - Timber Land means any parcel of land th..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Washington-San_Juan_County ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Washington-San Juan County) - Timber Land means any parcel of land that is five or more acres or multiple parcels of land that are contiguous and total five or more acres which is or are devoted primarily to the growth and harvest of forest crops for commercial purposes. http://www.co.san-juan.wa.us/assessor/current.aspx"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1770 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Washington-San Juan County) Land designated as ‘forest land’ means an..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Washington-San_Juan_County ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Washington-San Juan County) Land designated as ‘forest land’ means any parcel of land twenty or more acres in size or multiple parcels of land that are contiguous and total twenty acres or more in size that is primarily used for the growth and harvesting of timber. Forest land refers only to the land. http://www.co.san-juan.wa.us/assessor/default.asp?page=dfl"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1771 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Washington-Stevens County) Forestland means all land in contiguous ow..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Washington-Stevens_County ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Washington-Stevens County) Forestland means all land in contiguous ownership of 20 or more acres; which is primarily devoted to and used for growing and harvesting timber. http://www.co.stevens.wa.us/assessor/Current%20Land%20Use/PDF%20docs/continuance.PDF"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1773 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-California) \"Forest land\" means timberland defined pursuant to subdiv..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-California ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-California) \"Forest land\" means timberland defined pursuant to subdivision (g), and other lands that have been withdrawn from timber production, such as units of the state park system, national parks, and wilderness areas. http://caselaw.lp.findlaw.com/cacodes/prc/4789-4789.7.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1775 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Minnesota) \"Forest land\" means land which is at least ten percent sto..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1775_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Minnesota ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Minnesota) \"Forest land\" means land which is at least ten percent stocked by trees of any size and capable of producing timber, or of exerting an influence on the climate or on the water regime; land from which the trees described above have been removed to less than ten percent stocking and which has not been developed for other use; and afforested areas. Source: Section: 88.01 continued... http://www.revisor.leg.state.mn.us:81/SEARCH/BASIS/mnstat/public/www/DDW?W%3DTEXT+PH+IS+%27forest+means%27+ORDER+BY+SORT_KEY/Ascend%26M%3D1%26K%3D88.01%26R%3DY%26U%3D20%26PCU%3D1"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1775_criteria ex:minHeight "26.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "26.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1776 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Montana) \"Forest land\" means land that has enough timber, standing or..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Montana ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Montana) \"Forest land\" means land that has enough timber, standing or down, slash, or brush to constitute in the judgment of the department a fire menace to life or property. Grassland and agricultural areas are included when those areas are intermingled with or contiguous to and no further than one-half mile from areas of forest land. http://www.dnrc.state.mt.us/forestry/classifi.htm and http://www.discoveringmontana.com/racicot/eo/21-22-23Background.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1777 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Oregon) \"Forestland\" means any woodland, brushland, timberland, grazi..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Oregon ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Oregon) \"Forestland\" means any woodland, brushland, timberland, grazing land or clearing, which, during any time of the year, contains enough forest growth, slashing or vegetation to constitute, in the opinion of the forester, a fire hazard, regardless of how the land is zoned or taxed. Source: 526.005 Definitions http://www.leg.state.or.us/ors/526.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1780 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Illinois) \"Tree\" or \"trees\" means any tree, standing or felled, livin..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Illinois ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Illinois) \"Tree\" or \"trees\" means any tree, standing or felled, living or dead, and includes both those trees included within the definition of \"timber\" in Section 2 of the \"Timber Buyers Licensing Act\" and Christmas trees. The term does not apply to trees or parts of trees that have been cut into firewood http://www.legis.state.il.us/ilcs/ch225/ch225act740.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1781 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Virginia) - \"Forest trees\" means only those trees which are a part of..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Virginia ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Virginia) - \"Forest trees\" means only those trees which are a part of and constitute a stand of potential, immature, or mature commercial timber trees. The term \"forest trees\" includes shade trees of any species around houses, along highways and within cities and towns if the trees constitute an insect or disease menace to nearby timber trees or timber stands. Under Authority of Department of Forestry. § 10.1-1178. Definitions. \"Starr, James\" starrj@dof.state.va.us"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1787 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Stand Density - A measure of the amount of timber growing on a site expressed in..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Stand Density - A measure of the amount of timber growing on a site expressed in number of trees, basal area, or volume. http://216.239.39.100/search?q=cache:3wFtRKEEkxEC:www.gfc.state.ga.us/Publications/Educational/glossary.pdf+%22stand+density%22++definition+glossary&hl=en&ie=UTF-8#10"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1803 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Nevada) Land which is at least 10 percent occupied by forest trees of..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Nevada ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Nevada) Land which is at least 10 percent occupied by forest trees of any size or formerly having had such tree cover and not currently developed for non-forest use. Lands developed for non-forest use include areas for crops, improved pasture, residential, or administrative areas, improved roads of any width, and adjoining road clearing and power line clearing of any width. http://www.state.nv.us/cnr/ndwp/dict-1/WORD_F.htm Water Words Dictionary, http://www.nalms.org/glossary/lkword_f.htm Lake and Water Words Glossary, http://www.dcnr.nv.gov/nrp/y-tr1nrp.pdf and (36 CFR 219.3) http://www.safc.org/resources/glossary.htm#definitions"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1838 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-West Virginia) (a) \"Timberland\" means any surface real property excep..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-West_Virginia ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-West Virginia) (a) \"Timberland\" means any surface real property except farm woodlots of not less than ten contiguous acres which is primarily in forest and which, in consideration of their size, has sufficient numbers of commercially valuable species of trees to constitute at least forty percent normal stocking of forest trees which are well distributed over the growing site. http://www.legis.state.wv.us/scripts/as_web.exe?Command=search&file=total2&request=forest+definition&MaxHits=10&NumLines=1"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1840 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-FED-DA-FS-NC) Land not currently developed for nonforest use and having a s..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1840_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-FED-DA-FS-NC ;
    skos:note "(USA-FED-DA-FS-NC) Land not currently developed for nonforest use and having a stocking value of at least 10.0 of all live forest trees of any size or formerly having a stocking value of at least 10.0. Unimproved roads and trails, streams or other bodies of water or clearings in forest areas will be classed as forest if less than 120 feet wide. The minimum area for classification of forest land is one acre and 120 feet in width. Roadside, streamside, and shelterbelt strips of timber must be at least 120 feet wide to qualify as forest land. Also see definitions for land area, commercial forest land, noncommercial forest land, productive-reserved forest land, stocking, unproductive forest land, and water. North Central FIA manual 9/99 – terms not in National Manual"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1840_criteria ex:minHeight "120.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "36.576"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1843 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Minnesota) \"Forest land\" means land which is at least ten percent sto..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1843_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Minnesota ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Minnesota) \"Forest land\" means land which is at least ten percent stocked by trees of any size and capable of producing timber, or of exerting an influence on the climate or on the water regime; land from which the trees described above have been removed to less than ten percent stocking and which has not been developed for other use; and afforested areas. Source: Section: 88.01 continued... http://www.revisor.leg.state.mn.us:81/SEARCH/BASIS/mnstat/public/www/DDW?W%3DTEXT+PH+IS+%27forest+means%27+ORDER+BY+SORT_KEY/Ascend%26M%3D1%26K%3D88.01%26R%3DY%26U%3D20%26PCU%3D1"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1843_criteria ex:minHeight "26.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "26.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1850 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Stocking - The number of trees in a forest stand. Often, stocking level is compa..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Stocking - The number of trees in a forest stand. Often, stocking level is compared to the desirable number of trees for best growth and management, such as partially stocked, well stocked or over-stocked. http://216.239.39.100/search?q=cache:3wFtRKEEkxEC:www.gfc.state.ga.us/Publications/Educational/glossary.pdf+%22stand+density%22++definition+glossary&hl=en&ie=UTF-8#10"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1854 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-FED-DA-FS) The restocking of an area with forest trees, by either natural o..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-FED-DA-FS ;
    skos:note "(USA-FED-DA-FS) The restocking of an area with forest trees, by either natural or artificial means, such as planting (http://www.fs.fed.us/land/emterms.html)."@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1855 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Oregon) \"Natural reforestation\" means restocking a site with self-gro..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Oregon ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Oregon) \"Natural reforestation\" means restocking a site with self-grown trees resulting from self-seeding or vegetative means. http://www.cof.orst.edu/cof/teach/for442/odfdefin.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_1857 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Illinois) \"Reforestation\" means the natural or artificial restocking ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Illinois ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Illinois) \"Reforestation\" means the natural or artificial restocking with trees on forest land. http://dnr.state.il.us/legal/1537.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_302 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA) A stand of trees where trees are no more than 60 feet apart. Based upon ex..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_302_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(USA) A stand of trees where trees are no more than 60 feet apart. Based upon excavated roots of some mature trees and determined that a forest could not be a forest if the trees were more than about 20 meters apart. This definition assumed that the trees were mature. This was a definition for the USA. Source: \"J. Foster\" <borealis@mail.wellsgray.net from an article in Journal of Forestry."@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_302_criteria ex:minHeight "20.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "20.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_303 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-FED-Census Bureau1995) Forest land is characterized by a predominance of tr..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-FED-Census_Bureau1995 ;
    skos:note "(USA-FED-Census Bureau1995) Forest land is characterized by a predominance of tree cover and is further divided by the U.S. Census into timberland and non-timberland. By definition, the former must be capable of producing 20 cubic feet of industrial wood per acre per year and remain legally open to timber production. http://www.gcrio.org/CONSEQUENCES/spring95/Land.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_405 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-FED-DA-NRCS) Forestland ecological sites are separated from rangeland ecolo..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_405_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-FED-DA-NRCS ;
    skos:note "(USA-FED-DA-NRCS) Forestland ecological sites are separated from rangeland ecological sites based on the historic climax plant community that occupied the site before the arrival of European settlers. An Ecological Site Type of \"Forestland\" is assigned and described where this historic vegetation was dominated by a 25% overstory canopy of trees, as determined by crown perimeter-vertical projection. A tree is defined as a woody-stemmed plant that can grow to 4 meters in height at maturity. http://www.statlab.iastate.edu/soils/nssh/622.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_405_criteria ex:minHeight "4.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "4.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_406 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-FED-DI-BIA) (2) \"forest\" means an ecosystem of at least one acre in size, i..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-FED-DI-BIA ;
    skos:note "(USA-FED-DI-BIA) (2) \"forest\" means an ecosystem of at least one acre in size, including timberland and woodland, which - (A) is characterized by a more or less dense and extensive tree cover, (B) contains, or once contained, at least ten percent tree crown cover, and (C) is not developed or planned for exclusive nonforest use; http://codes.lp.findlaw.com/uscode/25/33/3103"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_416 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Alaska) In the Preliminary Classification for Alaskan Vegetation, veg..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_416_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Alaska ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Alaska) In the Preliminary Classification for Alaskan Vegetation, vegetation with at least a 10% crown cover by trees; i.e., single stemmed woody plants at least 5 m in height at maturity. http://www.Colorado.Edu/INSTAAR/TEAML/atlas/chapters/definitions.html#Forest"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_416_criteria ex:minCanopyCover "10.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCoverSI "10.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "5.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "5.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_429 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Arkansas) Forest - a large area of land primarily covered with trees ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Arkansas ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Arkansas) Forest - a large area of land primarily covered with trees as well as the other organisms, soil, water and air associated with them. Source: Principles of Silviculture, Frederick F. Baker Jim Grant jim.grant@mail.state.ar.us no official definitions in Arkansas law."@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_432 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Delaware) \"Forest\" means a biological community dominated by trees co..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Ecological" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Delaware ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Delaware) \"Forest\" means a biological community dominated by trees covering a contiguous area of land and includes any definition thereof developed by the Department of Agriculture Forest Service. A \"forest\" may be identified by the diversity of the tree species composing it or by its type. A \"forest type\" is a forest composed of associations of tree species that have similar ecological requirements."@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_435 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Hawaii-Kauai County) \"Forest\" means forestland occupied by forest tre..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Hawaii-Kauai_County ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Hawaii-Kauai County) \"Forest\" means forestland occupied by forest trees and associated wildlife species, and timber thereon. http://www.kauaigov.org/finance/RPA/tfde.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_436 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Idaho) Forest land means any land which has enough forest growth, sta..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Idaho ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Idaho) Forest land means any land which has enough forest growth, standing or down, to constitute, in the judgement of the Department, an insect or disease infestation breeding ground of a nature to constitute a menace, injurious and dangerous to the forest resources in the district or zone of infestation. www.fs.fed.us/im/directives/field/r1/fsm/3400/3400_zero_code.rtf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_437 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Illinois) Forest means a dense growth of trees and underbrush coverin..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Illinois ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Illinois) Forest means a dense growth of trees and underbrush covering a large tract of land, or a significant portion of a large tract of land. http://www.gurnee.il.us/municipal_code/pdf_chapters/chapter45.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_440 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Iowa) \"Forestland\" means stands of native or introduced forest planta..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Iowa ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Iowa) \"Forestland\" means stands of native or introduced forest plantation of at least three acres, including trees located on privately owned land. However, a stand of fruit trees or Christmas trees is not forestland. http://www.legis.state.ia.us/GA/77GA/Legislation/HF/02300/HF02351/Current.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_441 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Kentucky) \"Forest land\" means lands dominated by canopy forming trees..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Kentucky ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Kentucky) \"Forest land\" means lands dominated by canopy forming trees, or from a postmining land use standpoint, areas planted throughout with trees. http://www.surfacemining.ky.gov/Publications/NonCoalRegs/405KAR5_001_Definitions_091203.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_442 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Kentucky) \"Forest\" means a concentration of trees and related vegetat..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Kentucky ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Kentucky) \"Forest\" means a concentration of trees and related vegetation in nonurban areas characterized by natural terrain and drainage patterns. http://www.lrc.state.ky.us/kar/302/028/010.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_443 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Kentucky) Forest - an ecosystem characterized by a more or less dense..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Kentucky ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Kentucky) Forest - an ecosystem characterized by a more or less dense and extensive tree cover, often consisting of composition, structure, age class, and associated processes, and commonly including meadows, streams, fish, and wildlife. The State of Kentucky does not have the terms Forest, Forestland, or Tree officially defined in State Statute or Regulation. The Division of Forestry utilizes the Society of American Forester's definitions for these terms as listed in John A. Helms' The Dictionary of Forestry. Steve.Kull@mail.state.ky.us"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_444 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Maryland) “Forest” means:(i) a biological community dominated by tree..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_444_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Maryland ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Maryland) “Forest” means:(i) a biological community dominated by trees or other woody plants covering a land area of 1 acre or more, or (ii) an area that has been cut but not cleared of trees or other woody plants. http://www.dnr.state.md.us/download/reforest.pdf and http://www.sha.state.md.us/businesswithsha/bizStdsSpecs/oed/reforestationLawSum/reforestlaw.asp"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_444_criteria ex:minArea "1.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "0.404686"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_446 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Michigan) Upland Forest - Natural areas dominated by tree cover that ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_446_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Michigan ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Michigan) Upland Forest - Natural areas dominated by tree cover that is generally over 6 meters, or 20 feet, in height. The forest cover must occur in an upland setting with an understory of natural plant material or ground cover. If the understory has been altered to accommodate an agricultural or urban land use activity, such as a pasture or park, the area would be assigned to the appropriate land use type. Forest cover occurring in wetland environments would be assigned to the forested wetland group. http://www.rsgis.msu.edu/pdf/lclu/MIRIS_2_definitions.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_446_criteria ex:minHeight "6.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "6.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_449 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Montana) \"Forest\" means a tract of land with trees and underbrush. ht..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Montana ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Montana) \"Forest\" means a tract of land with trees and underbrush. http://www.deq.state.mt.us/dir/Legal/Chapters/CH50-08.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_45 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Forest land is characterized by a predominance of tree cover and is further divi..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Forest land is characterized by a predominance of tree cover and is further divided by the U.S. Census into timberland and non-timberland. By definition, the former must be capable of producing 20 cubic feet of industrial wood per acre per year and remain legally open to timber production. http://www.gcrio.org/CONSEQUENCES/spring95/Land.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_450 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Montana) \"Forest\" means forest land and the timber on the land. http:..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Montana ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Montana) \"Forest\" means forest land and the timber on the land. http://data.opi.state.mt.us/bills/mca/15/44/15-44-102.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_451 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-New Jersey) “Forest” means and includes any forest, bushland, grassla..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-New_Jersey ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-New Jersey) “Forest” means and includes any forest, bushland, grassland, salt marsh, and any combination thereof. http://www.state.nj.us/dep/parksandforests/fire/docs/conservation_and_development.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_454 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-North Dakota) \"Forest\" means an area of land normally supporting a gr..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-North_Dakota ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-North Dakota) \"Forest\" means an area of land normally supporting a growth of planted tree cover, woodlands, or windbreaks. http://www.state.nd.us/lr//cencode/T57C57.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_455 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Oregon) \"Forestland\" means any woodland, brushland, timberland, grazi..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Oregon ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Oregon) \"Forestland\" means any woodland, brushland, timberland, grazing land or clearing that, during any time of the year, contains enough forest growth, slashing or vegetation to constitute, in the judgment of the forester, a fire hazard, regardless of how the land is zoned or taxed. As used in this subsection, \"clearing\" means any grassland, improved area, lake, meadow, mechanically or manually cleared area, road, rocky area, stream or other similar forestland opening that is surrounded by or contiguous to forestland and that has been included in areas classified as forestland under ORS 526.305 to 526.370 http://www.leg.state.or.us/ors/477.html and http://www.paperadvantage.org/ORS/526.html#forestland."@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_457 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Texas) \"Forest\" means a tract of land thick with trees and underbrush..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Texas ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Texas) \"Forest\" means a tract of land thick with trees and underbrush. http://www.capitol.state.tx.us/tlo/74R/billtext/SB00977H.HTM and . http://www.statutes.legis.state.tx.us/Docs/NR/htm/NR.152.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_458 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Texas) (3) \"Forest land\" means land on which the trees are potentiall..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Texas ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Texas) (3) \"Forest land\" means land on which the trees are potentially valuable for timber products, protection of watersheds, wildlife habitat, recreational uses, or for other purposes, but does not include land within the incorporated limits of a village, town, or city. http://capitol.tlc.state.tx.us/cgi-bin/cqcgi?CQ_SESSION_KEY=XMYTLGTJBKOU&CQ_QUERY_HANDLE=123988&CQ_CUR_DOCUMENT=14&CQ_TLO_DOC_TEXT=YES and http://www.statutes.legis.state.tx.us/Docs/NR/htm/NR.152.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_459 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Virginia) - \"Forest land\" means land on which forest trees are found...." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Virginia ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Virginia) - \"Forest land\" means land on which forest trees are found. Under Authority of Department of Forestry. § 10.1-1178. Definitions. \"Starr, James\" starrj@dof.state.va.us."@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_460 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Virginia) – For Gypsy Moth Spraying - Any spray block proposed for tr..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_460_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Virginia ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Virginia) – For Gypsy Moth Spraying - Any spray block proposed for treatment under this program must contain an area that meets the following definition of susceptible forest. A susceptible forest is a wooded area where the trees are 25 feet or more in height and 50% or more of the surface area, when viewed from above, is covered by the tree crowns of moderately or highly susceptible hardwood tree species. Any block that does not contain a forested area as defined will not be accepted for treatment under this program. Residential or other qualified properties with only scattered ornamental trees and shrubs or only a few large shade trees are not acceptable. However, residential or other qualified properties, even if they do not contain trees directly around them, are acceptable if they are less than 200 feet from a susceptible forest. http://gypsymoth.ento.vt.edu/vagm/VDACS_CostShare02.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_460_criteria ex:minHeight "25.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "7.62"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_461 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-West Virginia) (a) \"Timberland\" means any surface real property excep..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-West_Virginia ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-West Virginia) (a) \"Timberland\" means any surface real property except farm woodlots of not less than ten contiguous acres which is primarily in forest and which, in consideration of their size, has sufficient numbers of commercially valuable species of trees to constitute at least forty percent normal stocking of forest trees which are well distributed over the growing site. http://www.legis.state.wv.us/scripts/as_web.exe?Command=search&file=total2&request=forest+definition&MaxHits=10&NumLines=1"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_463 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Wyoming) Forest -We informally use the FS definition of >10% crown co..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_463_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Wyoming ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Wyoming) Forest -We informally use the FS definition of >10% crown cover to define forest vs nonforest. To the best of my knowledge there is no definition either in statute or in any written documents. \"Howard Pickerd\" HPICKE@state.wy.us"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_463_criteria ex:minCanopyCover "10.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCoverSI "10.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_474 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-FED-DA-FS-NC) Land not currently developed for nonforest use and having a s..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_474_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-FED-DA-FS-NC ;
    skos:note "(USA-FED-DA-FS-NC) Land not currently developed for nonforest use and having a stocking value of at least 10.0 of all live forest trees of any size or formerly having a stocking value of at least 10.0. Unimproved roads and trails, streams or other bodies of water or clearings in forest areas will be classed as forest if less than 120 feet wide. The minimum area for classification of forest land is one acre and 120 feet in width. Roadside, streamside, and shelterbelt strips of timber must be at least 120 feet wide to qualify as forest land. Also see definitions for land area, commercial forest land, noncommercial forest land, productive-reserved forest land, stocking, unproductive forest land, and water. North Central FIA manual 9/99 – terms not in National Manual"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_474_criteria ex:minHeight "120.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "36.576"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_476 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-FED-DA–R8) An area managed for the production of timber and other forest pr..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-FED-DA_R8 ;
    skos:note "(USA-FED-DA–R8) An area managed for the production of timber and other forest products, or maintained under woody vegetation for indirect benefits as protection of a watershed, recreation, or wildlife habitat. http://www.r8web.com/gwj/lrmp/plandocs/glossary.html#definitions"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_477 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Alaska) \"Forest land\" means land stocked or having been stocked with ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Alaska ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Alaska) \"Forest land\" means land stocked or having been stocked with forest trees of any size and not currently developed for nonforest use, regardless of whether presently available or accessible for commercial purposes, and includes any such land under state, municipal, or private ownership; http://touchngo.com/lglcntr/akstats/Statutes/Title41/Chapter17/Section950.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_479 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-California) \"Forestland\" means the land: (1) can support 10 percent o..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-California ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-California) \"Forestland\" means the land: (1) can support 10 percent or more tree cover with trees native to California, including native oaks, (generally but not always this is Site V (Dunning) and better timberland); and (2) is zoned to allow forest resource management. http://ceres.ca.gov/foreststeward/pdf/CFIPguide.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_480 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-California) ‘‘Forest’’ means lands that support, or can support,’’ at..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-California ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-California) ‘‘Forest’’ means lands that support, or can support,’’ at least 10 percent tree canopy cover and that allow for management of one or more forest resources including timber, fish and wildlife, biodiversity, water quality, recreation, aesthetics and other public benefits. http://www.energy.ca.gov/global_climate_change/documents/SB_812_20020909_chapter.pdf and http://www.arb.ca.gov/bluebook/bb03/HS/42801.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_481 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-California-Mendocino County) “Forest Land” means lands, which are sui..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-California-Mendocino_County ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-California-Mendocino County) “Forest Land” means lands, which are suited for and are appropriately retained for the growing, harvesting and production of timber and forest and timber-related products. The classification includes lands eligible to be zoned Timberland Production (TPZ), including lands which have the present or future potential for timber production, intermixed smaller parcels and other contiguous lands, the inclusion of which is necessary for the protection and efficient management of forest resource lands. http://mendolafco.org/lafcopp/lafcopandp2002.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_482 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Colorado) \"Forest land\" means land of which at least ten percent is s..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Colorado ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Colorado) \"Forest land\" means land of which at least ten percent is stocked by forest trees of any size and includes land that formerly had such tree cover and that will be naturally or artificially regenerated. \"Forest land\" includes roadside, streamside, and shelterbelt strips of timber which have a crown width of at least one hundred twenty feet. \"Forest land\" includes unimproved roads and trails, streams, and clearings which are less than one hundred twenty feet wide. http://www.palmerfoundation.org/Legal_CO.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_483 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Florida) ``Forest\" means land stocked by trees of any size used in th..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Florida ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Florida) ``Forest\" means land stocked by trees of any size used in the production of forest products, or forest land that has been harvested and is not currently developed for nonforest use. http://www.myflorida.com/dor/tips/tip98a115.html and http://election.dos.state.fl.us/laws/98laws/ch_98-294.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_484 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Idaho) Forestland means privately owned land being held and used prim..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Idaho ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Idaho) Forestland means privately owned land being held and used primarily for the continuous purpose of growing and harvesting trees of a marketable species. http://www2.state.id.us/tax/propertytax/PTpdfs/revisedforestlanddesign.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_486 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Illinois) \"Forest\" means an area whose principal crop is trees. http:..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Illinois ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Illinois) \"Forest\" means an area whose principal crop is trees. http://www.legis.state.il.us/commission/jcar/admincode/017/017015370000010R.html and http://dnr.state.il.us/legal/1537.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_487 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Illinois) \"Forestry\" means land used or managed for the long-term pro..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Illinois ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Illinois) \"Forestry\" means land used or managed for the long-term production of wood, wood fiber, or wood-derived products. Allowable support facilities include water impoundments, access and fire control lanes, erosion control structures such as grassed waterways, downdrains, terraces and sediment ponds, and other incidental facilities related to sound multiple use management of the forest resource. http://dnr.state.il.us/legal/62-1701.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_489 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Kentucky) Forest land\" means land used or managed for the long-term p..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Kentucky ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Kentucky) Forest land\" means land used or managed for the long-term production of wood, wood fiber, or wood derived products. Land used for facilities in support of forest harvest and management operations which is adjacent to or an integral part of these operations is also included. http://www.lrc.state.ky.us/kar/405/030/010.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_490 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Kentucky) Forestland - land at least 10 percent stocked by forest tre..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Kentucky ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Kentucky) Forestland - land at least 10 percent stocked by forest trees of any size, including land that formerly had such cover and that will be naturally or artificially regenerated. The State of Kentucky does not have the terms Forest, Forestland, or Tree officially defined in State Statute or Regulation. The Division of Forestry utilizes the Society of American Forester's definitions for these terms as listed in John A. Helms' The Dictionary of Forestry. Steve.Kull@mail.state.ky.us"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_491 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Maine) \"Forest land\" means land used for the production of forest pro..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Maine ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Maine) \"Forest land\" means land used for the production of forest products. http://janus.state.me.us/legis/statutes/17/title17sec3853-D.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_492 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Maine) Forest land. \"Forest land\" means land used primarily for growt..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Maine ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Maine) Forest land. \"Forest land\" means land used primarily for growth of trees to be harvested for commercial use, but does not include ledge, marsh, open swamp, bog, water and similar areas, which are unsuitable for growing a forest product or for harvesting for commercial use even though these areas may exist within forest lands. Source: http://janus.state.me.us/legis/statutes/36/title36sec573.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_496 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Maryland-Easton) \"Forest\" means a biological community dominated by t..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_496_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Maryland-Easton ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Maryland-Easton) \"Forest\" means a biological community dominated by trees and other woody plants covering a land area of 10,000 square feet or greater. B. \"Forest\" includes: (1) Areas that have at least 100 live trees per acre with at least 50 percent of those trees having a 2-inch or greater diameter at 4.5 feet above the ground and larger; and (2) Areas that have been cut but not cleared. C. \"Forest\" does not include orchards. http://www.town-eastonmd.com/Planning/fco/fco_a002.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_496_criteria ex:minCanopyCover "50.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minCanopyCoverSI "50.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeight "4.5"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "1.3716000000000002"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_498 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Massachusetts) Forest Land means land with at least 15% of the area o..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Massachusetts ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Massachusetts) Forest Land means land with at least 15% of the area occupied by the crowns of forest trees of any size that contains at least 7.5 square feet of basal area per acre; or that is a plantation containing at least 500 trees per acre; or land recently harvested that is in the process of regeneration. http://www.state.ma.us/dem/regs/304011c.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_499 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Michigan) \"Forest land\" means a tract of land or the timber rights in..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_499_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Michigan ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Michigan) \"Forest land\" means a tract of land or the timber rights in that land owned or occupied by a member, which land is at least 10% occupied by forest tree species with a growth potential of 50 cubic feet per acre per year and consists of 40 acres or more. Forest land includes land from which forest tree species have been removed and have not been restocked, but does not include land converted to uses other than the growing of forest tree species or land currently zoned for uses incompatible with forest practices. http://www.dnr.state.mi.us/www/law/law_book/statutes/code/part501.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_499_criteria ex:minArea "40.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "16.18744"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_500 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Michigan) \"Forest land\" means timbered land, potential timber-produci..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Michigan ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Michigan) \"Forest land\" means timbered land, potential timber-producing land, cutover or burned timber land or grass lands not including lands devoted to agriculture. http://www.michigan.gov/dnr/0,1607,7-153-10367_11851-24039--,00.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_501 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Michigan) (d) \" Forest land\" means a tract of land that may include n..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Michigan ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Michigan) (d) \" Forest land\" means a tract of land that may include nonproductive land that is intermixed with productive land that is an integral part of a managed forest and that meets all the following: (i) Does not have material natural resources other than those resources suitable for forest growth or the potential for forest growth. (ii) Is not used for agricultural, mineral extraction except as provided in section 51113, grazing, industrial, developed recreational, residential, resort, commercial, or developmental purposes. (iii) The owner agrees to develop, maintain, and actively manage the land as a commercial forest through planting, natural reproduction, or other silvicultural practices. Source: http://www.michiganlegislature.org/law/getObject.asp?objName=324-51101&objType=section&highlight=forest"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_504 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Minnesota) Forest land or forest. Forest land or forest, means land o..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Minnesota ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Minnesota) Forest land or forest. Forest land or forest, means land on which occurs a stand or potential stand of trees valuable for timber products, watershed or wildlife protection, recreational uses or other purposes, and shall include lands owned or controlled by the state of Minnesota. http://www.revisor.leg.state.mn.us/stats/89/51.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_506 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Montana) \"Forest land\" means contiguous land of 15 acres or more in o..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_506_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Montana ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Montana) \"Forest land\" means contiguous land of 15 acres or more in one ownership that is capable of producing timber that can be harvested in commercial quantity and is producing timber unless the trees have been removed by man through harvest, including clearcuts, or by natural disaster, including but not limited to fire. Forest land includes land: a) that has not been converted to another use; and b) on which the annual net wood production equals or exceeds 25 cubic feet an acre at the culmination of mean annual increment. http://data.opi.state.mt.us/bills/mca/15/44/15-44-102.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_506_criteria ex:minArea "15.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "6.07029"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_507 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Nevada) “Forest” or “forest land” means land on which occurs a stand ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Nevada ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Nevada) “Forest” or “forest land” means land on which occurs a stand or potential stand of trees valuable for timber products, watershed or wildlife protection, recreational uses or for other purposes. http://www.leg.state.nv.us/NRS/NRS-527.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_508 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Nevada) Land which is at least 10 percent occupied by forest trees of..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Nevada ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Nevada) Land which is at least 10 percent occupied by forest trees of any size or formerly having had such tree cover and not currently developed for non-forest use. Lands developed for non-forest use include areas for crops, improved pasture, residential, or administrative areas, improved roads of any width, and adjoining road clearing and power line clearing of any width. http://www.state.nv.us/cnr/ndwp/dict-1/WORD_F.htm Water Words Dictionary, http://www.nalms.org/glossary/lkword_f.htm Lake and Water Words Glossary, http://www.dcnr.nv.gov/nrp/y-tr1nrp.pdf and (36 CFR 219.3) http://www.safc.org/resources/glossary.htm#definitions"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_509 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-New York) Forest land means land primarily devoted to and suitable fo..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-New_York ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-New York) Forest land means land primarily devoted to and suitable for forest crop production under accepted evenaged or unevenaged forest management systems through natural regeneration or through forestation and sufficiently stocked with forest trees to produce a merchantable forest crop within 30 years of time of original certification. Forest land shall consist of a stand or stands of commercial species of forest trees which contain at least either 500 stems per acre or 60 square feet of basal area per acre which shall be evenly distributed over the area of the stand. The department may approve a smaller number of planted trees per acre if the resulting spacing between trees is appropriate for satisfactory growth for the species being planted. For natural seedlings to be part of a stand, they must be at least one foot in height, and planted trees must be at least in their third growing season on the site. http://www.dec.state.ny.us/website/regs/199.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_510 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-North Carolina-Counties) Forestland means land that is a part of a fo..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_510_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-North_Carolina-Counties ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-North Carolina-Counties) Forestland means land that is a part of a forest unit that is actively engaged in the commercial growing of trees under a sound management program. Forestland includes wasteland that is a part of the forest unit, but the wasteland included in the unit shall be appraised under the use value schedules as wasteland. The requirements for a forestland deferment are as follows: May consist of more than one tract of forestland, but at least one of the tracts must meet the qualification requirements and each tract must be under a sound management program. One tract must consist of at least 20 acres that are in actual production and are not included in a farm unit. If individually owned, the property must be the owner's residence or have been owned by the current owner or a relative of the current owner for four years preceding January 1 of the year in which the benefit is claimed. http://www.lincolncounty.org/County/Departments/Tax/LandUseValueQualifications.htm and http://www.co.anson.nc.us/assessor/defermnt.htm, http://www.co.chatham.nc.us/dept/tax/web/Listing.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_510_criteria ex:minArea "20.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "8.09372"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_513 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Oklahoma) \"Forests\" means forest land that is at least ten percent (1..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Oklahoma ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Oklahoma) \"Forests\" means forest land that is at least ten percent (10%) stocked by forest trees of any size, whether of commercial or noncommercial species, or formerly having such tree cover and not currently developed for nonforest use, including woodlands, woodlots, windbreaks and shelterbelts; Source: &sect;2-1301-102. http://oklegal.onenet.net/oklegal-cgi/isearch"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_514 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Oregon) \"Forestland\" means land zoned in a county comprehensive plan ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Oregon ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Oregon) \"Forestland\" means land zoned in a county comprehensive plan for forest or farm use that is capable of producing commercial hardwood or softwood timber, regardless of the vegetation currently on the land. http://arcweb.sos.state.or.us/rules/OARS_600/OAR_629/629_022.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_515 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Oregon) “Forestland\" means forestland that is a parcel of land of mor..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_515_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Oregon ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Oregon) “Forestland\" means forestland that is a parcel of land of more than 10 acres that has been zoned in the comprehensive plan for exclusive farm use, forest use or farm and forest use and that is, as of the assessment date for which value for the forest homesite is being determined: (a) Land that has as its highest and best use the growing and harvesting of trees of a marketable species; (b) Land that has been designated as forestland under ORS 321.257 to 321.390 or 321.805 to 321.825; or (c) Land that has been classified under ORS 321.705 to 321.765. http://www.savinggraves-us.org/or/laws/308a.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_515_criteria ex:minArea "10.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "4.04686"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_516 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Oregon) Forestland” means land used for the growing and harvesting of..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Oregon ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Oregon) Forestland” means land used for the growing and harvesting of forest tree species, regardless of how the land is zoned, taxed or how any state statutes or local ordinances, rules or regulations are applied. http://159.121.125.11/forasst/Library/Pub/UrbanFP.pdf, http://www.cof.orst.edu/cof/teach/for442/odfdefin.htm and http://arcweb.sos.state.or.us/rules/OARS_600/OAR_629/629_600.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_517 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Rhode Island) -“Forestland” means any tract or contiguous tracts of l..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Rhode_Island ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Rhode Island) -“Forestland” means any tract or contiguous tracts of land, five (5) acres or more bearing a dense growth of trees, young regenerating forest, and having either the quality of selfperpetuation, or being dependent upon its development by the planting and replanting. http://www.state.ri.us/dem/pubs/regs/regs/forest/altgrant.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_518 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Rhode Island) I.2.c. Forestland - In this report, forestland is defin..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Rhode_Island ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Rhode Island) I.2.c. Forestland - In this report, forestland is defined in the same way as \"commercial forestland,\" and is based on the standard definition developed by the USDA Forest Service. According to the Forest Service, \"Commercial forestland is land that is capable of producing more than 20 cubic feet of biomass per acre per year.\" http://rredc.nrel.gov/biomass/doe/rbep/ri_wd_waste/one.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_519 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Rhode Island) The term \"forest land\" means any tract or contiguous tr..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Rhode_Island ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Rhode Island) The term \"forest land\" means any tract or contiguous tracts of land, ten (10) acres or larger bearing a dense growth of trees, including any underbrush thereon, and having either the quality of self perpetuation, or being dependent upon its development by the planting and replanting of trees in stands of closely growing timber, actively managed under a forest management plan approved by the director of environmental management. http://farm.fic.niu.edu/fic/laws/state/ri44271.html and http://www.state.ri.us/dem/pubs/regs/regs/agric/ffosimp.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_521 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Tennessee) \"Forest land\" means land constituting a forest unit engage..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Tennessee ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Tennessee) \"Forest land\" means land constituting a forest unit engaged in the growing of trees under a sound program of sustained yield management or any tract of fifteen (15) or more acres having tree growth in such quantity and quality and so managed as to constitute a forest; Source: http://farm.fic.niu.edu/fic/laws/state/tn675100.html and http://www.padctn.com/greenbelt_law.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_522 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Texas) \"Forest land\" means land on which the trees are potentially va..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Texas ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Texas) \"Forest land\" means land on which the trees are potentially valuable for timber products, protection of watersheds, wildlife habitat, recreational uses, or for other purposes, but does not include land within the incorporated limits of a village, town, or city. http://www.capitol.state.tx.us/statutes/nr/nr0015200.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_523 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Texas) Forest land” means land on which the trees are potentially val..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Texas ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Texas) Forest land” means land on which the trees are potentially valuable for timber products. http://www.tpwd.state.tx.us/texaswater/rivers/riddellcriminaltrespass.phtml"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_524 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Vermont) (9) \"Managed forest land\" means any land, exclusive of any h..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_524_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Vermont ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Vermont) (9) \"Managed forest land\" means any land, exclusive of any housesite, which is at least 25 acres in size and which is under active forest management for the purpose of growing and harvesting repeated forest crops in accordance with accepted forest management practices. There shall be a presumption that land is under active forest management if at least 50 percent of the land: (A) is certified to be a \"tree farm\" under the American Tree Farm System; (B) has qualified for a federal cost-sharing forest improvement program, and that program has actually been carried out within the past five years; (C) is certified by the county forester as conforming with accepted forest management practices; or (D) conforms with such criteria for managed forest land as are accepted by the board; Source: Vt. Stat. Ann. tit. 32, &sect;&sect; 3751 to 3775 http://farm.fic.niu.edu/fic/laws/state/vt323751.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_524_criteria ex:minArea "25.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "10.11715"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_525 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Vermont) Forest land means any land, exclusive of any housesite, whic..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Vermont ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Vermont) Forest land means any land, exclusive of any housesite, which is under active forest management for the purpose of growing and harvesting repeated forest crops. www.leg.state.vt.us/statutes/fullchapter.cfm?Title=24&Chapter=075."@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_529 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Washington) (3) \"Timber land\" means any parcel of land that is five o..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Washington ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Washington) (3) \"Timber land\" means any parcel of land that is five or more acres or multiple parcels of land that are contiguous and total five or more acres which is or are devoted primarily to the growth and harvest of forest crops for commercial purposes. Wash. Rev. Code secs. 84.34.010 to - .922 http://farm.fic.niu.edu/fic/laws/state/wa8434.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_530 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Washington-San Juan County) - Timber Land means any parcel of land th..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Washington-San_Juan_County ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Washington-San Juan County) - Timber Land means any parcel of land that is five or more acres or multiple parcels of land that are contiguous and total five or more acres which is or are devoted primarily to the growth and harvest of forest crops for commercial purposes. http://www.co.san-juan.wa.us/assessor/current.aspx"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_531 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Washington-San Juan County) Land designated as ‘forest land’ means an..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Washington-San_Juan_County ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Washington-San Juan County) Land designated as ‘forest land’ means any parcel of land twenty or more acres in size or multiple parcels of land that are contiguous and total twenty acres or more in size that is primarily used for the growth and harvesting of timber. Forest land refers only to the land. http://www.co.san-juan.wa.us/assessor/default.asp?page=dfl"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_532 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Washington-Stevens County) Forestland means all land in contiguous ow..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "International" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Washington-Stevens_County ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Washington-Stevens County) Forestland means all land in contiguous ownership of 20 or more acres; which is primarily devoted to and used for growing and harvesting timber. http://www.co.stevens.wa.us/assessor/Current%20Land%20Use/PDF%20docs/continuance.PDF"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_538 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-California) \"Forest land\" means timberland defined pursuant to subdiv..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-California ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-California) \"Forest land\" means timberland defined pursuant to subdivision (g), and other lands that have been withdrawn from timber production, such as units of the state park system, national parks, and wilderness areas. http://caselaw.lp.findlaw.com/cacodes/prc/4789-4789.7.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_540 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Minnesota) \"Forest land\" means land which is at least ten percent sto..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_540_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Minnesota ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Minnesota) \"Forest land\" means land which is at least ten percent stocked by trees of any size and capable of producing timber, or of exerting an influence on the climate or on the water regime; land from which the trees described above have been removed to less than ten percent stocking and which has not been developed for other use; and afforested areas. Source: Section: 88.01 continued... http://www.revisor.leg.state.mn.us:81/SEARCH/BASIS/mnstat/public/www/DDW?W%3DTEXT+PH+IS+%27forest+means%27+ORDER+BY+SORT_KEY/Ascend%26M%3D1%26K%3D88.01%26R%3DY%26U%3D20%26PCU%3D1"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_540_criteria ex:minHeight "26.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "26.0"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_541 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Montana) \"Forest land\" means land that has enough timber, standing or..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Montana ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Montana) \"Forest land\" means land that has enough timber, standing or down, slash, or brush to constitute in the judgment of the department a fire menace to life or property. Grassland and agricultural areas are included when those areas are intermingled with or contiguous to and no further than one-half mile from areas of forest land. http://www.dnrc.state.mt.us/forestry/classifi.htm and http://www.discoveringmontana.com/racicot/eo/21-22-23Background.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_542 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Nebraska) Nebraska accepts the definitions of forestland, forest, etc..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Nebraska ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Nebraska) Nebraska accepts the definitions of forestland, forest, etc. as defined in the U.S. Forest Service's Forest Inventory and Analysis program. ghergenr@unlnotes.unl.edu."@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_543 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-New Hampshire) \"Forestland'' means all lands in this state, except th..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-New_Hampshire ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-New Hampshire) \"Forestland'' means all lands in this state, except those owned and managed by the United States of America, which by reason of their location and character of soil have the capacity to grow trees and the continuance of which under forest cover is of substantial importance to the public interest. http://www.gencourt.state.nh.us/rsa/html/XIX-A/227-G/227-G-2.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_544 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-New Jersey) A \"forest\" means and includes any forest, brush land, gra..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-New_Jersey ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-New Jersey) A \"forest\" means and includes any forest, brush land, grass land, salt marsh, wooded area and any combination thereof, including but not limited to, an open space area, public lands, wetlands, park lands, natural habitats, a State conservation area, a wildlife refuge area or any other designated undeveloped open space whether or not it is subject to specific protection under law. http://www.judiciary.state.nj.us/criminal/charges/arson2.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_545 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-North Dakota) \"Forest\" means an area of land normally supporting a gr..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-North_Dakota ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-North Dakota) \"Forest\" means an area of land normally supporting a growth of planted tree cover, woodlands, or windbreaks. http://www.legis.nd.gov/cencode/t57c57.pdf"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_546 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Oregon) \"Forestland\" means any woodland, brushland, timberland, grazi..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Oregon ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Oregon) \"Forestland\" means any woodland, brushland, timberland, grazing land or clearing, which, during any time of the year, contains enough forest growth, slashing or vegetation to constitute, in the opinion of the forester, a fire hazard, regardless of how the land is zoned or taxed. Source: 526.005 Definitions http://www.leg.state.or.us/ors/526.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_547 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Pennsylvania) Forests are defined as ecosystems dominated by trees, b..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Pennsylvania ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Pennsylvania) Forests are defined as ecosystems dominated by trees, but with other components such as shrubs, herbs, mammals, birds, insects, microscopic creatures, soil, air, water, and the interactive processes that bind them together. http://www.dcnr.state.pa.us/forestry/sfrmp/overview.htm#sustainability"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_561 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Kentucky) A woody perennial plant, typically large and with a well-de..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Cover" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_561_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Kentucky ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Kentucky) A woody perennial plant, typically large and with a well-defined stem or stems carrying a more or less definite crown (usually more that 12 feet in height at maturity). The State of Kentucky does not have the terms Forest, Forestland, or Tree officially defined in State Statute or Regulation. The Division of Forestry utilizes the Society of American Forester's definitions for these terms as listed in John A. Helms' The Dictionary of Forestry. Steve.Kull@mail.state.ky.us"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_561_criteria ex:minHeight "12.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minHeightSI "3.6576000000000004"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_564 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Virginia) - \"Forest trees\" means only those trees which are a part of..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Virginia ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Virginia) - \"Forest trees\" means only those trees which are a part of and constitute a stand of potential, immature, or mature commercial timber trees. The term \"forest trees\" includes shade trees of any species around houses, along highways and within cities and towns if the trees constitute an insect or disease menace to nearby timber trees or timber stands. Under Authority of Department of Forestry. § 10.1-1178. Definitions. \"Starr, James\" starrj@dof.state.va.us"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_579 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-FED-DI-GS) -Woodland, which is defined as \"forest land,\" includes deciduous..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_579_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-FED-DI-GS ;
    skos:note "(USA-FED-DI-GS) -Woodland, which is defined as \"forest land,\" includes deciduous, evergreen, and mixed forest land, and orchards. The woodland data layer identifies deforestation or reforestation resulting from urbanization or conservation. The woodland is compiled using criteria based on tint and spectral reflectance. The minimum mapping unit for woodland is 10 acres. The classification scheme adopted for woodland is a modification of the Anderson Level II classification system. All woodland areas are collected as polygons, compiled into one separate coverage, and assigned category 44. http://mcmcweb.er.usgs.gov/phil/gis.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_579_criteria ex:minArea "10.0"^^xsd:float ;
    ex:minAreaSI "4.04686"^^xsd:float .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_595 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "Stocking - The number of trees in a forest stand. Often, stocking level is compa..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "Stocking - The number of trees in a forest stand. Often, stocking level is compared to the desirable number of trees for best growth and management, such as partially stocked, well stocked or over-stocked. http://216.239.39.100/search?q=cache:3wFtRKEEkxEC:www.gfc.state.ga.us/Publications/Educational/glossary.pdf+%22stand+density%22++definition+glossary&hl=en&ie=UTF-8#10"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_608 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA – STATE -Maryland) The establishment of a forest, according to the definiti..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_Unknown ;
    skos:note "(USA – STATE -Maryland) The establishment of a forest, according to the definitions and procedures contained herein, on an area which is not presently in forest cover. http://pilot.wash.lib.md.us/washco/forestcn.html"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_653 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-FED-DA-FS) The restocking of an area with forest trees, by either natural o..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-FED-DA-FS ;
    skos:note "(USA-FED-DA-FS) The restocking of an area with forest trees, by either natural or artificial means, such as planting (http://www.fs.fed.us/land/emterms.html)."@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_654 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Oregon) \"Natural reforestation\" means restocking a site with self-gro..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Oregon ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Oregon) \"Natural reforestation\" means restocking a site with self-grown trees resulting from self-seeding or vegetative means. http://www.cof.orst.edu/cof/teach/for442/odfdefin.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_658 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-STATE-Illinois) \"Reforestation\" means the natural or artificial restocking ..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Administrative" ;
    ex:geographicScope "Local/State" ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-STATE-Illinois ;
    skos:note "(USA-STATE-Illinois) \"Reforestation\" means the natural or artificial restocking with trees on forest land. http://dnr.state.il.us/legal/1537.htm"@en .

ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_694 a ex:Definition ;
    rdfs:label "(USA-FED-DI-GS) -Woodland, which is defined as \"forest land,\" includes deciduous..." ;
    ex:appliesTo ex:Country_USA ;
    ex:country "USA" ;
    ex:definitionType "Land Use" ;
    ex:geographicScope "National" ;
    ex:hasCriteria ex:Def_def_usa_unknown_694_criteria ;
    ex:hasSource ex:Source_USA-FED-DI-GS ;
    skos:note "(USA-FED-DI-GS) -Woodland, which is defined as \"forest land,\" includes deciduous, evergreen, and mixed forest land, and orchards. The woodland data layer identifies deforestation or reforestation resulting from urbanization or conservation. The woodland is compiled using criteria based on tint and spectral reflectance. The minimum mapping unit for woodland is 10 acres. The classification scheme adopted for woodland is a modification of the Anderson Level II classification system. All woodland areas are collected as polygons, compiled into one separate coverage, and assigned category 44. http://mcmcweb.er.usgs.gov/phil/gis.html"@en .

