    skos:note "(Zimbabwe) Natural forest - This class which consists of moist evergreen or deciduous species can be defined as vegetation which shows a canopy cover greater than 80% and tree heights greater than 15 metres. This class usually occurs in high rainfall areas and as riverine vegetation along big rivers. Dominick Kwesha \"VegRIS\" vegris@harare.iafrica.com"@en .

